# Individual: X2012_m_donepezil_SSRI_SNRI_interaction_Serotoni_syndrome_2nd:Serotonin_syndrome (Serotonin syndrome pathophysiology)

AnnotationAssertion(rdfs:label X2012_m_donepezil_SSRI_SNRI_interaction_Serotoni_syndrome_2nd:Serotonin_syndrome "Serotonin syndrome pathophysiology"^^xsd:string)
ClassAssertion(OpenPVSignal:Free_text_reporting_element X2012_m_donepezil_SSRI_SNRI_interaction_Serotoni_syndrome_2nd:Serotonin_syndrome)
ObjectPropertyAssertion(OpenPVSignal:refers_to_adverse_effect X2012_m_donepezil_SSRI_SNRI_interaction_Serotoni_syndrome_2nd:Serotonin_syndrome X2012_m_donepezil_SSRI_SNRI_interaction_Serotoni_syndrome_2nd:serotoninSyndrome)
ObjectPropertyAssertion(mp:references X2012_m_donepezil_SSRI_SNRI_interaction_Serotoni_syndrome_2nd:Serotonin_syndrome X2012_m_donepezil_SSRI_SNRI_interaction_Serotoni_syndrome_2nd:Ref.5)
ObjectPropertyAssertion(mp:references X2012_m_donepezil_SSRI_SNRI_interaction_Serotoni_syndrome_2nd:Serotonin_syndrome X2012_m_donepezil_SSRI_SNRI_interaction_Serotoni_syndrome_2nd:Ref.6)
DataPropertyAssertion(OpenPVSignal:has_content X2012_m_donepezil_SSRI_SNRI_interaction_Serotoni_syndrome_2nd:Serotonin_syndrome "Serotonin syndrome is a potentially life-threatening reaction that may occur in patients  using drugs that elevate the serotonin levels. The  most common drugs causing this reaction are  monoamine oxidase inhibitors (MAO-inhibitors),  tri-cyclic antidepressants (TCAs) and selective  serotonin reuptake inhibitors (SSRIs), SNRIs and  SARIs.5 The excess serotonin activity in receptors  in the central nervous system and peripheral  serotonin receptors results in myoclonus,  hyperreflexia, diaphoresis, mental changes,  autonomic symptoms, shivering, tremor and in  severe cases neuromuscular rigidity, delirium and  life-threatening hyperthermia. Complications are  common and include dehydration, infection,  respiratory and renal failure and disseminated  intravascular coagulation. 5,6 The primary  treatment consists of discontinuation of suspected drugs and sometimes administration of serotonin receptor antagonists. The symptoms of the syndrome usually resolve within 24 hours if 
discontinuing the causative drugs, but confusion may last for days and complications may result in death.6"^^xsd:string)

# Individual: X2012_m_donepezil_SSRI_SNRI_interaction_Serotoni_syndrome_2nd:Studies_in_rats_and_mice (Studies in rats and mice)

AnnotationAssertion(rdfs:label X2012_m_donepezil_SSRI_SNRI_interaction_Serotoni_syndrome_2nd:Studies_in_rats_and_mice "Studies in rats and mice"^^xsd:string)
ClassAssertion(obo:OAE_0001197 X2012_m_donepezil_SSRI_SNRI_interaction_Serotoni_syndrome_2nd:Studies_in_rats_and_mice)
ObjectPropertyAssertion(OpenPVSignal:refers_to_drug X2012_m_donepezil_SSRI_SNRI_interaction_Serotoni_syndrome_2nd:Studies_in_rats_and_mice X2012_m_donepezil_SSRI_SNRI_interaction_Serotoni_syndrome_2nd:donepezil)
ObjectPropertyAssertion(mp:references X2012_m_donepezil_SSRI_SNRI_interaction_Serotoni_syndrome_2nd:Studies_in_rats_and_mice X2012_m_donepezil_SSRI_SNRI_interaction_Serotoni_syndrome_2nd:Ref.3)
ObjectPropertyAssertion(mp:references X2012_m_donepezil_SSRI_SNRI_interaction_Serotoni_syndrome_2nd:Studies_in_rats_and_mice X2012_m_donepezil_SSRI_SNRI_interaction_Serotoni_syndrome_2nd:Ref.4)
DataPropertyAssertion(OpenPVSignal:has_content X2012_m_donepezil_SSRI_SNRI_interaction_Serotoni_syndrome_2nd:Studies_in_rats_and_mice "An in vitro study on rats showed changes in serotonin levels by acute doses of donepezil3 and another study on mice showed that twice daily treatment of donepezil for two weeks significantly increased striatal 5HT2A mRNA levels.4"^^xsd:string)
DataPropertyAssertion(OpenPVSignal:has_content X2012_m_donepezil_SSRI_SNRI_interaction_Serotoni_syndrome_2nd:Studies_in_rats_and_mice "Studies in rats and mice show effects on serotonin or serotonin receptors in brain but the effect in humans remains unclear.3,4"^^xsd:string)

# Individual: X2012_m_donepezil_SSRI_SNRI_interaction_Serotoni_syndrome_2nd:SummaryContent (Summary content)

AnnotationAssertion(rdfs:label X2012_m_donepezil_SSRI_SNRI_interaction_Serotoni_syndrome_2nd:SummaryContent "Summary content"^^xsd:string)
ClassAssertion(OpenPVSignal:Summary X2012_m_donepezil_SSRI_SNRI_interaction_Serotoni_syndrome_2nd:SummaryContent)
DataPropertyAssertion(OpenPVSignal:has_content X2012_m_donepezil_SSRI_SNRI_interaction_Serotoni_syndrome_2nd:SummaryContent "Donepezil is a specific and reversible inhibitor of acetylcholinesterase used to treat Alzheimer’s disease. A number of combinations of donepezil and the adverse reaction serotonin syndrome appeared in VigiBase. This is not listed for donepezil. The reports showed that different antidepressants like serotonin reuptake inhibitors SSRIs, selective serotonin-norepinephrine reuptake inhibitors (SNRIs) and a serotonin antagonist and reuptake inhibitor (SARI) were co- reported with donepezil suspected to cause this effect. An extended search was made to investigate a possible interacting effect between donepezil and antidepressants. After removing suspected duplicates 13 reports from six countries remained. In four cases donepezil was added to pre-existing SSRI/SNRI/SARI treatment and in five cases SSRI/SNRI/ SARI was added to pre-existing donepezil treatment. In three of the four cases where donepezil was added to pre-existing treatment the reporters suspected an interaction between donepezil and the other drug/drugs.
Studies in the brain of mice and rats have shown that donepezil seem to affect serotonin levels and serotonin receptors, however there is limited information in literature about donepezil’s serotonergic effects in human brain. These spontaneous reports from several countries indicate that donepezil might have an effect on serotonin levels in human brain and that there might be an interacting effect of this drug and SSRIs/SNRIs/SARIs."^^xsd:string)

# Individual: X2012_m_donepezil_SSRI_SNRI_interaction_Serotoni_syndrome_2nd:TimeToOnsetForSerotonineSyndromeInTheLiterature (Time to onset for serotonine syndrome in the literature)

AnnotationAssertion(rdfs:label X2012_m_donepezil_SSRI_SNRI_interaction_Serotoni_syndrome_2nd:TimeToOnsetForSerotonineSyndromeInTheLiterature "Time to onset for serotonine syndrome in the literature"^^xsd:string)
ClassAssertion(obo:OAE_0001197 X2012_m_donepezil_SSRI_SNRI_interaction_Serotoni_syndrome_2nd:TimeToOnsetForSerotonineSyndromeInTheLiterature)
ObjectPropertyAssertion(mp:references X2012_m_donepezil_SSRI_SNRI_interaction_Serotoni_syndrome_2nd:TimeToOnsetForSerotonineSyndromeInTheLiterature X2012_m_donepezil_SSRI_SNRI_interaction_Serotoni_syndrome_2nd:Ref.9)
DataPropertyAssertion(OpenPVSignal:has_content X2012_m_donepezil_SSRI_SNRI_interaction_Serotoni_syndrome_2nd:TimeToOnsetForSerotonineSyndromeInTheLiterature "The time to onset of the reaction seem to be plausible when comparing to a post- marketing surveillance study aiming to identify serotonin syndrome cases in United Kingdom in the late nineties. Out of 19 patients identified with serotonin syndrome the time to onset was less than 14 days for all.9"^^xsd:string)

