ObjectPropertyAssertion(mp:references X2012_m_everolimus_and_serious_gastrointestinal_disorders_3rd:casesOfGIBleedingAndEverolimus X2012_m_everolimus_and_serious_gastrointestinal_disorders_3rd:Ref.15)
DataPropertyAssertion(OpenPVSignal:has_content X2012_m_everolimus_and_serious_gastrointestinal_disorders_3rd:casesOfGIBleedingAndEverolimus "Two case reports of GI bleeding (grade 5 and 2 respectively) regarding patients with hepatocellular carcinoma recurrence after liver transplantation, treated with sorafenib and everolimus have recently been published.13,14 The authors did not exclude a possible additive effect of everolimus on the already known increase in risk of GI and non GI bleeding for sorafenib and other vascular endothelial growth factor receptor (VEGFR) tyrosine-kinase inhibitors.15"^^xsd:string)

