# Individual: X2012_m_ondasetrone_3rd:infoForCaseWthGranisetron1 (info for case wth granisetron 1)

AnnotationAssertion(rdfs:label X2012_m_ondasetrone_3rd:infoForCaseWthGranisetron1 "info for case wth granisetron 1"^^xsd:string)
ClassAssertion(OpenPVSignal:Case_Report_Information X2012_m_ondasetrone_3rd:infoForCaseWthGranisetron1)
DataPropertyAssertion(OpenPVSignal:has_content X2012_m_ondasetrone_3rd:infoForCaseWthGranisetron1 "One case was found published in literature and reports an 11 year-old female with acute lymphoblastic leukemia. The patient developed symptoms of serotonin syndrome when a worsening medical condition led to compromised endothelial function, coinciding with the use of granisetron and fentanyl.7"^^xsd:string)

# Individual: X2012_m_ondasetrone_3rd:infoForCaseWthGranisetron2 (info for case wth granisetron 2)

AnnotationAssertion(rdfs:label X2012_m_ondasetrone_3rd:infoForCaseWthGranisetron2 "info for case wth granisetron 2"^^xsd:string)
ClassAssertion(OpenPVSignal:Case_Report_Information X2012_m_ondasetrone_3rd:infoForCaseWthGranisetron2)
DataPropertyAssertion(OpenPVSignal:has_content X2012_m_ondasetrone_3rd:infoForCaseWthGranisetron2 "The second case reports a 69 year-old female. Suspected drugs include granisetron, venlafaxine, sufentanil and methylthioninium and the reporter mentions the suspicion of interaction between venlafaxine and methylthioninium, with contributions from the other drugs. Venlafaxine had been used for almost one year when adding the other three drugs and serotonin syndrome started with a latency of hours after start of the new drugs."^^xsd:string)

# Individual: X2012_m_ondasetrone_3rd:infoForCaseWthGranisetron3 (info for case wth granisetron 3)

AnnotationAssertion(rdfs:label X2012_m_ondasetrone_3rd:infoForCaseWthGranisetron3 "info for case wth granisetron 3"^^xsd:string)
ClassAssertion(OpenPVSignal:Case_Report_Information X2012_m_ondasetrone_3rd:infoForCaseWthGranisetron3)
DataPropertyAssertion(OpenPVSignal:has_content X2012_m_ondasetrone_3rd:infoForCaseWthGranisetron3 "The third case reports a 12 year-old male with acute lymphatic leukaemia. Granisetron and olanzapine were reported as suspected drugs, but many concomitant drugs were also mentioned, including fentanyl and other anaesthetics. Neuroleptic malignant syndrome was reported as an additional ADR."^^xsd:string)

# Individual: X2012_m_ondasetrone_3rd:infoForPublishedVigibaseCase1 (info for published vigibase case 1)

AnnotationAssertion(rdfs:label X2012_m_ondasetrone_3rd:infoForPublishedVigibaseCase1 "info for published vigibase case 1"^^xsd:string)
ClassAssertion(OpenPVSignal:Case_Report_Information X2012_m_ondasetrone_3rd:infoForPublishedVigibaseCase1)
ObjectPropertyAssertion(mp:references X2012_m_ondasetrone_3rd:infoForPublishedVigibaseCase1 X2012_m_ondasetrone_3rd:Ref.8)
ObjectPropertyAssertion(mp:references X2012_m_ondasetrone_3rd:infoForPublishedVigibaseCase1 X2012_m_ondasetrone_3rd:Ref.9)
DataPropertyAssertion(OpenPVSignal:has_content X2012_m_ondasetrone_3rd:infoForPublishedVigibaseCase1 "Serotonin toxicity suggested being due to interaction between methylthioninium and paroxetine. The authors did not exclude that interaction between ondansetron and residual paroxetine could increase the vulnerability to serotonin toxicity (paroxetine withdrawn two days before reaction onset).8,9"^^xsd:string)

# Individual: X2012_m_ondasetrone_3rd:infoForPublishedVigibaseCase2 (info for published vigibase case 2)

AnnotationAssertion(rdfs:label X2012_m_ondasetrone_3rd:infoForPublishedVigibaseCase2 "info for published vigibase case 2"^^xsd:string)
ClassAssertion(OpenPVSignal:Case_Report_Information X2012_m_ondasetrone_3rd:infoForPublishedVigibaseCase2)
ObjectPropertyAssertion(mp:references X2012_m_ondasetrone_3rd:infoForPublishedVigibaseCase2 X2012_m_ondasetrone_3rd:Ref.10)
DataPropertyAssertion(OpenPVSignal:has_content X2012_m_ondasetrone_3rd:infoForPublishedVigibaseCase2 "Medical history included major
depression, polysubstance abuse and overdose.
Paracetamol/Hydrocodorate first administered second day after
reaction onset.10"^^xsd:string)

# Individual: X2012_m_ondasetrone_3rd:infoForPublishedVigibaseCase3 (info for published vigibase case 3)

AnnotationAssertion(rdfs:label X2012_m_ondasetrone_3rd:infoForPublishedVigibaseCase3 "info for published vigibase case 3"^^xsd:string)
ClassAssertion(OpenPVSignal:Case_Report_Information X2012_m_ondasetrone_3rd:infoForPublishedVigibaseCase3)
ObjectPropertyAssertion(mp:references X2012_m_ondasetrone_3rd:infoForPublishedVigibaseCase3 X2012_m_ondasetrone_3rd:Ref.11)
DataPropertyAssertion(OpenPVSignal:has_content X2012_m_ondasetrone_3rd:infoForPublishedVigibaseCase3 "Medical history included malignant hyperthermia (MH). Authors suggested that a putative episode of MH, not serotonin syndrome, was triggered by ondansetron.11"^^xsd:string)

# Individual: X2012_m_ondasetrone_3rd:infoForPublishedVigibaseCase4 (info for published vigibase case 4)

AnnotationAssertion(rdfs:label X2012_m_ondasetrone_3rd:infoForPublishedVigibaseCase4 "info for published vigibase case 4"^^xsd:string)
ClassAssertion(OpenPVSignal:Case_Report_Information X2012_m_ondasetrone_3rd:infoForPublishedVigibaseCase4)
ObjectPropertyAssertion(mp:references X2012_m_ondasetrone_3rd:infoForPublishedVigibaseCase4 X2012_m_ondasetrone_3rd:Ref.12)
DataPropertyAssertion(OpenPVSignal:has_content X2012_m_ondasetrone_3rd:infoForPublishedVigibaseCase4 "Accidental intake by healthy infant, overdose.12"^^xsd:string)

# Individual: X2012_m_ondasetrone_3rd:infoForVigibaseCase3 (info for vigibase case  3 )

AnnotationAssertion(rdfs:label X2012_m_ondasetrone_3rd:infoForVigibaseCase3 "info for vigibase case  3 "^^xsd:string)
ClassAssertion(OpenPVSignal:Case_Report_Information X2012_m_ondasetrone_3rd:infoForVigibaseCase3)
DataPropertyAssertion(OpenPVSignal:has_content X2012_m_ondasetrone_3rd:infoForVigibaseCase3 "Serotonin reaction possibly attributed to venlafaxine and ondansetron mentioned by reporter, but subsequently the patient's physician reported that the events probably were related to another medication (unspecified)."^^xsd:string)

# Individual: X2012_m_ondasetrone_3rd:info_for_published_vigibase_case_5 (info for published vigibase case 5)

AnnotationAssertion(rdfs:label X2012_m_ondasetrone_3rd:info_for_published_vigibase_case_5 "info for published vigibase case 5"^^xsd:string)
ClassAssertion(OpenPVSignal:Case_Report_Information X2012_m_ondasetrone_3rd:info_for_published_vigibase_case_5)
DataPropertyAssertion(OpenPVSignal:has_content X2012_m_ondasetrone_3rd:info_for_published_vigibase_case_5 "The fifth case involves a 12 year old male patient seriously ill with disseminated Ewing's Sarcoma, receiving mirtazapine and morphine in addition to chemotherapy. The following day after starting ondansetron he was confused and tremulous with myoclonus. Ondansetron and mirtazapine were both discontinued, and the reaction resolved with a single dose of droperidol the following day. Mirtazapine was reintroduced several days later without problem.7"^^xsd:string)

