AnnotationAssertion(rdfs:label X2012_m_mometasone_and_arrhythmia_4rth:arrhythmia "arrhythmia pathobiology"^^xsd:string)
ClassAssertion(OpenPVSignal:Free_text_reporting_element X2012_m_mometasone_and_arrhythmia_4rth:arrhythmia)
ObjectPropertyAssertion(OpenPVSignal:is_part_of X2012_m_mometasone_and_arrhythmia_4rth:arrhythmia X2012_m_mometasone_and_arrhythmia_4rth:IntroductionContent)
ObjectPropertyAssertion(OpenPVSignal:refers_to_adverse_effect X2012_m_mometasone_and_arrhythmia_4rth:arrhythmia X2012_m_mometasone_and_arrhythmia_4rth:arrhythmiaIncident)
ObjectPropertyAssertion(mp:references X2012_m_mometasone_and_arrhythmia_4rth:arrhythmia X2012_m_mometasone_and_arrhythmia_4rth:Ref.4)
ObjectPropertyAssertion(mp:references X2012_m_mometasone_and_arrhythmia_4rth:arrhythmia X2012_m_mometasone_and_arrhythmia_4rth:Ref.5)
DataPropertyAssertion(OpenPVSignal:has_content X2012_m_mometasone_and_arrhythmia_4rth:arrhythmia "Arrhythmia refers to disturbances in normal cardiac rhythm. It includes a large and heterogeneous group of conditions which arise from abnormal electrical activity in the heart. Arrhythmias can range from minor, common \"skipped beats\" to life-threatening conditions general, arrhythmia can refer to disturbances in rate or rhythm but simple disturbances in rate such as bradychardia or tachycardia would usually be coded as such. Arrhythmias may be caused by many different factors including coronary artery disease, electrolyte imbalance, heart muscle disorders and as indicated above, may occur in \"normal, healthy\" hearts.4"^^xsd:string)

