DataPropertyAssertion(OpenPVSignal:has_content X2012_m_mometasone_and_arrhythmia_4rth:usage_of_mometasone "The topical form is presented as a cream or lotion and is indicated for the short term relief of inflammatory and pruritic manifestations of corticosteroid responsive dermatoses, such as psoriasis and atopic dermatitis. Common adverse effects (AEs) of the topical preparations include skin reactions such as pruritus, burning, tingling, signs of skin atrophy and acneiform reactions.1
