# Individual: X2013_m_abiraterone_6th_2013:drug-induced_immune_thrombocytopenia (drug-induced immune thrombocytopenia)

AnnotationAssertion(rdfs:label X2013_m_abiraterone_6th_2013:drug-induced_immune_thrombocytopenia "drug-induced immune thrombocytopenia"^^xsd:string)
ClassAssertion(OpenPVSignal:Adverse_Effect_Mechanism X2013_m_abiraterone_6th_2013:drug-induced_immune_thrombocytopenia)
ObjectPropertyAssertion(OpenPVSignal:refers_to_adverse_effect X2013_m_abiraterone_6th_2013:drug-induced_immune_thrombocytopenia X2013_m_abiraterone_6th_2013:immune_thrombocytopenia)
DataPropertyAssertion(OpenPVSignal:has_content X2013_m_abiraterone_6th_2013:drug-induced_immune_thrombocytopenia "Drug-induced immune thrombocytopenia is characterized by drug-dependent antibodies that bind to platelets and cause their destruction, and can be triggered by a wide range of medications, including cytotoxic agents. In immunemediated thrombocytopenia, time to onset is reported. to be on the order of 1 to 2 weeks following the patient's first exposure to an immunogenic drug, and of 2-3 days if the drug has been taken previously."^^xsd:string)

