DataPropertyAssertion(OpenPVSignal:has_content X2013_m_ptu_2nd_2013:MechanismOfPropylthiouracil "Propylthiouracil (PTU) is a thiouracil-derived drug used to treat hyperthyroidism, including Graves' disease. It is also used to alleviate symptoms of hyperthyroidism in preparation for thyroidectomy or radioactive iodine therapy in patients who are intolerant of methimazole (carbimazole) and in the treatment of thyroid storm. PTU acts by inhibiting the formation of thyroid hormones. It does not interfere with the existing triiodothyronine within the thyroid or circulating in the blood, nor does it affect thyroid hormone activity."^^xsd:string)

