DataPropertyAssertion(OpenPVSignal:has_content X2013_m_ptu_2nd_2013:epidermal_necrolysis_pathophysiology "Epidermal necrolysis (EN) like SJS, is a severe epidermolytic disorder usually caused by drugs, although other causes such as infection can occur. EN and SJS are considered by many to be the same disease, differing only by their extent of skin detachment, where in the case of EN a larger proportion of the body surface area is affected. SJS and EN can be life-threatening. The average reported mortality rate of SJS is 1-5%, and of EN is 25-35%. Elderly patients and those with a large surface area of epidermal detachment are at a higher risk.8,9"^^xsd:string)

