# Individual: X2013_m_ptu_2nd_2013:stevenJohnson (steven johnson pathophysiology)

AnnotationAssertion(rdfs:label X2013_m_ptu_2nd_2013:stevenJohnson "steven johnson pathophysiology"^^xsd:string)
ClassAssertion(OpenPVSignal:Free_text_reporting_element X2013_m_ptu_2nd_2013:stevenJohnson)
ObjectPropertyAssertion(OpenPVSignal:refers_to_adverse_effect X2013_m_ptu_2nd_2013:stevenJohnson X2013_m_ptu_2nd_2013:stevens-johnsonSyndrome)
ObjectPropertyAssertion(mp:references X2013_m_ptu_2nd_2013:stevenJohnson X2013_m_ptu_2nd_2013:Ref.5)
ObjectPropertyAssertion(mp:references X2013_m_ptu_2nd_2013:stevenJohnson X2013_m_ptu_2nd_2013:Ref.6)
DataPropertyAssertion(OpenPVSignal:has_content X2013_m_ptu_2nd_2013:stevenJohnson "Stevens-Johnson syndrome (SJS) is an immune- complex-mediated hypersensitivity reaction that involves the skin and mucous membranes. It is characterized by mucous ulceration, conjunctivitis and epidermal necrosis. SJS is a rare, serious and potentially fatal disorder that is often, but not always, due to drugs. Drugs commonly implicated in SJS include antibiotics, non-steroidal anti- inflammatory drugs, allopurinol and anti- convulsants.5,6"^^xsd:string)

