# Individual: X2013_m_febuxostat_and_hepatic_failure_2nd_2013:Introduction_content (Introduction content)

AnnotationAssertion(rdfs:label X2013_m_febuxostat_and_hepatic_failure_2nd_2013:Introduction_content "Introduction content"^^xsd:string)
ClassAssertion(OpenPVSignal:Introduction X2013_m_febuxostat_and_hepatic_failure_2nd_2013:Introduction_content)
DataPropertyAssertion(OpenPVSignal:has_content X2013_m_febuxostat_and_hepatic_failure_2nd_2013:Introduction_content "Febuxostat is a xanthine oxidase inhibitor (the same mechanism of action as allopurinol) indicated for the chronic management of hyperuricaemia in patients with gout. It was approved in Europe in 2008 and in the US in 2009"^^xsd:string)

# Individual: X2013_m_febuxostat_and_hepatic_failure_2nd_2013:Literature_and_Labelling (Literature and Labelling)

AnnotationAssertion(rdfs:label X2013_m_febuxostat_and_hepatic_failure_2nd_2013:Literature_and_Labelling "Literature and Labelling"^^xsd:string)
ClassAssertion(OpenPVSignal:Literature_information X2013_m_febuxostat_and_hepatic_failure_2nd_2013:Literature_and_Labelling)
ObjectPropertyAssertion(mp:references X2013_m_febuxostat_and_hepatic_failure_2nd_2013:Literature_and_Labelling X2013_m_febuxostat_and_hepatic_failure_2nd_2013:Ref.2)
ObjectPropertyAssertion(mp:references X2013_m_febuxostat_and_hepatic_failure_2nd_2013:Literature_and_Labelling X2013_m_febuxostat_and_hepatic_failure_2nd_2013:Ref.3)
DataPropertyAssertion(OpenPVSignal:has_content X2013_m_febuxostat_and_hepatic_failure_2nd_2013:Literature_and_Labelling "Hepatic failure was added to the Warnings and Precautions section of the US Product Information (PI) for febuxostat in November 2012, but has not yet been added to the UK Summary of Product Characteristics (SPC).2,3 The US PI states that liver function should be tested at baseline and on development of symptoms that may indicate liver injury, and that febuxostat should be ceased if ALT is ≥ three times ULN. However, the reports in VigiBase indicate that hepatic failure, sometimes fatal, may occur with rapid onset after starting febuxostat. The lack of reversibility of hepatic enzyme increases seen in clinical trials is also of concern.
In clinical trials of febuxostat, the incidence of alanine transaminase (ALT) ≥ three times the upper limit of normal (ULN) was 2-5% in the febuxostat groups (but not dose-related), 2% in the allopurinol group, and <1% in the placebo group.1 Reversibility of ALT and aspartate transaminase (AST) values to normal or below baseline was seen in 19/57 patients in the febuxostat groups, 10/17 for allopurinol, and 2/2 for placebo."^^xsd:string)

# Individual: X2013_m_febuxostat_and_hepatic_failure_2nd_2013:MechanismOfFebuxostat (Mechanism of febuxostat)

AnnotationAssertion(rdfs:label X2013_m_febuxostat_and_hepatic_failure_2nd_2013:MechanismOfFebuxostat "Mechanism of febuxostat"^^xsd:string)
ClassAssertion(OpenPVSignal:Mechanism X2013_m_febuxostat_and_hepatic_failure_2nd_2013:MechanismOfFebuxostat)
DataPropertyAssertion(OpenPVSignal:has_content X2013_m_febuxostat_and_hepatic_failure_2nd_2013:MechanismOfFebuxostat "Febuxostat is a xanthine oxidase inhibitor (the same mechanism of action as allopurinol) indicated for the chronic management of hyperuricaemia in patients with gout."^^xsd:string)

