DataPropertyAssertion(OpenPVSignal:has_content X2013_m_febuxostat_and_hepatic_failure_2nd_2013:clinicalTrialData "In clinical trials of febuxostat, the incidence of alanine transaminase (ALT) ≥ three times the upper limit of normal (ULN) was 2-5% in the febuxostat groups (but not dose-related), 2% in the allopurinol group, and <1% in the placebo group.1 Reversibility of ALT and aspartate transaminase (AST) values to normal or below baseline was seen in 19/57 patients in the febuxostat groups, 10/17 for allopurinol, and 2/2 for placebo"^^xsd:string)

