# Individual: X2013_m_fluoxetine_and_deafness_2013_3rd:IntroductionContent (Introduction content)

AnnotationAssertion(rdfs:label X2013_m_fluoxetine_and_deafness_2013_3rd:IntroductionContent "Introduction content"^^xsd:string)
ClassAssertion(OpenPVSignal:Introduction X2013_m_fluoxetine_and_deafness_2013_3rd:IntroductionContent)
ObjectPropertyAssertion(mp:references X2013_m_fluoxetine_and_deafness_2013_3rd:IntroductionContent X2013_m_fluoxetine_and_deafness_2013_3rd:Ref.2)
ObjectPropertyAssertion(mp:references X2013_m_fluoxetine_and_deafness_2013_3rd:IntroductionContent X2013_m_fluoxetine_and_deafness_2013_3rd:Ref.3)
DataPropertyAssertion(OpenPVSignal:has_content X2013_m_fluoxetine_and_deafness_2013_3rd:IntroductionContent "The drug-ADR combination of fluoxetine and deafness was highlighted during testing of a new quantitative method for detecting potential signals at the UMC in 2012.2 Fluoxetine is a Selective Serotonin Reuptake Inhibitor (SSRI) used for major depressive illness, obsessive-compulsive disorder and bulimia nervosa.3 Besides deafness, the hearing disorders tinnitus and hyperacusis (an increased sensitivity to sound) were also considered."^^xsd:string)

