# Individual: X2013_m_tapentadol_and_aggressive_reaction:aggressive_reaction (aggressive reaction pathophysiology)

AnnotationAssertion(rdfs:label X2013_m_tapentadol_and_aggressive_reaction:aggressive_reaction "aggressive reaction pathophysiology"^^xsd:string)
ClassAssertion(OpenPVSignal:Free_text_reporting_element X2013_m_tapentadol_and_aggressive_reaction:aggressive_reaction)
ObjectPropertyAssertion(mp:references X2013_m_tapentadol_and_aggressive_reaction:aggressive_reaction X2013_m_tapentadol_and_aggressive_reaction:Ref.2)
DataPropertyAssertion(OpenPVSignal:has_content X2013_m_tapentadol_and_aggressive_reaction:aggressive_reaction "Aggressive reaction, or aggression, is one of a number of ill-defined behaviour and socialisation disturbances. Aggression can be either proactive or reactive.2 Proactive aggression is goal-oriented requiring neither provocation nor anger. It can be directed towards possessing objects or dominating people. Reactive aggression involves angry outbursts in response to provocation.2 However, regardless of its psychiatric definition, an aggressive reaction is a clinical judgment"^^xsd:string)

