# Individual: X2013_m_tapentadol_and_delusion5th_2013:LiteratureAndLabelling (Literature and Labelling)

AnnotationAssertion(rdfs:label X2013_m_tapentadol_and_delusion5th_2013:LiteratureAndLabelling "Literature and Labelling"^^xsd:string)
ClassAssertion(OpenPVSignal:Literature_information X2013_m_tapentadol_and_delusion5th_2013:LiteratureAndLabelling)
ObjectPropertyAssertion(mp:references X2013_m_tapentadol_and_delusion5th_2013:LiteratureAndLabelling X2013_m_tapentadol_and_delusion5th_2013:Ref.1)
DataPropertyAssertion(OpenPVSignal:has_content X2013_m_tapentadol_and_delusion5th_2013:LiteratureAndLabelling "The product literature does not refer to delusion. However, other psychiatric reactions such as anxiety, depressed mood, sleep disorder, nervousness and restlessness are described as common and disorientation, confusion, agitation, perception disturbances, abnormal dreams and euphoria are described as uncommon.1 There have been no reports in the literature of delusion in association with tapentadol."^^xsd:string)

