DataPropertyAssertion(OpenPVSignal:has_content X2013_m_baclofen_and_renal_failure_6th:LabellingUKSPC "Kidney failure is labelled in the US FDA Label for the injection but not for the oral formulation and renal failure is not labelled in the UK Summary of Product Characteristics (SPC)."^^xsd:string)

# Individual: X2013_m_baclofen_and_renal_failure_6th:LiteratureAndLabelling (Literature and labelling)

AnnotationAssertion(rdfs:label X2013_m_baclofen_and_renal_failure_6th:LiteratureAndLabelling "Literature and labelling"^^xsd:string)
ClassAssertion(OpenPVSignal:Literature_information X2013_m_baclofen_and_renal_failure_6th:LiteratureAndLabelling)
ObjectPropertyAssertion(mp:references X2013_m_baclofen_and_renal_failure_6th:LiteratureAndLabelling X2013_m_baclofen_and_renal_failure_6th:Ref.2)
ObjectPropertyAssertion(mp:references X2013_m_baclofen_and_renal_failure_6th:LiteratureAndLabelling X2013_m_baclofen_and_renal_failure_6th:Ref.4)
DataPropertyAssertion(OpenPVSignal:has_content X2013_m_baclofen_and_renal_failure_6th:LiteratureAndLabelling "The British National Formulary lists many cautions when using baclofen in pre-existing disease such as psychiatric disease, respiratory disorders and bladder outlet obstruction. Recorded adverse effects include hypotension, respiratory or cardiovascular depression, and urinary disturbances.4 The US FDA Label lists renal failure, oliguria, renal calculus as well as hypotension and bradycardia as adverse drug events.2"^^xsd:string)

