# Individual: X2014_m_Ibuprofen_2014_1st:ConclusionContent (Conclusion content)

AnnotationAssertion(rdfs:label X2014_m_Ibuprofen_2014_1st:ConclusionContent "Conclusion content"^^xsd:string)
ClassAssertion(OpenPVSignal:Conclusion X2014_m_Ibuprofen_2014_1st:ConclusionContent)
DataPropertyAssertion(OpenPVSignal:has_content X2014_m_Ibuprofen_2014_1st:ConclusionContent "Although the information coming from spontaneous reporting is barely sufficient to support a possible signal, evidence from epidemiological studies point to a possible causal association between ibuprofen and erectile dysfunction; in addition, there is a biologically plausible explanation. There is the possibility that in certain patients and with certain dosages ibuprofen may be able to induce erectile dysfunction. The association cannot be ruled out and should be followed up."^^xsd:string)

# Individual: X2014_m_Ibuprofen_2014_1st:Confounders (Confounders)

AnnotationAssertion(rdfs:label X2014_m_Ibuprofen_2014_1st:Confounders "Confounders"^^xsd:string)
ClassAssertion(obo:OAE_0001182 X2014_m_Ibuprofen_2014_1st:Confounders)
DataPropertyAssertion(OpenPVSignal:has_content X2014_m_Ibuprofen_2014_1st:Confounders "Confounders included age (some of the patients were older than 60 years), medical conditions which may lead to this ADR, concomitant drugs and alcohol."^^xsd:string)
DataPropertyAssertion(OpenPVSignal:has_content X2014_m_Ibuprofen_2014_1st:Confounders "In eight of these cases, concomitant conditions including diabetes and neuropathy and/or concomitant substances including beta-blockers, tramadol, cimetidine and ethanol that could cause erectile dysfunction were reported."^^xsd:string)

