# Individual: X2014_m_parathyroid_hormone_and_myocardial_ischaemia_1st:PossibleMechanismOfPTHTriggeringTheAEOfInterest (Possible mechanism of PTH triggering the AE of interest)

AnnotationAssertion(rdfs:label X2014_m_parathyroid_hormone_and_myocardial_ischaemia_1st:PossibleMechanismOfPTHTriggeringTheAEOfInterest "Possible mechanism of PTH triggering the AE of interest"^^xsd:string)
ClassAssertion(OpenPVSignal:Adverse_Effect_Mechanism X2014_m_parathyroid_hormone_and_myocardial_ischaemia_1st:PossibleMechanismOfPTHTriggeringTheAEOfInterest)
ObjectPropertyAssertion(OpenPVSignal:refers_to_adverse_effect X2014_m_parathyroid_hormone_and_myocardial_ischaemia_1st:PossibleMechanismOfPTHTriggeringTheAEOfInterest X2014_m_parathyroid_hormone_and_myocardial_ischaemia_1st:cardiomyopathy)
ObjectPropertyAssertion(mp:references X2014_m_parathyroid_hormone_and_myocardial_ischaemia_1st:PossibleMechanismOfPTHTriggeringTheAEOfInterest X2014_m_parathyroid_hormone_and_myocardial_ischaemia_1st:Ref.4)
DataPropertyAssertion(OpenPVSignal:has_content X2014_m_parathyroid_hormone_and_myocardial_ischaemia_1st:PossibleMechanismOfPTHTriggeringTheAEOfInterest "It has been noted that PTH raises the plasma calcium level by causing release of calcium from the bones, increases the absorption of calcium from the small intestine, and reduces the renal excretion of calcium. In addition to these classical PTH target organs, it appears that PTH may have effects on other tissues as well. Accordingly, PTH receptors have been demonstrated in the heart, and in vitro, PTH induces hypertrophy of cardiomyocytes.4"^^xsd:string)

