# Individual: X2014_m_parathyroid_hormone_and_myocardial_ischaemia_1st:confoundingInTheSignal (confounding in the signal)

AnnotationAssertion(rdfs:label X2014_m_parathyroid_hormone_and_myocardial_ischaemia_1st:confoundingInTheSignal "confounding in the signal"^^xsd:string)
ClassAssertion(obo:OAE_0001182 X2014_m_parathyroid_hormone_and_myocardial_ischaemia_1st:confoundingInTheSignal)
DataPropertyAssertion(OpenPVSignal:has_content X2014_m_parathyroid_hormone_and_myocardial_ischaemia_1st:confoundingInTheSignal "There may, of course be other explanations for the reactions reported in this case series. Most of the patients were elderly. In some of the cases, there are possible alternative explanations such as chronic obstructive pulmonary disease in Case 5, stress in Case 6 and a history of transient ischaemic attacks, ischaemic cardiomyopathy and pulmonary fibrosis in Case 9. All cases, however, had PTH as the only suspected drug and the cases in VigiBase suggest that the association of myocardial infarction with PTH should be further reviewed."^^xsd:string)

