# Individual: X2014_m_ibuprofen_2014_2nd:Combined_Ibuprofen_and_Metamizole_treatment_-_Acute_renal_failure (Combined Ibuprofen and Metamizole treatment - Acute renal failure)

AnnotationAssertion(rdfs:label X2014_m_ibuprofen_2014_2nd:Combined_Ibuprofen_and_Metamizole_treatment_-_Acute_renal_failure "Combined Ibuprofen and Metamizole treatment - Acute renal failure"^^xsd:string)
ClassAssertion(OpenPVSignal:Pharmacovigilance_Signal_Report X2014_m_ibuprofen_2014_2nd:Combined_Ibuprofen_and_Metamizole_treatment_-_Acute_renal_failure)
ObjectPropertyAssertion(OpenPVSignal:refers_to_author X2014_m_ibuprofen_2014_2nd:Combined_Ibuprofen_and_Metamizole_treatment_-_Acute_renal_failure X2014_m_ibuprofen_2014_2nd:Prof._Staffan_Hagg)
ObjectPropertyAssertion(OpenPVSignal:refers_to_signal X2014_m_ibuprofen_2014_2nd:Combined_Ibuprofen_and_Metamizole_treatment_-_Acute_renal_failure X2014_m_ibuprofen_2014_2nd:pvSignal)
DataPropertyAssertion(OpenPVSignal:has_creation_date X2014_m_ibuprofen_2014_2nd:Combined_Ibuprofen_and_Metamizole_treatment_-_Acute_renal_failure "2014-05-01"^^xsd:date)
DataPropertyAssertion(OpenPVSignal:has_overall_conclusion X2014_m_ibuprofen_2014_2nd:Combined_Ibuprofen_and_Metamizole_treatment_-_Acute_renal_failure "causal association"^^xsd:string)

# Individual: X2014_m_ibuprofen_2014_2nd:Discussion (Discussion)

AnnotationAssertion(rdfs:label X2014_m_ibuprofen_2014_2nd:Discussion "Discussion"^^xsd:string)
ClassAssertion(OpenPVSignal:Discussion X2014_m_ibuprofen_2014_2nd:Discussion)
DataPropertyAssertion(OpenPVSignal:has_content X2014_m_ibuprofen_2014_2nd:Discussion "Acute renal failure is a well-documented adverse reaction to NSAIDs such as ibuprofen. In addition, metamizole has been associated with acute renal failure although the available evidence is limited. Comparing the proportion of reports in VigiBase where acute renal failure is reported as an ADR when taking both the drugs together (7.7%) compare to the proportion of reports where the ADR is reported taking ibuprofen or metamizole separately (2.0% and 0.9% respectively), demonstrates that concomitant treatment with the two drugs might increase the risk for developing acute renal failure.
The review of the post-marketing cases, especially the 14 where the drugs were reported as suspected or interacting together with the eight ICSRs where both ibuprofen and metamizole were reported as interacting, reveals that the reporter suspected a possible interaction between the  drugs which should be considered in the assessment. Studying all the ICSRs, a time-to- onset pattern for developing the ADR was identified in four cases after having added either ibuprofen or metamizole to the treatment. Taking this reported information together gives as an association that concomitant treatment with ibuprofen and metamizole could be associated with acute renal failure.
In four cases, diclofenac was used as concomitant drug which can be an additional risk factor for acute renal failure. In three of the recovered cases the drugs were withdrawn at the same time, which makes it difficult to determine which one of the drugs that might have caused the ADR, but at the same time it demonstrates that these drugs together might increase the risk of developing acute renal failure. Although multi-ingredients drugs with both substances have been launched in some countries, the combination treatment seems irrational from a pharmacological perspective and should therefore probably be avoided.
Whether the risk of acute renal failure during concomi- tant treatment of ibuprofen and metamizole is additi- vely or synergistically increased compared with the risk when these drugs are used separately is difficult to evaluate using spontaneously submitted reports."^^xsd:string)

