# Individual: X2014_m_ibuprofen_2014_2nd:Literature_and_Labelling (Literature and Labelling)

AnnotationAssertion(rdfs:label X2014_m_ibuprofen_2014_2nd:Literature_and_Labelling "Literature and Labelling"^^xsd:string)
ClassAssertion(OpenPVSignal:Literature_information X2014_m_ibuprofen_2014_2nd:Literature_and_Labelling)
ObjectPropertyAssertion(mp:references X2014_m_ibuprofen_2014_2nd:Literature_and_Labelling X2014_m_ibuprofen_2014_2nd:ref10)
ObjectPropertyAssertion(mp:references X2014_m_ibuprofen_2014_2nd:Literature_and_Labelling X2014_m_ibuprofen_2014_2nd:ref9)
DataPropertyAssertion(OpenPVSignal:has_content X2014_m_ibuprofen_2014_2nd:Literature_and_Labelling "The interaction has not been described in available drug interaction sources such as Stockley’s Drug Interactions9 or Swedish Finnish Interaction X- referencing (SFINX).10 A literature search in Medline has not revealed any published cases where acute renal failure was associated with the combination ibuprofen and metamizole."^^xsd:string)

# Individual: X2014_m_ibuprofen_2014_2nd:Mechanism_metamizole (Mechanism metamizole)

AnnotationAssertion(rdfs:label X2014_m_ibuprofen_2014_2nd:Mechanism_metamizole "Mechanism metamizole"^^xsd:string)
ClassAssertion(OpenPVSignal:Mechanism X2014_m_ibuprofen_2014_2nd:Mechanism_metamizole)
ObjectPropertyAssertion(mp:references X2014_m_ibuprofen_2014_2nd:Mechanism_metamizole X2014_m_ibuprofen_2014_2nd:ref1)
DataPropertyAssertion(OpenPVSignal:has_content X2014_m_ibuprofen_2014_2nd:Mechanism_metamizole "Metamizole is a pirazolone derivative of analgesic and antipyretic action, but without an anti-inflammatory effect. Both ibuprofen and metamizole inhibit cyclooxygenase (COX), but metamizole has a different mode of action compared to classical COX-inhibitors.1"^^xsd:string)

