# Individual: X2014_m_ibuprofen_2014_2nd:introduction (introduction)

AnnotationAssertion(rdfs:label X2014_m_ibuprofen_2014_2nd:introduction "introduction"^^xsd:string)
ClassAssertion(OpenPVSignal:Introduction X2014_m_ibuprofen_2014_2nd:introduction)
ObjectPropertyAssertion(mp:references X2014_m_ibuprofen_2014_2nd:introduction X2014_m_ibuprofen_2014_2nd:ref1)
ObjectPropertyAssertion(mp:references X2014_m_ibuprofen_2014_2nd:introduction X2014_m_ibuprofen_2014_2nd:ref2)
ObjectPropertyAssertion(mp:references X2014_m_ibuprofen_2014_2nd:introduction X2014_m_ibuprofen_2014_2nd:ref3)
ObjectPropertyAssertion(mp:references X2014_m_ibuprofen_2014_2nd:introduction X2014_m_ibuprofen_2014_2nd:ref4)
ObjectPropertyAssertion(mp:references X2014_m_ibuprofen_2014_2nd:introduction X2014_m_ibuprofen_2014_2nd:ref5)
ObjectPropertyAssertion(mp:references X2014_m_ibuprofen_2014_2nd:introduction X2014_m_ibuprofen_2014_2nd:ref6)
ObjectPropertyAssertion(mp:references X2014_m_ibuprofen_2014_2nd:introduction X2014_m_ibuprofen_2014_2nd:ref7)
ObjectPropertyAssertion(mp:references X2014_m_ibuprofen_2014_2nd:introduction X2014_m_ibuprofen_2014_2nd:ref8)
DataPropertyAssertion(OpenPVSignal:has_content X2014_m_ibuprofen_2014_2nd:introduction "Ibuprofen is a non-steroidal anti-inflammatory drug (NSAID), a class of medications widely used for their analgesic and anti-inflammatory benefits. Metamizole is a pirazolone derivative of analgesic and antipyretic action, but without an anti- inflammatory effect. Both ibuprofen and metamizole inhibit cyclooxygenase (COX), but metamizole has a different mode of action compared to classical COX-inhibitors.1 NSAIDs are known to induce several different types of renal injury including acute renal failure.2 This adverse reaction may occur with any non-selective NSAID or COX-2 specific NSAID3-6 and is a well- documented adverse reaction to ibuprofen.1 The biological mechanism for acute renal failure during NSAID treatment is inhibition of COX enzymes with consequent decreased synthesis of prostaglandins, which can lead to reversible renal ischemia, a reduction in glomerular filtration, and acute renal insufficiency.3,4
The association between acute renal failure and metamizole is less well documented. A number of sporadic cases published in the literature and the pharmacological properties with COX inhibition support an association.7,8"^^xsd:string)

