ClassAssertion(OpenPVSignal:Case_Report_Information X2014_m_agomelatine_and_hypotension_4th:BloodPressureReadings)
DataPropertyAssertion(OpenPVSignal:has_content X2014_m_agomelatine_and_hypotension_4th:BloodPressureReadings "Blood pressure readings were provided for four patients regularly treated (90/60 mmHg; 74/40 mmHg; 100/75 mmHg; 110/70 mmHg) and for three patients with an intentional overdose (70/40 mmHg; 70/(not available) mmHg; 106/45 mmHg)."^^xsd:string)

# Individual: X2014_m_agomelatine_and_hypotension_4th:CamposData (Campos data)

AnnotationAssertion(rdfs:label X2014_m_agomelatine_and_hypotension_4th:CamposData "Campos data"^^xsd:string)
ClassAssertion(obo:OAE_0001197 X2014_m_agomelatine_and_hypotension_4th:CamposData)
ObjectPropertyAssertion(OpenPVSignal:refers_to_adverse_effect X2014_m_agomelatine_and_hypotension_4th:CamposData X2014_m_agomelatine_and_hypotension_4th:agomelatine)
ObjectPropertyAssertion(OpenPVSignal:refers_to_adverse_effect X2014_m_agomelatine_and_hypotension_4th:CamposData X2014_m_agomelatine_and_hypotension_4th:bloodPressureDecreased)
ObjectPropertyAssertion(mp:references X2014_m_agomelatine_and_hypotension_4th:CamposData X2014_m_agomelatine_and_hypotension_4th:Ref3)
ObjectPropertyAssertion(mp:references X2014_m_agomelatine_and_hypotension_4th:CamposData X2014_m_agomelatine_and_hypotension_4th:Ref4)
DataPropertyAssertion(OpenPVSignal:has_content X2014_m_agomelatine_and_hypotension_4th:CamposData "Campos et al studied the effect of exogenous melatonin in normotensive rats: a continuous infusion of melatonin induced a significant decrease in blood pressure as well as a reduction in heart rate, hinting at a blunting of the baroreceptor reflex through the area postrema. Ablation of the area postrema, on the other hand, abolished the melatonin effects."^^xsd:string)

# Individual: X2014_m_agomelatine_and_hypotension_4th:ConclusionContent (Conclusion content)

AnnotationAssertion(rdfs:label X2014_m_agomelatine_and_hypotension_4th:ConclusionContent "Conclusion content"^^xsd:string)
ClassAssertion(OpenPVSignal:Conclusion X2014_m_agomelatine_and_hypotension_4th:ConclusionContent)
ClassAssertion(OpenPVSignal:Discussion X2014_m_agomelatine_and_hypotension_4th:ConclusionContent)
DataPropertyAssertion(OpenPVSignal:has_content X2014_m_agomelatine_and_hypotension_4th:ConclusionContent "The combination agomelatine — hypotension does not stand out statistically in VigiBase. However, the published literature on melatonin (and to a significantly lesser extent on melatoninergic drugs) supports a possible, multifactorial involvement of these compounds in the regulation of arterial pressure.
The analysed ICSRs point at a positive causal relationship based on a consistent time to onset (the two outliers with longer times to onset might be explained by a concurrent reported infection that might have triggered the hypotensive episode in one case and an extensive comedication with missing therapy dates in the other), the high number of positive dechallenges reported and the patient experiencing a positive rechallenge.
In conclusion, we consider hypotension under agomelatine a signal that should be taken into consideration when prescribing this medication."^^xsd:string)

# Individual: X2014_m_agomelatine_and_hypotension_4th:EuropeanSPCForAgomelatine (European SPC for agomelatine)

AnnotationAssertion(rdfs:label X2014_m_agomelatine_and_hypotension_4th:EuropeanSPCForAgomelatine "European SPC for agomelatine"^^xsd:string)
ClassAssertion(OpenPVSignal:Structured_Product_Labels_information X2014_m_agomelatine_and_hypotension_4th:EuropeanSPCForAgomelatine)
ObjectPropertyAssertion(OpenPVSignal:refers_to_drug X2014_m_agomelatine_and_hypotension_4th:EuropeanSPCForAgomelatine X2014_m_agomelatine_and_hypotension_4th:agomelatine)
DataPropertyAssertion(OpenPVSignal:has_content X2014_m_agomelatine_and_hypotension_4th:EuropeanSPCForAgomelatine "Hypotension/orthostatic hypotension is not listed in the European SPC for agomelatine. According to the same text, agomelatine had neutral effect on heart rate and blood pressure in clinical trials."^^xsd:string)

# Individual: X2014_m_agomelatine_and_hypotension_4th:Hypotension_pathobiology (Hypotension pathophysiology)

AnnotationAssertion(rdfs:label X2014_m_agomelatine_and_hypotension_4th:Hypotension_pathobiology "Hypotension pathophysiology"^^xsd:string)
ClassAssertion(obo:OAE_0000005 X2014_m_agomelatine_and_hypotension_4th:Hypotension_pathobiology)
ObjectPropertyAssertion(OpenPVSignal:refers_to_adverse_effect X2014_m_agomelatine_and_hypotension_4th:Hypotension_pathobiology X2014_m_agomelatine_and_hypotension_4th:hypotension)
DataPropertyAssertion(OpenPVSignal:has_content X2014_m_agomelatine_and_hypotension_4th:Hypotension_pathobiology "Hypotension is a physiologic state characterized by abnormally low blood pressure. As normal blood pressure varies with age, there is no absolute threshold to define hypotension. In a younger adult hypotension might be defined as systolic pressure <90 mmHg and diastolic pressure <60 mmHg. As blood pressure is influenced by different factors such as cardiac output, vascular resistance and venous return and pressure, any change in one of these variables can lead to fluctuations in blood pressure."^^xsd:string)

