# Individual: X2014_m_dronedarone_ventricular_arrhythmia_6th:potentialInteractionWithAntiarrythmicDrugs (potential interaction with antiarrythmic drugs)

AnnotationAssertion(rdfs:label X2014_m_dronedarone_ventricular_arrhythmia_6th:potentialInteractionWithAntiarrythmicDrugs "potential interaction with antiarrythmic drugs"^^xsd:string)
ClassAssertion(obo:OAE_0001182 X2014_m_dronedarone_ventricular_arrhythmia_6th:potentialInteractionWithAntiarrythmicDrugs)
DataPropertyAssertion(OpenPVSignal:has_content X2014_m_dronedarone_ventricular_arrhythmia_6th:potentialInteractionWithAntiarrythmicDrugs "A potential interaction should be taken into consideration. Dronedarone has a warning for concomitant use of β-blockers, calcium antagonists or digoxin. It is recommended to reduce the dose of these drugs especially for increased risk of toxicity. On the other hand, as the washout period was not enough to eliminate arrhythmic events associated with other antiarrhythmic drugs, a residual effect of amiodarone, sotalol or flecainide could be another explanation"^^xsd:string)

# Individual: X2014_m_dronedarone_ventricular_arrhythmia_6th:potentialMechanismOfDronedaroneTriggeringArrhythmias (potential mechanism of dronedarone triggering arrhythmias)

AnnotationAssertion(rdfs:label X2014_m_dronedarone_ventricular_arrhythmia_6th:potentialMechanismOfDronedaroneTriggeringArrhythmias "potential mechanism of dronedarone triggering arrhythmias"^^xsd:string)
ClassAssertion(OpenPVSignal:Adverse_Effect_Mechanism X2014_m_dronedarone_ventricular_arrhythmia_6th:potentialMechanismOfDronedaroneTriggeringArrhythmias)
ObjectPropertyAssertion(OpenPVSignal:refers_to_adverse_effect X2014_m_dronedarone_ventricular_arrhythmia_6th:potentialMechanismOfDronedaroneTriggeringArrhythmias X2014_m_dronedarone_ventricular_arrhythmia_6th:proarrhythmic_effect)
ObjectPropertyAssertion(mp:references X2014_m_dronedarone_ventricular_arrhythmia_6th:potentialMechanismOfDronedaroneTriggeringArrhythmias X2014_m_dronedarone_ventricular_arrhythmia_6th:Ref.3)
ObjectPropertyAssertion(mp:references X2014_m_dronedarone_ventricular_arrhythmia_6th:potentialMechanismOfDronedaroneTriggeringArrhythmias X2014_m_dronedarone_ventricular_arrhythmia_6th:Ref.4)
DataPropertyAssertion(OpenPVSignal:has_content X2014_m_dronedarone_ventricular_arrhythmia_6th:potentialMechanismOfDronedaroneTriggeringArrhythmias "There is evidence that the inhibition of potassium currents appears to trigger early after depolarizations (EAD) in animals. These EADs may trigger another action potential and promote triggered activity; therefore it might induce reentry and lead to proarrhythmic events.3,4"^^xsd:string)

