# Individual: X2014_m_finasterine_and_convulsions_4th:PotentialMechanismOfFinasterideTriggeringconvulsions-theGABAAParadigm (Potential mechanism of finasteride triggering convulsions-the GABAA paradigm)

AnnotationAssertion(rdfs:label X2014_m_finasterine_and_convulsions_4th:PotentialMechanismOfFinasterideTriggeringconvulsions-theGABAAParadigm "Potential mechanism of finasteride triggering convulsions-the GABAA paradigm"^^xsd:string)
ClassAssertion(OpenPVSignal:Adverse_Effect_Mechanism X2014_m_finasterine_and_convulsions_4th:PotentialMechanismOfFinasterideTriggeringconvulsions-theGABAAParadigm)
ObjectPropertyAssertion(OpenPVSignal:refers_to_adverse_effect X2014_m_finasterine_and_convulsions_4th:PotentialMechanismOfFinasterideTriggeringconvulsions-theGABAAParadigm X2014_m_finasterine_and_convulsions_4th:convulsions)
ObjectPropertyAssertion(mp:references X2014_m_finasterine_and_convulsions_4th:PotentialMechanismOfFinasterideTriggeringconvulsions-theGABAAParadigm X2014_m_finasterine_and_convulsions_4th:ref15)
ObjectPropertyAssertion(mp:references X2014_m_finasterine_and_convulsions_4th:PotentialMechanismOfFinasterideTriggeringconvulsions-theGABAAParadigm X2014_m_finasterine_and_convulsions_4th:ref16)
DataPropertyAssertion(OpenPVSignal:has_content X2014_m_finasterine_and_convulsions_4th:PotentialMechanismOfFinasterideTriggeringconvulsions-theGABAAParadigm "Finasteride crosses the blood-brain barrier so it has the potential to reduce neurosteroid synthesis in the brain, through inhibition of 5a-reductase: in patients who exhibit seizure susceptibility, this might be enough to further lower seizure threshold and trigger convulsions."^^xsd:string)
DataPropertyAssertion(OpenPVSignal:has_content X2014_m_finasterine_and_convulsions_4th:PotentialMechanismOfFinasterideTriggeringconvulsions-theGABAAParadigm "The enzyme 5a-reductase is involved in the production of the endogenous neurosteroids 5a- THDOC (from deoxycorticosterone) ,allopregnanolone (from progesterone) and androstanediol (from testosterone). Recent studies on mice have shown that these endogenous neurosteroids may reduce seizure susceptibility by enhancing the inhibitory effects of GABA on GABAA receptors. Hence, neurosteroids act as allosteric modulators of GABAA, similar to barbiturates or benzodiazepines.16 Inhibition of 5a-reductase by finasteride, with consequent reduction in the production of endogenous neurosteroids, may increase the potential for seizure activity"^^xsd:string)

