DataPropertyAssertion(OpenPVSignal:has_content X2014_m_finasterine_and_convulsions_4th:case29 "one patient accidentally took two doses of finasteride instead of one (case 29). "^^xsd:string)

# Individual: X2014_m_finasterine_and_convulsions_4th:case3 (case 3 info)

AnnotationAssertion(rdfs:label X2014_m_finasterine_and_convulsions_4th:case3 "case 3 info"^^xsd:string)
ClassAssertion(OpenPVSignal:Case_Report_Information X2014_m_finasterine_and_convulsions_4th:case3)
DataPropertyAssertion(OpenPVSignal:has_content X2014_m_finasterine_and_convulsions_4th:case3 "Two patients (case 3 — alcoholic, and 21), were found to have high levels of alcohol when the event occurred"^^xsd:string)
DataPropertyAssertion(OpenPVSignal:has_content X2014_m_finasterine_and_convulsions_4th:case3 "case 3 involves an alcoholic patient who had one hypoglycaemic seizure and recovered after glucose infusion."^^xsd:string)

# Individual: X2014_m_finasterine_and_convulsions_4th:case30 (case 30 info)

AnnotationAssertion(rdfs:label X2014_m_finasterine_and_convulsions_4th:case30 "case 30 info"^^xsd:string)
ClassAssertion(OpenPVSignal:Case_Report_Information X2014_m_finasterine_and_convulsions_4th:case30)
DataPropertyAssertion(OpenPVSignal:has_content X2014_m_finasterine_and_convulsions_4th:case30 "One patient reported to have had his first seizure after one year of treatment with finasteride, but the seizures occurred at shorter intervals thereafter and resolved upon discontinuation of the medicine (case 30)"^^xsd:string)

# Individual: X2014_m_finasterine_and_convulsions_4th:case_15_info (case 15 info)

AnnotationAssertion(rdfs:label X2014_m_finasterine_and_convulsions_4th:case_15_info "case 15 info"^^xsd:string)
ClassAssertion(OpenPVSignal:Case_Report_Information X2014_m_finasterine_and_convulsions_4th:case_15_info)
ObjectPropertyAssertion(mp:references X2014_m_finasterine_and_convulsions_4th:case_15_info X2014_m_finasterine_and_convulsions_4th:ref8)
DataPropertyAssertion(OpenPVSignal:has_content X2014_m_finasterine_and_convulsions_4th:case_15_info "One of the case reports (which was also reported to VigiBase and appears as case 15 in Table 1 below) concerns a woman from Italy who developed focal seizures at the age of 43 years. Two years later the seizures intensified and carbamazepine 800 mg per day was initiated. The seizures were kept under control for one year, until one night she experienced a convulsive seizure and, despite therapeutic levels of carbamazepine, her seizures relapsed with a frequency of eight to 10 seizures per year. Lamotrigine (300 mg) was added to her treatment regimen but the seizures were not controlled. The patient had a history of mild hirsutism for which she was treated with finasteride from age 45 years. Following discontinuation of finasteride at age 50 years, the lamotrigine dose was gradually reduced and withdrawn, and the carbamazepine dose was reduced to 600 mg without further seizures.8"^^xsd:string)

