# Individual: X2014_m_finasterine_and_convulsions_4th:inVivoExperiments (in vivo experiments)

AnnotationAssertion(rdfs:label X2014_m_finasterine_and_convulsions_4th:inVivoExperiments "in vivo experiments"^^xsd:string)
ClassAssertion(obo:OAE_0001197 X2014_m_finasterine_and_convulsions_4th:inVivoExperiments)
ObjectPropertyAssertion(OpenPVSignal:refers_to_adverse_effect X2014_m_finasterine_and_convulsions_4th:inVivoExperiments X2014_m_finasterine_and_convulsions_4th:convulsions)
ObjectPropertyAssertion(OpenPVSignal:refers_to_drug X2014_m_finasterine_and_convulsions_4th:inVivoExperiments X2014_m_finasterine_and_convulsions_4th:finasteride)
ObjectPropertyAssertion(mp:references X2014_m_finasterine_and_convulsions_4th:inVivoExperiments X2014_m_finasterine_and_convulsions_4th:ref15)
ObjectPropertyAssertion(mp:references X2014_m_finasterine_and_convulsions_4th:inVivoExperiments X2014_m_finasterine_and_convulsions_4th:ref16)
ObjectPropertyAssertion(mp:references X2014_m_finasterine_and_convulsions_4th:inVivoExperiments X2014_m_finasterine_and_convulsions_4th:ref17)
DataPropertyAssertion(OpenPVSignal:has_content X2014_m_finasterine_and_convulsions_4th:inVivoExperiments "The enzyme 5a-reductase is involved in the production of the endogenous neurosteroids 5a-THDOC (from deoxycorticosterone) ,allopregnanolone (from progesterone) and androstanediol (from testosterone). Recent studies on mice have shown that these endogenous neurosteroids may reduce seizure susceptibility by enhancing the inhibitory effects of GABA on GABAA receptors. Hence, neurosteroids act as allosteric modulators of GABAA, similar to barbiturates or benzodiazepines.16 Inhibition of 5a-reductase by finasteride, with consequent reduction in the production of endogenous neurosteroids, may increase the potential for seizure activity. Permanently lowering the seizure threshold in rats and subsequently administering finasteride in dose ranges compatible with humans, resulted in the development of seizures.15 Relatively long times to seizure onset have been explained by the time it takes for existing neurosteroids to be broken down.17"^^xsd:string)

