# Individual: X2014_m_finasterine_and_convulsions_4th:literature_case (literature case)

AnnotationAssertion(rdfs:label X2014_m_finasterine_and_convulsions_4th:literature_case "literature case"^^xsd:string)
ClassAssertion(obo:OAE_0001197 X2014_m_finasterine_and_convulsions_4th:literature_case)
ObjectPropertyAssertion(OpenPVSignal:refers_to_adverse_effect X2014_m_finasterine_and_convulsions_4th:literature_case X2014_m_finasterine_and_convulsions_4th:convulsions)
ObjectPropertyAssertion(OpenPVSignal:refers_to_drug X2014_m_finasterine_and_convulsions_4th:literature_case X2014_m_finasterine_and_convulsions_4th:finasteride)
DataPropertyAssertion(OpenPVSignal:has_content X2014_m_finasterine_and_convulsions_4th:literature_case "The second case describes a 34-year-old obese, woman with hirsutism who suffered from intractable complex partial and generalized seizures, managed with 400 mg carbamazepine per day. She was treated with progesterone and her general seizure profile improved for two years. However, seizure frequency and severity increased after the introduction of finasteride, even though carbamazepine levels were within therapeutic range. The patient's condition returned to baseline levels after finasteride was withdrawn."^^xsd:string)

