# Individual: X2014_m_febuxostat_and_cardiac_failure_5th:labelling_for_febuxostat (labelling for febuxostat)

AnnotationAssertion(rdfs:label X2014_m_febuxostat_and_cardiac_failure_5th:labelling_for_febuxostat "labelling for febuxostat"^^xsd:string)
ClassAssertion(OpenPVSignal:Structured_Product_Labels_information X2014_m_febuxostat_and_cardiac_failure_5th:labelling_for_febuxostat)
ObjectPropertyAssertion(OpenPVSignal:refers_to_drug X2014_m_febuxostat_and_cardiac_failure_5th:labelling_for_febuxostat X2014_m_febuxostat_and_cardiac_failure_5th:febuxostat)
ObjectPropertyAssertion(mp:references X2014_m_febuxostat_and_cardiac_failure_5th:labelling_for_febuxostat X2014_m_febuxostat_and_cardiac_failure_5th:Ref.5)
ObjectPropertyAssertion(mp:references X2014_m_febuxostat_and_cardiac_failure_5th:labelling_for_febuxostat X2014_m_febuxostat_and_cardiac_failure_5th:Ref.6)
ObjectPropertyAssertion(mp:references X2014_m_febuxostat_and_cardiac_failure_5th:labelling_for_febuxostat X2014_m_febuxostat_and_cardiac_failure_5th:Ref.7)
ObjectPropertyAssertion(mp:references X2014_m_febuxostat_and_cardiac_failure_5th:labelling_for_febuxostat X2014_m_febuxostat_and_cardiac_failure_5th:Ref.8)
DataPropertyAssertion(OpenPVSignal:has_content X2014_m_febuxostat_and_cardiac_failure_5th:labelling_for_febuxostat "The registration labels for febuxostat in the United States and Europe are slightly different. The FDA has approved a dose of 40 and 80 mg per day respectively while the EMA has approved a daily dose of 80 and 120 mg. The EMA has advised to avoid the drug in patients diagnosed with coronary artery disease (CAD) and congestive heart failure (CHF). Adjustment of the dose in patients with renal impairment is not needed. There is no warning for cardiac failure. Febuxostat is not considered cost-effective in comparison to allopuri- nol as first-line therapy but is generally considered equi- valently tolerated and at least similarly effective.5,6, 7,8"^^xsd:string)

