ObjectPropertyAssertion(mp:references X2014_m_agomelatine_and_thrombocytopenia_6th:ListedAEForAgomelatin X2014_m_agomelatine_and_thrombocytopenia_6th:Ref.6)
DataPropertyAssertion(OpenPVSignal:has_content X2014_m_agomelatine_and_thrombocytopenia_6th:ListedAEForAgomelatin "Thrombocytopenia is not listed among undesirable effects in the UKSPC for agomelatine."^^xsd:string)

# Individual: X2014_m_agomelatine_and_thrombocytopenia_6th:LiteratureAndLabelling (Literature and Labelling)

AnnotationAssertion(rdfs:label X2014_m_agomelatine_and_thrombocytopenia_6th:LiteratureAndLabelling "Literature and Labelling"^^xsd:string)
ClassAssertion(OpenPVSignal:Literature_information X2014_m_agomelatine_and_thrombocytopenia_6th:LiteratureAndLabelling)
ObjectPropertyAssertion(mp:references X2014_m_agomelatine_and_thrombocytopenia_6th:LiteratureAndLabelling X2014_m_agomelatine_and_thrombocytopenia_6th:Ref.5)
ObjectPropertyAssertion(mp:references X2014_m_agomelatine_and_thrombocytopenia_6th:LiteratureAndLabelling X2014_m_agomelatine_and_thrombocytopenia_6th:Ref.6)
ObjectPropertyAssertion(mp:references X2014_m_agomelatine_and_thrombocytopenia_6th:LiteratureAndLabelling X2014_m_agomelatine_and_thrombocytopenia_6th:Ref.7)
ObjectPropertyAssertion(mp:references X2014_m_agomelatine_and_thrombocytopenia_6th:LiteratureAndLabelling X2014_m_agomelatine_and_thrombocytopenia_6th:Ref.8)
DataPropertyAssertion(OpenPVSignal:has_content X2014_m_agomelatine_and_thrombocytopenia_6th:LiteratureAndLabelling "Thrombocytopenia is not listed among undesirable effects in the UKSPC for agomelatine.6 Many agomelatine placebo-controlled and active comparator trials have been published, in which the most common adverse effects reported were headache, dizziness, somnolence, diarrhoea, nausea, sedation, fatigue and insomnia.5 There are no published cases of agomelatine and thrombocytopenia or thrombocytopenic purpura in the literature. In March 2011 the Netherlands Pharmacovigilance Centre Lareb published an overview on 39 received reports related to the use of agomelatine. These reports contained a total of 93 possible adverse drug reactions including two cases of thrombocytopenia. In the overview they said that thrombocytopenia will be monitored, and possibly analysed in the future.7 In September 2013 the EMA also presented an overview of agomelatine, including two cases of thrombocytopenic purpura. In both cases positive dechallenges were reported but overall the evidence was not considered sufficient to conclude that there was an association. The MAH was requested to keep agomelatine and thrombocytopenic purpura under close monitoring.8"^^xsd:string)

