ObjectPropertyAssertion(mp:references X2014_m_agomelatine_and_thrombocytopenia_6th:common_ADRs_of_agomelatine X2014_m_agomelatine_and_thrombocytopenia_6th:Ref.4)
ObjectPropertyAssertion(mp:references X2014_m_agomelatine_and_thrombocytopenia_6th:common_ADRs_of_agomelatine X2014_m_agomelatine_and_thrombocytopenia_6th:Ref.5)
DataPropertyAssertion(OpenPVSignal:has_content X2014_m_agomelatine_and_thrombocytopenia_6th:common_ADRs_of_agomelatine "Many agomelatine placebo-controlled and active comparator trials have been published, in which the most common adverse effects reported were headache, dizziness, somnolence, diarrhoea, nausea, sedation, fatigue and insomnia.5"^^xsd:string)
DataPropertyAssertion(OpenPVSignal:has_content X2014_m_agomelatine_and_thrombocytopenia_6th:common_ADRs_of_agomelatine "The most common adverse effects that occur within the first few weeks of agomelatine treatment are transient nausea and dizziness, which are usually mild or moderate. Other gastrointestinal disturbances, headache, somnolence, insomnia, migraine, hyperhidrosis, back pain and fatigue are also reported as being common adverse effects.4"^^xsd:string)

