# Individual: X2014_m_dronedarone_and_vision_abnormal_6th:LiteratureAndLabelling (Literature and labelling)

AnnotationAssertion(rdfs:label X2014_m_dronedarone_and_vision_abnormal_6th:LiteratureAndLabelling "Literature and labelling"^^xsd:string)
ClassAssertion(OpenPVSignal:Literature_information X2014_m_dronedarone_and_vision_abnormal_6th:LiteratureAndLabelling)
ObjectPropertyAssertion(mp:references X2014_m_dronedarone_and_vision_abnormal_6th:LiteratureAndLabelling X2014_m_dronedarone_and_vision_abnormal_6th:Ref.4)
DataPropertyAssertion(OpenPVSignal:has_content X2014_m_dronedarone_and_vision_abnormal_6th:LiteratureAndLabelling "The product literature does not refer to vision abnormal. There are no reports of vision abnormal in association with dronedarone in the literature. There is, however, an isolated report of blurred vision in the DIONYSOS trial which compared the efficacy and safety of amiodarone and dronedarone in patients with persistent AF. In this trial, there was a report of blur- red vision in one of 249 patients taking dronedarone as well as a report of blurred vision in one of 255 patients taking amiodarone.4"^^xsd:string)

# Individual: X2014_m_dronedarone_and_vision_abnormal_6th:MechanismContent (Mechanism of dronedarone)

AnnotationAssertion(rdfs:label X2014_m_dronedarone_and_vision_abnormal_6th:MechanismContent "Mechanism of dronedarone"^^xsd:string)
ClassAssertion(OpenPVSignal:Mechanism X2014_m_dronedarone_and_vision_abnormal_6th:MechanismContent)
ObjectPropertyAssertion(mp:references X2014_m_dronedarone_and_vision_abnormal_6th:MechanismContent X2014_m_dronedarone_and_vision_abnormal_6th:Ref.1)
DataPropertyAssertion(OpenPVSignal:has_content X2014_m_dronedarone_and_vision_abnormal_6th:MechanismContent "Dronedarone has been shown to prevent atrial fibrillation (AF) or restore normal sinus rhythm depending on the model used. The drug can also prevent ventricular tachycardia and ventricular fibrillation in several animal models. These effects most likely result from its electrophysiological properties belonging to all four Vaughan-Williams classes. Dronedarone is a multichannel blocker inhibiting the potassium currents and thus prolonging cardiac action potential and refractory periods. It also inhibits the sodium currents and the calcium currents. It also non-competitively antagonises adrenergic activities. It is indicated for the maintenance of sinus rhythm after successful cardioversion in adult clinically stable patients with paroxysmal or persistent atrial fibrillation."^^xsd:string)

