DataPropertyAssertion(OpenPVSignal:has_content X2014_m_dronedarone_and_vision_abnormal_6th:vision_abnormal_pathophysiology "Vision abnormal is a non-specific term which refers to a change, usually a deterioration, in visual function or perception.2 In WHO-ART, vision abnormal is a preferred term (PT) which encompasses many included terms (ITs) consisting of amblyopia (reduced vision in an apparently normal eye), asthenopia (eye strain), depth perception difficulty, metaporphopsia (a specific type of distorted vision), refractive error, tired eye, vision abnormal, vision abnormal aggravated, vision blurred, vision decreased, visual acuity alteration, visual disturbance and visual impairment."^^xsd:string)

