# Individual: X2015_m_Hexetidine_and_severe_hypersensitivity_1st_2015:Azorubin (Azorubin info)

AnnotationAssertion(rdfs:label X2015_m_Hexetidine_and_severe_hypersensitivity_1st_2015:Azorubin "Azorubin info"^^xsd:string)
ClassAssertion(OpenPVSignal:Free_text_reporting_element X2015_m_Hexetidine_and_severe_hypersensitivity_1st_2015:Azorubin)
ObjectPropertyAssertion(OpenPVSignal:refers_to_drug X2015_m_Hexetidine_and_severe_hypersensitivity_1st_2015:Azorubin X2015_m_Hexetidine_and_severe_hypersensitivity_1st_2015:azorubin)
DataPropertyAssertion(OpenPVSignal:has_content X2015_m_Hexetidine_and_severe_hypersensitivity_1st_2015:Azorubin "Commercial hexetidine solutions contain azorubin (E122), known as a potential allergen. Salicylate intolerance is considered a risk factor for allergic reactions to azorubin. While E122 is banned in the USA, it is allowed in Europe as a food colorant and as an additive to medicinal products which must be listed in the product information leaflet."^^xsd:string)

# Individual: X2015_m_Hexetidine_and_severe_hypersensitivity_1st_2015:AzorubinAndAllergicReactions (Azorubin and allergic reactions)

