DataPropertyAssertion(OpenPVSignal:has_content X2015_m_Hexetidine_and_severe_hypersensitivity_1st_2015:HypersensitivityTriggeredByChlorhexidine "Hexetidine is not as widely used as chlorhexidine, an antiseptic well known to induce severe allergic reactions and no cross-sensitivity between the two substances has been documented: hexetidine has been recommended as a therapeutic alternative for patients sensitized to chlorhexidine."^^xsd:string)

# Individual: X2015_m_Hexetidine_and_severe_hypersensitivity_1st_2015:Hypersensitivity_background (Hypersensitivity background)

AnnotationAssertion(rdfs:label X2015_m_Hexetidine_and_severe_hypersensitivity_1st_2015:Hypersensitivity_background "Hypersensitivity background"^^xsd:string)
ClassAssertion(OpenPVSignal:Free_text_reporting_element X2015_m_Hexetidine_and_severe_hypersensitivity_1st_2015:Hypersensitivity_background)
ObjectPropertyAssertion(OpenPVSignal:refers_to_adverse_effect X2015_m_Hexetidine_and_severe_hypersensitivity_1st_2015:Hypersensitivity_background X2015_m_Hexetidine_and_severe_hypersensitivity_1st_2015:hypersensitivity)
ObjectPropertyAssertion(mp:references X2015_m_Hexetidine_and_severe_hypersensitivity_1st_2015:Hypersensitivity_background X2015_m_Hexetidine_and_severe_hypersensitivity_1st_2015:Ref.1)
ObjectPropertyAssertion(mp:references X2015_m_Hexetidine_and_severe_hypersensitivity_1st_2015:Hypersensitivity_background X2015_m_Hexetidine_and_severe_hypersensitivity_1st_2015:Ref.2)
DataPropertyAssertion(OpenPVSignal:has_content X2015_m_Hexetidine_and_severe_hypersensitivity_1st_2015:Hypersensitivity_background "Hypersensitivity (or allergic/anaphylactic) reactions are caused by interactions between immunologically active antigens and humoral antibodies or sensitized lymphocytes causing a wide range of minor to life-threatening symptoms. Life-threatening reactions that compromise respiratory and circulatory functions are described as anaphylaxis. The Gell and Coombs classification describes Type I (immediate type) reactions as IgE mediated with release of potent vasoactive and inflammatory mediators that cause vasodilation, increased capillary permeability, spasms of smooth muscles and inflammatory tissues reactions within hours.1 Anaphylactoid reactions are not IgE mediated but present the same clinical picture.2"^^xsd:string)

