# Individual: X2015_m_linagliptin_cardiac_failure_1st_2015:AlogliptinClinicalTrial (Alogliptin clinical trial)

AnnotationAssertion(rdfs:label X2015_m_linagliptin_cardiac_failure_1st_2015:AlogliptinClinicalTrial "Alogliptin clinical trial"^^xsd:string)
ClassAssertion(OpenPVSignal:Clinical_trial_information X2015_m_linagliptin_cardiac_failure_1st_2015:AlogliptinClinicalTrial)
ObjectPropertyAssertion(OpenPVSignal:refers_to_adverse_effect X2015_m_linagliptin_cardiac_failure_1st_2015:AlogliptinClinicalTrial X2015_m_linagliptin_cardiac_failure_1st_2015:heartFailure)
ObjectPropertyAssertion(OpenPVSignal:refers_to_drug X2015_m_linagliptin_cardiac_failure_1st_2015:AlogliptinClinicalTrial X2015_m_linagliptin_cardiac_failure_1st_2015:alogliptin)
ObjectPropertyAssertion(mp:references X2015_m_linagliptin_cardiac_failure_1st_2015:AlogliptinClinicalTrial X2015_m_linagliptin_cardiac_failure_1st_2015:Ref.25)
ObjectPropertyAssertion(mp:references X2015_m_linagliptin_cardiac_failure_1st_2015:AlogliptinClinicalTrial X2015_m_linagliptin_cardiac_failure_1st_2015:Ref.26)
DataPropertyAssertion(OpenPVSignal:has_content X2015_m_linagliptin_cardiac_failure_1st_2015:AlogliptinClinicalTrial "In a large trial assessing the effect of alogliptin on cardiovascular outcomes in 5,380 patients followed for a median of 18 months, 28% of the participants had HF at baseline; HF was not part of the primary composite outcome or secondary outcomes. Although the heterogeneity of sub-groups is mentioned, no specific details are provided.25 Prior HF was the strongest predictor of hospitalization during the study, followed by impaired kidney function. In the EXAMINE study, the risk increase for hospitalization due to HF associated with alogliptin was apparently less clear in spite of the percentage of patients with prior HF, the higher use of ß-blocking agents, and the more frequent medical controls with treatment adaptations in EXAMINE might be one of the potential explanations.26"^^xsd:string)

# Individual: X2015_m_linagliptin_cardiac_failure_1st_2015:Cardiac_failure_background (Cardiac failure background)

AnnotationAssertion(rdfs:label X2015_m_linagliptin_cardiac_failure_1st_2015:Cardiac_failure_background "Cardiac failure background"^^xsd:string)
ClassAssertion(OpenPVSignal:Free_text_reporting_element X2015_m_linagliptin_cardiac_failure_1st_2015:Cardiac_failure_background)
ObjectPropertyAssertion(OpenPVSignal:refers_to_adverse_effect X2015_m_linagliptin_cardiac_failure_1st_2015:Cardiac_failure_background X2015_m_linagliptin_cardiac_failure_1st_2015:cardiacFailureComplication)
ObjectPropertyAssertion(mp:references X2015_m_linagliptin_cardiac_failure_1st_2015:Cardiac_failure_background X2015_m_linagliptin_cardiac_failure_1st_2015:Ref.4)
ObjectPropertyAssertion(mp:references X2015_m_linagliptin_cardiac_failure_1st_2015:Cardiac_failure_background X2015_m_linagliptin_cardiac_failure_1st_2015:Ref.5)
DataPropertyAssertion(OpenPVSignal:has_content X2015_m_linagliptin_cardiac_failure_1st_2015:Cardiac_failure_background "Cardiac failure, or heart failure (HF), is a pathophysiologically complex clinical syndrome, not fully understood, which results from an impaired function of the heart as a pump supporting physiological circulation. Symptoms are dyspnoea, exercise intolerance, and sodium and water retention, often manifested as oedema. Cardiac failure can be caused by any abnormality of the structure, mechanical function or electrical activity of the heart, or as a secondary dysfunction of other organs and tissues, e.g. kidneys, liver or muscles; other systemic processes, as neurohumoral activation, are also involved.4,5"^^xsd:string)

# Individual: X2015_m_linagliptin_cardiac_failure_1st_2015:Case12 (case info 12)

AnnotationAssertion(rdfs:label X2015_m_linagliptin_cardiac_failure_1st_2015:Case12 "case info 12"^^xsd:string)
ClassAssertion(OpenPVSignal:Case_Report_Information X2015_m_linagliptin_cardiac_failure_1st_2015:Case12)
DataPropertyAssertion(OpenPVSignal:has_content X2015_m_linagliptin_cardiac_failure_1st_2015:Case12 "In case 12, an 88 year-old woman who had started linagliptin 45 days earlier, went to a hospital for routine pacemaker battery replacement, and cardiac insufficiency was detected; the patient lost 13 kg with appropriate therapy (this indicates the amount of fluid retention), and her ejection fraction was 45%."^^xsd:string)
DataPropertyAssertion(OpenPVSignal:has_content X2015_m_linagliptin_cardiac_failure_1st_2015:Case12 "case 12 mentions hypertension and atrial fibrillation"^^xsd:string)

# Individual: X2015_m_linagliptin_cardiac_failure_1st_2015:Case13 (case info 13)

AnnotationAssertion(rdfs:label X2015_m_linagliptin_cardiac_failure_1st_2015:Case13 "case info 13"^^xsd:string)
ClassAssertion(OpenPVSignal:Case_Report_Information X2015_m_linagliptin_cardiac_failure_1st_2015:Case13)
DataPropertyAssertion(OpenPVSignal:has_content X2015_m_linagliptin_cardiac_failure_1st_2015:Case13 "Case 13 reports that an 83 year-old man with renal insufficiency and hypertension presented with cardiac failure. Linagliptin was withdrawn, but there is no information about the outcome.
Concomitant poly-medication is mentioned but details are not provided."^^xsd:string)
DataPropertyAssertion(OpenPVSignal:has_content X2015_m_linagliptin_cardiac_failure_1st_2015:Case13 "case 13 renal insufficiency and hypertension"^^xsd:string)

# Individual: X2015_m_linagliptin_cardiac_failure_1st_2015:Case14 (case info 14)

AnnotationAssertion(rdfs:label X2015_m_linagliptin_cardiac_failure_1st_2015:Case14 "case info 14"^^xsd:string)
ClassAssertion(OpenPVSignal:Case_Report_Information X2015_m_linagliptin_cardiac_failure_1st_2015:Case14)
DataPropertyAssertion(OpenPVSignal:has_content X2015_m_linagliptin_cardiac_failure_1st_2015:Case14 "The case from literature (case 14) was extracted from a 52 weeks multifactorial design study, and reports two drug related serious adverse events (SAEs) in the same patient on day 295 after starting the study treatment (2.5 mg linagliptin + 1000 mg metformin). The patient experienced cardiogenic shock and supraventricular tachycardia within one hour of administration of medication. The patient required hospitalisation and study medication was discontinued; the patient recovered.12"^^xsd:string)

# Individual: X2015_m_linagliptin_cardiac_failure_1st_2015:CaseInfo1 (Case info 1)

AnnotationAssertion(rdfs:label X2015_m_linagliptin_cardiac_failure_1st_2015:CaseInfo1 "Case info 1"^^xsd:string)
ClassAssertion(OpenPVSignal:Case_Report_Information X2015_m_linagliptin_cardiac_failure_1st_2015:CaseInfo1)
DataPropertyAssertion(OpenPVSignal:has_content X2015_m_linagliptin_cardiac_failure_1st_2015:CaseInfo1 "The first spontaneous reporting (case 1) referred to a woman presenting with cardiac failure 44 days after having started her treatment with linagliptin 5 mg. All the other adverse events (urinary infection, pulmonary infection) occurred at least 11 days after the HF onset, and were probably related to complications derived from hospitalization. Linagliptin was withdrawn after the patient had recovered from her cardiac failure, and hypothetically, after hospitalization."^^xsd:string)

