ObjectPropertyAssertion(mp:references X2015_m_linagliptin_cardiac_failure_1st_2015:DetailedMechanismOfDPP4InhibitionAndCardiacFailure X2015_m_linagliptin_cardiac_failure_1st_2015:Ref.29)
ObjectPropertyAssertion(mp:references X2015_m_linagliptin_cardiac_failure_1st_2015:DetailedMechanismOfDPP4InhibitionAndCardiacFailure X2015_m_linagliptin_cardiac_failure_1st_2015:Ref.6)
ObjectPropertyAssertion(mp:references X2015_m_linagliptin_cardiac_failure_1st_2015:DetailedMechanismOfDPP4InhibitionAndCardiacFailure X2015_m_linagliptin_cardiac_failure_1st_2015:Ref.7)
ObjectPropertyAssertion(mp:references X2015_m_linagliptin_cardiac_failure_1st_2015:DetailedMechanismOfDPP4InhibitionAndCardiacFailure X2015_m_linagliptin_cardiac_failure_1st_2015:Ref.9)
DataPropertyAssertion(OpenPVSignal:has_content X2015_m_linagliptin_cardiac_failure_1st_2015:DetailedMechanismOfDPP4InhibitionAndCardiacFailure "Mechanisms of the hypothesized effect of DDP4 inhibitors on HF are unknown. As previously mentioned, DPP4 cleaves not only GLP-1 and GIP, but also other cardioactive peptides, such as substance P, brain natriuretic peptide (BNP), neuropeptide Y, CXCL12, bradykinin, and related peptides.6-7 BNP is increased in HF, being both a diagnostic and prognostic marker.9,10 It has also been suggested that DPP4 is abnormally increased in patients with T2DM and these increased DPP4 levels are independently associated with asymptomatic left ventricular both diastolic and systolic dysfunction in T2DM patients which have a higher risk of presenting left ventricular dysfunction.27 Neuropeptide Y (NPY1-36) is released from sympathetic neurons; DPP4 removes the N-terminal from NPY1-36 to generate NPY3-36, which binds to Y2 receptors that have relative antagonist properties to Y1 receptor activation. Any decrease in the DPP4 mediated generation of NPY3-36 would decrease the activity of Y2 inhibitory autoreceptors; and so augment sympathetic and parasympathetic neurotransmitter release.28 A clinical study in 53 patients found that peptide Y is augmented in diabetic patients.29"^^xsd:string)

