# Individual: X2015_m_linagliptin_cardiac_failure_1st_2015:Mechanism_of_cilostazol (Mechanism of cilostazol)

AnnotationAssertion(rdfs:label X2015_m_linagliptin_cardiac_failure_1st_2015:Mechanism_of_cilostazol "Mechanism of cilostazol"^^xsd:string)
ClassAssertion(OpenPVSignal:Mechanism X2015_m_linagliptin_cardiac_failure_1st_2015:Mechanism_of_cilostazol)
DataPropertyAssertion(OpenPVSignal:has_content X2015_m_linagliptin_cardiac_failure_1st_2015:Mechanism_of_cilostazol "Cilostazol is a reversible phosphodiesterase III inhibitor with anti-platelet, vasodilatory and antithrombotic properties, metabolized by CYP3A4 and CYP2C19. Cilostazol is formally contraindicated in patients with pre-existing HF. Nifedipine is metabolized by CYP2C19 (interaction described in product information)."^^xsd:string)

# Individual: X2015_m_linagliptin_cardiac_failure_1st_2015:Mechanism_of_pioglitazone (Mechanism of pioglitazone)

