# Individual: X2015_m_linagliptin_cardiac_failure_1st_2015:data_favouring_beneficial_effects_on_cardiac_outcomes (data favouring beneficial effects on cardiac outcomes)

AnnotationAssertion(rdfs:label X2015_m_linagliptin_cardiac_failure_1st_2015:data_favouring_beneficial_effects_on_cardiac_outcomes "data favouring beneficial effects on cardiac outcomes"^^xsd:string)
ClassAssertion(obo:OAE_0001182 X2015_m_linagliptin_cardiac_failure_1st_2015:data_favouring_beneficial_effects_on_cardiac_outcomes)
ObjectPropertyAssertion(OpenPVSignal:refers_to_class X2015_m_linagliptin_cardiac_failure_1st_2015:data_favouring_beneficial_effects_on_cardiac_outcomes X2015_m_linagliptin_cardiac_failure_1st_2015:DDP4_inhibitors)
ObjectPropertyAssertion(mp:references X2015_m_linagliptin_cardiac_failure_1st_2015:data_favouring_beneficial_effects_on_cardiac_outcomes X2015_m_linagliptin_cardiac_failure_1st_2015:Ref.22)
ObjectPropertyAssertion(mp:references X2015_m_linagliptin_cardiac_failure_1st_2015:data_favouring_beneficial_effects_on_cardiac_outcomes X2015_m_linagliptin_cardiac_failure_1st_2015:Ref.23)
DataPropertyAssertion(OpenPVSignal:has_content X2015_m_linagliptin_cardiac_failure_1st_2015:data_favouring_beneficial_effects_on_cardiac_outcomes "DDP4 inhibitors have been expected to have beneficial effects on cardiac outcomes, both due to GLP-1 actions and to other peptide hormones with direct cardiorenal effects. Preclinical data and mechanistic studies suggested a possible additional non-glycaemic beneficial action on blood vessels and the heart, via both GLP-1 dependent and GLP-1-independent effects.22 It has been suggested that DPP4 inhibitors reduce the risk for the multiple co-morbidities associated with obesity/T2DM including hypertension, cardiovascular and kidney disease.23"^^xsd:string)

