# Individual: X2015_m_Prucalopride__3rd_2015:ReceptorOfCisapridePharmacologicalFunction (Receptor of cisapride pharmacological function)

AnnotationAssertion(rdfs:label X2015_m_Prucalopride__3rd_2015:ReceptorOfCisapridePharmacologicalFunction "Receptor of cisapride pharmacological function"^^xsd:string)
ClassAssertion(OpenPVSignal:Adverse_Effect_Mechanism X2015_m_Prucalopride__3rd_2015:ReceptorOfCisapridePharmacologicalFunction)
ObjectPropertyAssertion(OpenPVSignal:refers_to_adverse_effect X2015_m_Prucalopride__3rd_2015:ReceptorOfCisapridePharmacologicalFunction X2015_m_Prucalopride__3rd_2015:qtProlongation)
ObjectPropertyAssertion(mp:references X2015_m_Prucalopride__3rd_2015:ReceptorOfCisapridePharmacologicalFunction X2015_m_Prucalopride__3rd_2015:Ref.5)
ObjectPropertyAssertion(mp:references X2015_m_Prucalopride__3rd_2015:ReceptorOfCisapridePharmacologicalFunction X2015_m_Prucalopride__3rd_2015:Ref.6)
ObjectPropertyAssertion(mp:references X2015_m_Prucalopride__3rd_2015:ReceptorOfCisapridePharmacologicalFunction X2015_m_Prucalopride__3rd_2015:Ref.7)
DataPropertyAssertion(OpenPVSignal:has_content X2015_m_Prucalopride__3rd_2015:ReceptorOfCisapridePharmacologicalFunction "The highly selective nature of prucalopride for the 5-HT4 receptor represents an advantage over previous prokinetic non-selective 5-HT4 agonists, such as cisapride and tegaserod. Both of these agents have appreciable affinity for other receptors, channels or transporters [e.g. cisapride: human ether-a-go-go-related gene (hERG)/K+ channel and tegaserod: 5-HT1D and 5-HT2B receptors] which resulted in adverse event profiles (QT prolongation and cardiovascular ischemic events, respectively) which limited their clinical success.5-7"^^xsd:string)

# Individual: X2015_m_Prucalopride__3rd_2015:ReceptorOfTegaserodPharmacologicalFunction (Receptor of tegaserod pharmacological function)

AnnotationAssertion(rdfs:label X2015_m_Prucalopride__3rd_2015:ReceptorOfTegaserodPharmacologicalFunction "Receptor of tegaserod pharmacological function"^^xsd:string)
ClassAssertion(OpenPVSignal:Adverse_Effect_Mechanism X2015_m_Prucalopride__3rd_2015:ReceptorOfTegaserodPharmacologicalFunction)
ObjectPropertyAssertion(OpenPVSignal:refers_to_adverse_effect X2015_m_Prucalopride__3rd_2015:ReceptorOfTegaserodPharmacologicalFunction X2015_m_Prucalopride__3rd_2015:cardiovascularIschemicEvents)
ObjectPropertyAssertion(mp:references X2015_m_Prucalopride__3rd_2015:ReceptorOfTegaserodPharmacologicalFunction X2015_m_Prucalopride__3rd_2015:Ref.5)
ObjectPropertyAssertion(mp:references X2015_m_Prucalopride__3rd_2015:ReceptorOfTegaserodPharmacologicalFunction X2015_m_Prucalopride__3rd_2015:Ref.6)
ObjectPropertyAssertion(mp:references X2015_m_Prucalopride__3rd_2015:ReceptorOfTegaserodPharmacologicalFunction X2015_m_Prucalopride__3rd_2015:Ref.7)
DataPropertyAssertion(OpenPVSignal:has_content X2015_m_Prucalopride__3rd_2015:ReceptorOfTegaserodPharmacologicalFunction "The highly selective nature of prucalopride for the 5-HT4 receptor represents an advantage over previous prokinetic non-selective 5-HT4 agonists, such as cisapride and tegaserod. Both of these agents have appreciable affinity for other receptors, channels or transporters [e.g. cisapride: human ether-a-go-go-related gene (hERG)/K+ channel and tegaserod: 5-HT1D and 5-HT2B receptors] which resulted in adverse event profiles (QT prolongation and cardiovascular ischemic events, respectively) which limited their clinical success.5-7"^^xsd:string)

