# Individual: X2015_m_Prucalopride__3rd_2015:fdf (Suicidal ideation pathophysiology)

AnnotationAssertion(rdfs:label X2015_m_Prucalopride__3rd_2015:fdf "Suicidal ideation pathophysiology"^^xsd:string)
ClassAssertion(OpenPVSignal:Free_text_reporting_element X2015_m_Prucalopride__3rd_2015:fdf)
ObjectPropertyAssertion(OpenPVSignal:refers_to_adverse_effect X2015_m_Prucalopride__3rd_2015:fdf X2015_m_Prucalopride__3rd_2015:suicidalIdeation)
ObjectPropertyAssertion(mp:references X2015_m_Prucalopride__3rd_2015:fdf X2015_m_Prucalopride__3rd_2015:Ref.10)
ObjectPropertyAssertion(mp:references X2015_m_Prucalopride__3rd_2015:fdf X2015_m_Prucalopride__3rd_2015:Ref.11)
ObjectPropertyAssertion(mp:references X2015_m_Prucalopride__3rd_2015:fdf X2015_m_Prucalopride__3rd_2015:Ref.12)
ObjectPropertyAssertion(mp:references X2015_m_Prucalopride__3rd_2015:fdf X2015_m_Prucalopride__3rd_2015:Ref.13)
DataPropertyAssertion(OpenPVSignal:has_content X2015_m_Prucalopride__3rd_2015:fdf "Suicidal ideation is defined as thoughts about self- harm, with deliberate consideration or planning of possible techniques of causing one’s own death.10 Suicidal ideation is more common than suicide attempts or completed suicide.11 A 1995 study found that 3.3 percent of patients in an urban primary care outpatient clinic reported suicidal ideation.12 Risk factors for suicidal behaviours include female gender, younger age, fewer years of education, unmarried status and the presence of a mental disorder, with psychiatric comorbidity significantly increasing risk.13 In addition, some prescription drugs, such as selective serotonin re- uptake inhibitors, can have suicidal ideation as a side effect."^^xsd:string)

