DataPropertyAssertion(OpenPVSignal:has_content X2015_m_atomoxetine_and_pediatric_patients_4rth_2015:d "There were other drugs also suspected in the remaining 10 cases and they included drugs for treatment of psychotic disorders in seven cases, drugs for treatment of depression (3 cases), epilepsy (3 cases) and ADHD (3 cases). In seven of these 10 cases, at least one of these drugs (olanzapine, ziprasidone, risperidone, chlorpromazine) is a likely cause. Antipsychotic drugs are a well-known cause of dystonia and the four drugs listed above all refer to dystonia as a possible adverse effect in their product information.3"^^xsd:string)

