DataPropertyAssertion(OpenPVSignal:has_content X2015_m_vemurafenib_tls_4th:Mechanism_of_Vemurafenib "Vemurafenib is a B-Raf enzyme inhibitor indicated for the treatment of malignant melanoma.1 Vemurafenib causes programmed cell death and works in about 60% of melanoma patients whose cancer has either a V600E BRAF mutation or the more rare BRAF V600K mutation. Melanoma cells without these mutations are not inhibited by vemurafenib; instead the drug paradoxically stimulates normal BRAF and may promote tumour growth in such cases"^^xsd:string)

