# Individual: X2015_m_vemurafenib_tls_4th:Report1 (Info for Report 1)

AnnotationAssertion(rdfs:label X2015_m_vemurafenib_tls_4th:Report1 "Info for Report 1"^^xsd:string)
ClassAssertion(OpenPVSignal:Case_Report_Information X2015_m_vemurafenib_tls_4th:Report1)
DataPropertyAssertion(OpenPVSignal:has_content X2015_m_vemurafenib_tls_4th:Report1 "A 24-year-old male study patient was treated for malignant melanoma with vemurafenib at a dose of 960 mg twice daily. Dates of treatment and onset of symptoms, medical history or concurrent illness, and concomitant or past medication were not recorded. The patient was admitted to hospital with severe worsening of general condition, abdominal complaints, flank pain, nausea, vomiting and proteinuria and was diagnosed with TLS. The therapy, outcome and any causality assessment by the reporter was not provided. The marketing authorisation holder (MAH) assessed the TLS as related to vemurafenib. "^^xsd:string)

# Individual: X2015_m_vemurafenib_tls_4th:Report2 (Info for Report 2)

AnnotationAssertion(rdfs:label X2015_m_vemurafenib_tls_4th:Report2 "Info for Report 2"^^xsd:string)
ClassAssertion(OpenPVSignal:Case_Report_Information X2015_m_vemurafenib_tls_4th:Report2)
DataPropertyAssertion(OpenPVSignal:has_content X2015_m_vemurafenib_tls_4th:Report2 "A 58-year-old female patient was treated for malignant melanoma with vemurafenib in a dose of 960 mg twice daily. Concomitant medications were enoxaparin, metoclopramide, betamethasone, orlistat, levothyroxine, omeprazole, and paracetamol. The diagnosis of TLS was reported after five days of vemurafenib treatment. The patient recovered within three weeks."^^xsd:string)

# Individual: X2015_m_vemurafenib_tls_4th:Report3 (Info for Report 3)

AnnotationAssertion(rdfs:label X2015_m_vemurafenib_tls_4th:Report3 "Info for Report 3"^^xsd:string)
ClassAssertion(OpenPVSignal:Case_Report_Information X2015_m_vemurafenib_tls_4th:Report3)
DataPropertyAssertion(OpenPVSignal:has_content X2015_m_vemurafenib_tls_4th:Report3 "A patient of unknown gender and age was treated for malignant melanoma with vemurafenib with an unknown dose. The patient’s medical history, concomitant medication, concurrent conditions and past drugs were not reported. After an unspecified amount of time the patient died due to TLS; in the opinion of the reporter this was related to the treatment with vemurafenib. The patient was enrolled in a healthcare providers’ programme for malignant melanoma. The narrative indicated that this case actually described two different patients experiencing the event as described above. "^^xsd:string)

# Individual: X2015_m_vemurafenib_tls_4th:Report4 (Info for Report 4)

AnnotationAssertion(rdfs:label X2015_m_vemurafenib_tls_4th:Report4 "Info for Report 4"^^xsd:string)
ClassAssertion(OpenPVSignal:Case_Report_Information X2015_m_vemurafenib_tls_4th:Report4)
DataPropertyAssertion(OpenPVSignal:has_content X2015_m_vemurafenib_tls_4th:Report4 "A male patient was reported to have experienced TLS while receiving treatment with vemurafenib. No further relevant information was provided. "^^xsd:string)

