# Individual: X2015_m_dextromethorphan_2015_5th:Conclusion_content (Discussion and Conclusion content)

AnnotationAssertion(rdfs:label X2015_m_dextromethorphan_2015_5th:Conclusion_content "Discussion and Conclusion content"^^xsd:string)
ClassAssertion(OpenPVSignal:Conclusion X2015_m_dextromethorphan_2015_5th:Conclusion_content)
ClassAssertion(OpenPVSignal:Discussion X2015_m_dextromethorphan_2015_5th:Conclusion_content)
DataPropertyAssertion(OpenPVSignal:has_content X2015_m_dextromethorphan_2015_5th:Conclusion_content "Nonetheless, reports on dextromethorphan associated with serious ADRs within the SOC Neurological disorders for children below the age of 6 have continued to be reported to VigiBase® after 2009 (the latest submitted in 2014). The majority of these reports are not co-reported with accidental intake of the drug or overdose. Continuous reporting of serious neurological ADRs associated with off-label use of dextromethorphan in young children suggests that the risk-benefit balance for dextromethorphan is not clear to parents. Further revisions of the patient information leaflets are advised to clearly highlight the risk of serious neurological reactions in young children."^^xsd:string)

