ObjectPropertyAssertion(mp:references X2015_m_dextromethorphan_2015_5th:Literature_and_labelling X2015_m_dextromethorphan_2015_5th:Ref.1)
ObjectPropertyAssertion(mp:references X2015_m_dextromethorphan_2015_5th:Literature_and_labelling X2015_m_dextromethorphan_2015_5th:Ref.3)
DataPropertyAssertion(OpenPVSignal:has_content X2015_m_dextromethorphan_2015_5th:Literature_and_labelling "In the summary of product characteristics (SmPC) for several products containing multiple ingredients including dextromethorphan, coma is listed in the section for overdoses but for drugs containing only dextromethorphan in the United Kingdom, coma is not listed as a possible ADR other than as a contraindication in patients using MAO-inhibitors.1 In 2008/2009 the MHRA and the CHM in the United Kingdom advised that children under 6 years should not be given over-the-counter cough and cold medicines containing dextromethorphan.3"^^xsd:string)

