# Individual: X2015_m_dextromethorphan_2015_5th:introduction (introduction)

AnnotationAssertion(rdfs:label X2015_m_dextromethorphan_2015_5th:introduction "introduction"^^xsd:string)
ClassAssertion(OpenPVSignal:Introduction X2015_m_dextromethorphan_2015_5th:introduction)
ObjectPropertyAssertion(mp:references X2015_m_dextromethorphan_2015_5th:introduction X2015_m_dextromethorphan_2015_5th:Ref.1)
ObjectPropertyAssertion(mp:references X2015_m_dextromethorphan_2015_5th:introduction X2015_m_dextromethorphan_2015_5th:Ref.2)
DataPropertyAssertion(OpenPVSignal:has_content X2015_m_dextromethorphan_2015_5th:introduction "In the screening of paediatric individual case safety reports (ICSRs) from the WHO Global ICSR database, VigiBase® the adverse drug reaction (ADR) ataxia was highlighted for the drug dextromethorphan. The substance is used in many cough, cold and flu products sold over the counter globally.  It is approved for children and adults above 6 years of age in the United Kingdom and above 4 years of age in the United States.1,2 Most dextromethorphan containing products in the United Kingdom are however indicated from the age of 12.1"^^xsd:string)

