# Individual: X2015_m_temozolomide_oesophagitis_5th:PossiblePharmacologicalPlausabilityForTemozolomideAndOesophagitis (Possible pharmacological plausability for temozolomide and oesophagitis)

AnnotationAssertion(rdfs:label X2015_m_temozolomide_oesophagitis_5th:PossiblePharmacologicalPlausabilityForTemozolomideAndOesophagitis "Possible pharmacological plausability for temozolomide and oesophagitis"^^xsd:string)
ClassAssertion(OpenPVSignal:Adverse_Effect_Mechanism X2015_m_temozolomide_oesophagitis_5th:PossiblePharmacologicalPlausabilityForTemozolomideAndOesophagitis)
ObjectPropertyAssertion(OpenPVSignal:refers_to_adverse_effect X2015_m_temozolomide_oesophagitis_5th:PossiblePharmacologicalPlausabilityForTemozolomideAndOesophagitis X2015_m_temozolomide_oesophagitis_5th:enteritis)
ObjectPropertyAssertion(OpenPVSignal:refers_to_adverse_effect X2015_m_temozolomide_oesophagitis_5th:PossiblePharmacologicalPlausabilityForTemozolomideAndOesophagitis X2015_m_temozolomide_oesophagitis_5th:gastritis)
ObjectPropertyAssertion(OpenPVSignal:refers_to_adverse_effect X2015_m_temozolomide_oesophagitis_5th:PossiblePharmacologicalPlausabilityForTemozolomideAndOesophagitis X2015_m_temozolomide_oesophagitis_5th:oesophagitis)
ObjectPropertyAssertion(OpenPVSignal:refers_to_adverse_effect X2015_m_temozolomide_oesophagitis_5th:PossiblePharmacologicalPlausabilityForTemozolomideAndOesophagitis X2015_m_temozolomide_oesophagitis_5th:stomatitis)
DataPropertyAssertion(OpenPVSignal:has_content X2015_m_temozolomide_oesophagitis_5th:PossiblePharmacologicalPlausabilityForTemozolomideAndOesophagitis "Many anticancer drugs are able to interfere with the cellular cycle, and in this manner interrupt the cellular growth; this is particularly evident in rapidly growing tissues. For these drugs, stomatitis, oesophagitis, gastritis and enteritis would be a continuum depending on the route, dose and time of exposure. With this in mind, it would be expected for similar adverse reactions to occur. In fact, stomatitis, dysphagia and gastroenteritis are already labelled for temozolomide. Oesophagitis is therefore a possible reaction in connection with temozolomide.  "^^xsd:string)

