# Individual: X2015_m_atomoxetine_and_neutropenia_6th:IntroductionContent (Introduction content)

AnnotationAssertion(rdfs:label X2015_m_atomoxetine_and_neutropenia_6th:IntroductionContent "Introduction content"^^xsd:string)
ClassAssertion(OpenPVSignal:Introduction X2015_m_atomoxetine_and_neutropenia_6th:IntroductionContent)
ObjectPropertyAssertion(mp:references X2015_m_atomoxetine_and_neutropenia_6th:IntroductionContent X2015_m_atomoxetine_and_neutropenia_6th:Ref.1)
ObjectPropertyAssertion(mp:references X2015_m_atomoxetine_and_neutropenia_6th:IntroductionContent X2015_m_atomoxetine_and_neutropenia_6th:Ref.2)
DataPropertyAssertion(OpenPVSignal:has_content X2015_m_atomoxetine_and_neutropenia_6th:IntroductionContent "Atomoxetine is a relatively potent inhibitor of the presynaptic noradrenaline transporter, a moderate inhibitor of 5HT uptake, and a weak inhibitor of dopamine uptake with minimal affinity for the other noradrenergic receptors. Atomoxetine has moderate affinity for 5HT2 and GABAA receptors but poor affinity for most other receptors. It is indicated for the treatment of attention deficit hyperactivity disorder (ADHD) as defined by DSMIV criteria in children 6 years of age and older, adolescents and adults. The most frequent adverse reactions reported during clinical trials of atomoxetine in children and adolescents including gastrointestinal reactions, increased blood pressure and heart rate, decreased appetite, decreased weight and skin reactions. The product information does not refer to blood disorders.1 Neutropenia is a high level term in WHO-ART with preferred terms consisting of neutropenia, granulocytopoenia and leukopenia. The preferred term, neutropenia, which is the subject of this signal, is defined as a decrease to less than 1.5 x 109/L of segmented polymorphonuclear and band cells. Neutropenia is considered as ‘‘severe’’ below 0.5 x 109/L.2 "^^xsd:string)

# Individual: X2015_m_atomoxetine_and_neutropenia_6th:LabellingInformation (Product literature for atomoxetine)

AnnotationAssertion(rdfs:label X2015_m_atomoxetine_and_neutropenia_6th:LabellingInformation "Product literature for atomoxetine"^^xsd:string)
ClassAssertion(obo:OAE_0001125 X2015_m_atomoxetine_and_neutropenia_6th:LabellingInformation)
ObjectPropertyAssertion(OpenPVSignal:refers_to_drug X2015_m_atomoxetine_and_neutropenia_6th:LabellingInformation X2015_m_atomoxetine_and_neutropenia_6th:atomoxetine)
ObjectPropertyAssertion(mp:references X2015_m_atomoxetine_and_neutropenia_6th:LabellingInformation X2015_m_atomoxetine_and_neutropenia_6th:Ref.1)
DataPropertyAssertion(OpenPVSignal:has_content X2015_m_atomoxetine_and_neutropenia_6th:LabellingInformation " The product literature does not refer to neutropenia nor does it mention other blood disorders.1 No reports of neutropenia in association with atomoxetine could be found in the literature.  "^^xsd:string)

