# Individual: X2015_m_Desloratadine_and_aggressive_reaction_6th:PossibleMechanismOfAggression (Possible mechanism of aggression)

AnnotationAssertion(rdfs:label X2015_m_Desloratadine_and_aggressive_reaction_6th:PossibleMechanismOfAggression "Possible mechanism of aggression"^^xsd:string)
ClassAssertion(OpenPVSignal:Adverse_Effect_Mechanism X2015_m_Desloratadine_and_aggressive_reaction_6th:PossibleMechanismOfAggression)
ObjectPropertyAssertion(OpenPVSignal:refers_to_adverse_effect X2015_m_Desloratadine_and_aggressive_reaction_6th:PossibleMechanismOfAggression X2015_m_Desloratadine_and_aggressive_reaction_6th:aggression)
ObjectPropertyAssertion(mp:references X2015_m_Desloratadine_and_aggressive_reaction_6th:PossibleMechanismOfAggression X2015_m_Desloratadine_and_aggressive_reaction_6th:Ref.8)
DataPropertyAssertion(OpenPVSignal:has_content X2015_m_Desloratadine_and_aggressive_reaction_6th:PossibleMechanismOfAggression "The nature of aggressive behaviour is complex and involves genetic and environmental factors, different neural circuits, and several neurotransmitters, including serotonin (5-HT), dopamine, and GABA.8  "^^xsd:string)

# Individual: X2015_m_Desloratadine_and_aggressive_reaction_6th:PossibleMechanismOfAggressionDueToDesloratadine (Possible mechanism of aggression due to desloratadine)

AnnotationAssertion(rdfs:label X2015_m_Desloratadine_and_aggressive_reaction_6th:PossibleMechanismOfAggressionDueToDesloratadine "Possible mechanism of aggression due to desloratadine"^^xsd:string)
ClassAssertion(OpenPVSignal:Adverse_Effect_Mechanism X2015_m_Desloratadine_and_aggressive_reaction_6th:PossibleMechanismOfAggressionDueToDesloratadine)
ObjectPropertyAssertion(OpenPVSignal:refers_to_adverse_effect X2015_m_Desloratadine_and_aggressive_reaction_6th:PossibleMechanismOfAggressionDueToDesloratadine X2015_m_Desloratadine_and_aggressive_reaction_6th:aggression)
DataPropertyAssertion(OpenPVSignal:has_content X2015_m_Desloratadine_and_aggressive_reaction_6th:PossibleMechanismOfAggressionDueToDesloratadine "The neurobiology of aggression is complex and is supposed to involve many different neural circuits and neurotransmitters and a mechanism can only be speculated. However, penetration into the brain and the possibility of triggering clinically relevant CNS adverse effects in susceptible patients, cannot be ruled out"^^xsd:string)

