# Individual: X2016_m_vemurafenib_and_atrial_fibrillation_1st_2016:Cardiovascular_side_effects_of_TKIs (Cardiovascular side effects of TKIs)

AnnotationAssertion(rdfs:label X2016_m_vemurafenib_and_atrial_fibrillation_1st_2016:Cardiovascular_side_effects_of_TKIs "Cardiovascular side effects of TKIs"^^xsd:string)
ClassAssertion(OpenPVSignal:Literature_information X2016_m_vemurafenib_and_atrial_fibrillation_1st_2016:Cardiovascular_side_effects_of_TKIs)
ObjectPropertyAssertion(mp:references X2016_m_vemurafenib_and_atrial_fibrillation_1st_2016:Cardiovascular_side_effects_of_TKIs X2016_m_vemurafenib_and_atrial_fibrillation_1st_2016:Ref.6)
DataPropertyAssertion(OpenPVSignal:has_content X2016_m_vemurafenib_and_atrial_fibrillation_1st_2016:Cardiovascular_side_effects_of_TKIs ". In a review of cardiac adverse effects of tyrosine kinase inhibitors (TKIs) the authors state that the type of cardiovascular side effect differs between TKIs based on which cellular signalling pathways they inhibit.6 They divided the agents into two clinical groups: (i) the VSP (VEGF signalling pathway) inhibitors and (ii)the non-VSP inhibitor agents (which include vemurafenib). They went on to state that VSP inhibitors are typically associated with hypertension, cardiomyopathy and arterial ischemia. Non-VSP inhibitors are more commonly associated with QT prolongation, arrhythmia, fluid retention and rarely cardiomyopathy. However, only vemurafenib was linked with atrial fibrillation in a table of reported cardiac adverse effects associated with TK inhibitors. The incidence was reported as 5% but without a reference or discussion."^^xsd:string)

# Individual: X2016_m_vemurafenib_and_atrial_fibrillation_1st_2016:CaseInformationForReport1 (Case information for report 1)

AnnotationAssertion(rdfs:label X2016_m_vemurafenib_and_atrial_fibrillation_1st_2016:CaseInformationForReport1 "Case information for report 1"^^xsd:string)
ClassAssertion(OpenPVSignal:Case_Report_Information X2016_m_vemurafenib_and_atrial_fibrillation_1st_2016:CaseInformationForReport1)
DataPropertyAssertion(OpenPVSignal:has_content X2016_m_vemurafenib_and_atrial_fibrillation_1st_2016:CaseInformationForReport1 "In case 1, after developing atrial fibrillation, the patient was treated with antithrombotic but not anti-arrhythmic agents so that the treatment is not an explanation for recovery."^^xsd:string)

# Individual: X2016_m_vemurafenib_and_atrial_fibrillation_1st_2016:CaseInformationForReport2 (Case information for report 2)

AnnotationAssertion(rdfs:label X2016_m_vemurafenib_and_atrial_fibrillation_1st_2016:CaseInformationForReport2 "Case information for report 2"^^xsd:string)
ClassAssertion(OpenPVSignal:Case_Report_Information X2016_m_vemurafenib_and_atrial_fibrillation_1st_2016:CaseInformationForReport2)
DataPropertyAssertion(OpenPVSignal:has_content X2016_m_vemurafenib_and_atrial_fibrillation_1st_2016:CaseInformationForReport2 "“Ambulatory treatment” given, the atrial fibrillation did not recur. Indication for enoxaparin was “prophylaxis”"^^xsd:string)

# Individual: X2016_m_vemurafenib_and_atrial_fibrillation_1st_2016:CaseInformationForReport3 (Case information for report 3)

