# Individual: X2016_m_vemurafenib_and_atrial_fibrillation_1st_2016:concomitant_drugs (possible pre existing atrial fibrillation)

AnnotationAssertion(rdfs:label X2016_m_vemurafenib_and_atrial_fibrillation_1st_2016:concomitant_drugs "possible pre existing atrial fibrillation"^^xsd:string)
ClassAssertion(obo:OAE_0001182 X2016_m_vemurafenib_and_atrial_fibrillation_1st_2016:concomitant_drugs)
DataPropertyAssertion(OpenPVSignal:has_content X2016_m_vemurafenib_and_atrial_fibrillation_1st_2016:concomitant_drugs "Eight patients were taking medicines indicative of hypertension, angina, arrhythmia or cardiac failure (diuretics, digoxin, ACE inhibitors, angiotensin II receptor blockers, beta-blockers, calcium channel blockers). Three of these patients and one other patient were taking a statin. One was taking warfarin and a beta-adrenergic blocking agent suggesting that they might have pre-existing atrial fibrillation."^^xsd:string)

# Individual: X2016_m_vemurafenib_and_atrial_fibrillation_1st_2016:consistentTimeToOnset (consistent time to onset)

AnnotationAssertion(rdfs:label X2016_m_vemurafenib_and_atrial_fibrillation_1st_2016:consistentTimeToOnset "consistent time to onset"^^xsd:string)
ClassAssertion(obo:OAE_0001125 X2016_m_vemurafenib_and_atrial_fibrillation_1st_2016:consistentTimeToOnset)
DataPropertyAssertion(OpenPVSignal:has_content X2016_m_vemurafenib_and_atrial_fibrillation_1st_2016:consistentTimeToOnset "However, the consistent time to onset within three weeks in most of the reports that contained the best evidence of causality in other respects, the evidence of a dose response and the evidence for interactions with biological plausibility all support there being a signal for vemurafenib and atrial fibrillation . However, it is not a strong signal and further investigation would be useful. "^^xsd:string)

