# Individual: X2016_m_vemurafenib_and_atrial_fibrillation_1st_2016:review_of_cardiac_adverse_effects_of_TKIs (review of cardiac adverse effects of TKIs)

AnnotationAssertion(rdfs:label X2016_m_vemurafenib_and_atrial_fibrillation_1st_2016:review_of_cardiac_adverse_effects_of_TKIs "review of cardiac adverse effects of TKIs"^^xsd:string)
ClassAssertion(obo:OAE_0001197 X2016_m_vemurafenib_and_atrial_fibrillation_1st_2016:review_of_cardiac_adverse_effects_of_TKIs)
ObjectPropertyAssertion(OpenPVSignal:refers_to_adverse_effect X2016_m_vemurafenib_and_atrial_fibrillation_1st_2016:review_of_cardiac_adverse_effects_of_TKIs X2016_m_vemurafenib_and_atrial_fibrillation_1st_2016:atrialFibrillation)
ObjectPropertyAssertion(OpenPVSignal:refers_to_drug X2016_m_vemurafenib_and_atrial_fibrillation_1st_2016:review_of_cardiac_adverse_effects_of_TKIs X2016_m_vemurafenib_and_atrial_fibrillation_1st_2016:vemurafenib)
ObjectPropertyAssertion(mp:references X2016_m_vemurafenib_and_atrial_fibrillation_1st_2016:review_of_cardiac_adverse_effects_of_TKIs X2016_m_vemurafenib_and_atrial_fibrillation_1st_2016:Ref.6)
DataPropertyAssertion(OpenPVSignal:has_content X2016_m_vemurafenib_and_atrial_fibrillation_1st_2016:review_of_cardiac_adverse_effects_of_TKIs "In a review of cardiac adverse effects of tyrosine 
kinase inhibitors (TKIs) the authors state that the 
type of cardiovascular side effect differs between 
TKIs based on which cellular signalling pathways 
they inhibit.6 They divided the agents into two 
clinical groups: 
(i) the VSP (VEGF signalling pathway) inhibitors 
and 
(ii) the non-VSP inhibitor agents (which include 
vemurafenib). They went on to state that VSP inhibitors are 
typically associated with hypertension, 
cardiomyopathy and arterial ischemia. Non-VSP 
inhibitors are more commonly associated with QT 
prolongation, arrhythmia, fluid retention and 
rarely cardiomyopathy. However, only 
vemurafenib was linked with atrial fibrillation in a 
table of reported cardiac adverse effects 
associated with TK inhibitors. The incidence was 
reported as 5% but without a reference or 
discussion."^^xsd:string)

