# Individual: X2016_m_levetiracetam_and_impaired_renal_function_2nd_2016:infoForCase4 (info for case 5)

AnnotationAssertion(rdfs:label X2016_m_levetiracetam_and_impaired_renal_function_2nd_2016:infoForCase4 "info for case 5"^^xsd:string)
ClassAssertion(OpenPVSignal:Case_Report_Information X2016_m_levetiracetam_and_impaired_renal_function_2nd_2016:infoForCase4)
DataPropertyAssertion(OpenPVSignal:has_content X2016_m_levetiracetam_and_impaired_renal_function_2nd_2016:infoForCase4 "A 21-year-old male received levetiracetam 250 mg per day at the start of the month (exact time not given). On the 24th, the dose was increased to 500 mg per day and clobazam was added to the regimen. Two days thereafter, a five-fold increase in the creatinine was observed along with an abnormal creatine phosphokinase (CPK). Creatinine continued to increase during two more days reaching a 10- fold increase together with an increased CPK. Levetiracetam was discontinued (no date) and replaced with lamotrigine (clobazam was continued). Patient recovered."^^xsd:string)
DataPropertyAssertion(OpenPVSignal:has_content X2016_m_levetiracetam_and_impaired_renal_function_2nd_2016:infoForCase4 "Reaction abated after drug withdrawal."^^xsd:string)

# Individual: X2016_m_levetiracetam_and_impaired_renal_function_2nd_2016:infoForCase5 (info for case 6)

AnnotationAssertion(rdfs:label X2016_m_levetiracetam_and_impaired_renal_function_2nd_2016:infoForCase5 "info for case 6"^^xsd:string)
ClassAssertion(OpenPVSignal:Case_Report_Information X2016_m_levetiracetam_and_impaired_renal_function_2nd_2016:infoForCase5)
DataPropertyAssertion(OpenPVSignal:has_content X2016_m_levetiracetam_and_impaired_renal_function_2nd_2016:infoForCase5 "In a 60-year-old female; the creatinine had doubled on the fourth day of treatment with levetiracetam compared with the day of treatment start. Two days thereafter, levetiracetam was withdrawn followed by a decreasing creatinine. Patient recovered fully five days after levetiracetam withdrawal."^^xsd:string)
DataPropertyAssertion(OpenPVSignal:has_content X2016_m_levetiracetam_and_impaired_renal_function_2nd_2016:infoForCase5 "Reaction abated after drug withdrawal."^^xsd:string)

# Individual: X2016_m_levetiracetam_and_impaired_renal_function_2nd_2016:infoForCase6 (info for case 4)

AnnotationAssertion(rdfs:label X2016_m_levetiracetam_and_impaired_renal_function_2nd_2016:infoForCase6 "info for case 4"^^xsd:string)
ClassAssertion(OpenPVSignal:Case_Report_Information X2016_m_levetiracetam_and_impaired_renal_function_2nd_2016:infoForCase6)
DataPropertyAssertion(OpenPVSignal:has_content X2016_m_levetiracetam_and_impaired_renal_function_2nd_2016:infoForCase6 "A 73-year-old male presented at hospital with convulsions and started with levetiracetam, at which time creatinine was normal. Patient had a long-time treatment history of glicazide, losartan and aspirin. The day after levetiracetam start, the creatinine had almost doubled. Two days later the creatinine was still elevated. Renal echography was normal. An allergic nephritis was suspected. Levetiracetam, gliclazide and aspirin (unclear if also losartan) was stopped and the next day the creatinine had decreased and was normal five days thereafter. Patient started with carbamazepine and re-started losartan and gliclazide."^^xsd:string)
DataPropertyAssertion(OpenPVSignal:has_content X2016_m_levetiracetam_and_impaired_renal_function_2nd_2016:infoForCase6 "Reaction abated after drug withdrawal. The patient had a history of arterial hypertension and Type 2 diabetes mellitus, and a long-time treatment with glicazide, losartan and aspirin. Losartan is known to cause renal failure."^^xsd:string)

# Individual: X2016_m_levetiracetam_and_impaired_renal_function_2nd_2016:info_for_another_case (info for another case)

AnnotationAssertion(rdfs:label X2016_m_levetiracetam_and_impaired_renal_function_2nd_2016:info_for_another_case "info for another case"^^xsd:string)
ClassAssertion(obo:OAE_0001197 X2016_m_levetiracetam_and_impaired_renal_function_2nd_2016:info_for_another_case)
ClassAssertion(OpenPVSignal:Case_Report_Information X2016_m_levetiracetam_and_impaired_renal_function_2nd_2016:info_for_another_case)
DataPropertyAssertion(OpenPVSignal:has_content X2016_m_levetiracetam_and_impaired_renal_function_2nd_2016:info_for_another_case "In another report, where levetiracetam was the single suspect drug, a 16-year-old was described to be hospitalized for encephalopathy and chorea. The patient was placed on phenytoin, and then transitioned to valproic acid and later to levetiracetam. Serum creatinine started to increase thereafter. This report did not include any other co-reported drugs. Time to onset and dechallenge information was missing for this report."^^xsd:string)

# Individual: X2016_m_levetiracetam_and_impaired_renal_function_2nd_2016:info_for_case_7 (info for case 7)

AnnotationAssertion(rdfs:label X2016_m_levetiracetam_and_impaired_renal_function_2nd_2016:info_for_case_7 "info for case 7"^^xsd:string)
ClassAssertion(OpenPVSignal:Case_Report_Information X2016_m_levetiracetam_and_impaired_renal_function_2nd_2016:info_for_case_7)
DataPropertyAssertion(OpenPVSignal:has_content X2016_m_levetiracetam_and_impaired_renal_function_2nd_2016:info_for_case_7 "Reaction abated after drug withdrawal. Dates were not given for the different dosages."^^xsd:string)

# Individual: X2016_m_levetiracetam_and_impaired_renal_function_2nd_2016:info_for_case_8 (info for case 8)

