DataPropertyAssertion(OpenPVSignal:has_content X2016_m_levetiracetam_and_impaired_renal_function_2nd_2016:info_for_case_8 "Reaction abated after drug withdrawal."^^xsd:string)

# Individual: X2016_m_levetiracetam_and_impaired_renal_function_2nd_2016:info_for_case_9 (info for case 9)

AnnotationAssertion(rdfs:label X2016_m_levetiracetam_and_impaired_renal_function_2nd_2016:info_for_case_9 "info for case 9"^^xsd:string)
ClassAssertion(OpenPVSignal:Case_Report_Information X2016_m_levetiracetam_and_impaired_renal_function_2nd_2016:info_for_case_9)
DataPropertyAssertion(OpenPVSignal:has_content X2016_m_levetiracetam_and_impaired_renal_function_2nd_2016:info_for_case_9 "Reaction abated after drug withdrawal. Levetiracetam was changed to lacosamide and patient improved clinically and the creatinine normalized over 1 month."^^xsd:string)

# Individual: X2016_m_levetiracetam_and_impaired_renal_function_2nd_2016:info_for_case_with_nephritis_interstitial_1 (info for case with nephritis interstitial 1)

AnnotationAssertion(rdfs:label X2016_m_levetiracetam_and_impaired_renal_function_2nd_2016:info_for_case_with_nephritis_interstitial_1 "info for case with nephritis interstitial 1"^^xsd:string)
ClassAssertion(OpenPVSignal:Case_Report_Information X2016_m_levetiracetam_and_impaired_renal_function_2nd_2016:info_for_case_with_nephritis_interstitial_1)
DataPropertyAssertion(OpenPVSignal:has_content X2016_m_levetiracetam_and_impaired_renal_function_2nd_2016:info_for_case_with_nephritis_interstitial_1 "A 52-year-old female was diagnosed with interstitial nephritis after five months treatment with levetiracetam 2000 mg daily. Drug was stopped 10 months after event start. Patient had not recovered at the time of report. Reported concomitant drugs were: tramadol, citalopram, simvastatin, folic acid and iron. No dates were given for these drugs."^^xsd:string)

# Individual: X2016_m_levetiracetam_and_impaired_renal_function_2nd_2016:info_for_case_with_nephritis_interstitial_2 (info for case with nephritis interstitial 2)

AnnotationAssertion(rdfs:label X2016_m_levetiracetam_and_impaired_renal_function_2nd_2016:info_for_case_with_nephritis_interstitial_2 "info for case with nephritis interstitial 2"^^xsd:string)
ClassAssertion(OpenPVSignal:Case_Report_Information X2016_m_levetiracetam_and_impaired_renal_function_2nd_2016:info_for_case_with_nephritis_interstitial_2)
DataPropertyAssertion(OpenPVSignal:has_content X2016_m_levetiracetam_and_impaired_renal_function_2nd_2016:info_for_case_with_nephritis_interstitial_2 "A 37-year-old male was diagnosed with interstitial nephritis and renal interstitial fibrosis after about four months of treatment with levetiracetam. It is unknown if the drug was stopped. Patient had not recovered at the time of report. Reported concomitant drugs were: valproic acid and carbamazepine. No dates were given for these drugs."^^xsd:string)

# Individual: X2016_m_levetiracetam_and_impaired_renal_function_2nd_2016:info_for_more_cases (info for more cases)

AnnotationAssertion(rdfs:label X2016_m_levetiracetam_and_impaired_renal_function_2nd_2016:info_for_more_cases "info for more cases"^^xsd:string)
ClassAssertion(obo:OAE_0001125 X2016_m_levetiracetam_and_impaired_renal_function_2nd_2016:info_for_more_cases)
ClassAssertion(OpenPVSignal:Case_Report_Information X2016_m_levetiracetam_and_impaired_renal_function_2nd_2016:info_for_more_cases)
DataPropertyAssertion(OpenPVSignal:has_content X2016_m_levetiracetam_and_impaired_renal_function_2nd_2016:info_for_more_cases "In another report, levetiracetam was the single 
suspect drug and most likely the spontaneously 
reported published 69-year-old case described 
later in this signal.10
In three reports, levetiracetam was co-suspect 
with other drugs but because dates were lacking it 
was not possible to assess which of the drugs were 
more likely to have induced the event. The co-suspect drugs were valproic acid, topiramate, 
fluconazole. Interstitial nephritis is not labelled for 
any of these drugs.
In three additional reports, the co-suspect drugs; 
melperone, oesomeprazole and carbamazepine, 
respectively, were more likely the drugs inducing 
the interstitial nephritis in these cases.
The main event for a 32-year-old was DRESS 
syndrome that was co-reported with the interstitial 
nephritis. Co-suspect drugs for this patient were 
vancomycin and valproic acid."^^xsd:string)

# Individual: X2016_m_levetiracetam_and_impaired_renal_function_2nd_2016:informationForCase1 (info for case 1)

AnnotationAssertion(rdfs:label X2016_m_levetiracetam_and_impaired_renal_function_2nd_2016:informationForCase1 "info for case 1"^^xsd:string)
ClassAssertion(OpenPVSignal:Case_Report_Information X2016_m_levetiracetam_and_impaired_renal_function_2nd_2016:informationForCase1)
DataPropertyAssertion(OpenPVSignal:has_content X2016_m_levetiracetam_and_impaired_renal_function_2nd_2016:informationForCase1 "A 17-year-old published female case report (case 1), resulting in eight duplicate reports, had the most likely causal relationship.4 The patient had been treated with levetiracetam for 10 days when diagnosed with ARF and biopsy- confirmed interstitial nephritis. She sought health care because of vomiting, loose stools and abdominal pain for the past two days.
Creatinine levels were normal before she started levetiracetam and declined after withdrawal of the drug and treatment with prednisone. The authors of this publication stated that she had no prior history of renal problems or used other medications that could have explained the event."^^xsd:string)
DataPropertyAssertion(OpenPVSignal:has_content X2016_m_levetiracetam_and_impaired_renal_function_2nd_2016:informationForCase1 "Reaction abated after drug withdrawal and corticosteroidtreatment. No history of renal problems and no other medications. Changed antiepileptic treatment to oxcarbamazepine."^^xsd:string)

# Individual: X2016_m_levetiracetam_and_impaired_renal_function_2nd_2016:informationForCase2 (info for case 2)

AnnotationAssertion(rdfs:label X2016_m_levetiracetam_and_impaired_renal_function_2nd_2016:informationForCase2 "info for case 2"^^xsd:string)
ClassAssertion(OpenPVSignal:Case_Report_Information X2016_m_levetiracetam_and_impaired_renal_function_2nd_2016:informationForCase2)
DataPropertyAssertion(OpenPVSignal:has_content X2016_m_levetiracetam_and_impaired_renal_function_2nd_2016:informationForCase2 "A 12-year-old female (case 2) was admitted to hospital for ARF, metabolic acidosis, respiratory distress and confusion, which was described in a published abstract.8 A few hours after admission she became encephalopathic. Levetiracetam levels were found to be high and the probable cause of encephalopathy. Levetiracetam was stopped and replaced with valproate and patient improved after about five days. The focus in the abstract was on the encephalopathy, and it was unclear what the origin of the ARF was."^^xsd:string)
DataPropertyAssertion(OpenPVSignal:has_content X2016_m_levetiracetam_and_impaired_renal_function_2nd_2016:informationForCase2 "Patient returned to baseline after drug withdrawal.Unclear why she was admitted for acute renal failure. Had a history of Chiari II, myelomeningocele, shunted hydrocephalus, renal tubular acidosis and well-controlled epilepsy on levetiracetam."^^xsd:string)

# Individual: X2016_m_levetiracetam_and_impaired_renal_function_2nd_2016:informationForCase3 (info for case 3)

AnnotationAssertion(rdfs:label X2016_m_levetiracetam_and_impaired_renal_function_2nd_2016:informationForCase3 "info for case 3"^^xsd:string)
ClassAssertion(OpenPVSignal:Case_Report_Information X2016_m_levetiracetam_and_impaired_renal_function_2nd_2016:informationForCase3)
DataPropertyAssertion(OpenPVSignal:has_content X2016_m_levetiracetam_and_impaired_renal_function_2nd_2016:informationForCase3 "A 6-week-old premature baby (case 3) was diagnosed with ARF after 16 days treatment with levetiracetam. Reaction abated when the drug was withdrawn. Prematurity could contribute to the susceptibility."^^xsd:string)
DataPropertyAssertion(OpenPVSignal:has_content X2016_m_levetiracetam_and_impaired_renal_function_2nd_2016:informationForCase3 "Reaction abated after drug withdrawal. Prematurity could contribute to susceptibility. Renalfailure reported as transient."^^xsd:string)

