# Individual: X2016_m_dabigatran_3rd_2016:AssessmentLimitations (Assessment limitations )

AnnotationAssertion(rdfs:label X2016_m_dabigatran_3rd_2016:AssessmentLimitations "Assessment limitations "^^xsd:string)
ClassAssertion(obo:OAE_0001182 X2016_m_dabigatran_3rd_2016:AssessmentLimitations)
ClassAssertion(OpenPVSignal:Free_text_reporting_element X2016_m_dabigatran_3rd_2016:AssessmentLimitations)
DataPropertyAssertion(OpenPVSignal:has_content X2016_m_dabigatran_3rd_2016:AssessmentLimitations "It is acknowledged that the information in VigiBase® is heterogeneous, i.e., it originates from multiple sources (different countries and types of reporters) and the amount of information given may vary from case to case. As an example, even though there were several patients apparently following treatment guidelines, little information on whether patients were compliant or not could be retrieved. Our case series presents patients with additional risk factors to those connected with the primary indication for dabigatran and include neoplasm, concomitant prothrombotic medications, myocardial infarction and coronary artery disease. It is not possible at this stage to compare the effectiveness of dabigatran with warfarin or enoxaparin in the type of patients this case series represents.  "^^xsd:string)

# Individual: X2016_m_dabigatran_3rd_2016:CHMP_report_for_dabigatran (CHMP report for dabigatran)

AnnotationAssertion(rdfs:label X2016_m_dabigatran_3rd_2016:CHMP_report_for_dabigatran "CHMP report for dabigatran"^^xsd:string)
ClassAssertion(obo:OAE_0001197 X2016_m_dabigatran_3rd_2016:CHMP_report_for_dabigatran)
ObjectPropertyAssertion(OpenPVSignal:is_supported_by_statistical_entity X2016_m_dabigatran_3rd_2016:CHMP_report_for_dabigatran X2016_m_dabigatran_3rd_2016:frequencyOfDeepVeinthrombosis-CHMPreport-150Mg)
ObjectPropertyAssertion(OpenPVSignal:is_supported_by_statistical_entity X2016_m_dabigatran_3rd_2016:CHMP_report_for_dabigatran X2016_m_dabigatran_3rd_2016:frequencyOfDeepVeinthrombosis-CHMPreport-220Mg)
ObjectPropertyAssertion(OpenPVSignal:refers_to_adverse_effect X2016_m_dabigatran_3rd_2016:CHMP_report_for_dabigatran X2016_m_dabigatran_3rd_2016:venousThromboembolism)
ObjectPropertyAssertion(OpenPVSignal:refers_to_drug X2016_m_dabigatran_3rd_2016:CHMP_report_for_dabigatran X2016_m_dabigatran_3rd_2016:dabigatran)
ObjectPropertyAssertion(mp:references X2016_m_dabigatran_3rd_2016:CHMP_report_for_dabigatran X2016_m_dabigatran_3rd_2016:Ref.12)
DataPropertyAssertion(OpenPVSignal:has_content X2016_m_dabigatran_3rd_2016:CHMP_report_for_dabigatran "In the 2008 European Medicines Agency (EMA) Committee for Medicinal Products for Human Use (CHMP) Assessment Report, the event “deep vein thrombosis” is described among the most frequent adverse events in the pivotal studies of venous thromboembolism prevention after knee and hip total replacement with a frequency of 9.3% and 6.4% for dabigatran 150 mg and 220 mg daily respectively. In addition, deep vein thrombosis was reported among the most common reasons for discontinuation due to adverse events.12"^^xsd:string)

# Individual: X2016_m_dabigatran_3rd_2016:ConclusionContent (Conclusion content)

AnnotationAssertion(rdfs:label X2016_m_dabigatran_3rd_2016:ConclusionContent "Conclusion content"^^xsd:string)
ClassAssertion(OpenPVSignal:Conclusion X2016_m_dabigatran_3rd_2016:ConclusionContent)
ObjectPropertyAssertion(mp:references X2016_m_dabigatran_3rd_2016:ConclusionContent X2016_m_dabigatran_3rd_2016:Ref.26)
DataPropertyAssertion(OpenPVSignal:has_content X2016_m_dabigatran_3rd_2016:ConclusionContent "The most informative reports in VigiBase® reporting venous or arterial thrombotic or embolic events in patients on dabigatran therapy were collected and analysed according to the dabigatran indication. The information in two thirds of the 79 most informative reports indicated that dabigatran was ineffective in overcoming multiple thrombosis risk factors. However, modifiable risk factors included lower than recommended doses, coprescription of pro-thrombotic medicines and, possibly, co-prescription of proton pump inhibitors. The 79 discussed reports were submitted from Americas, Asia and Europe, with most of them coming from Europe. Spontaneous reporting is used for collecting information about unexpected adverse reactions once drugs are on the market. It is not used to assess drug efficacy, but can be used to detect unexpected cases of failure of therapy.26 In the case of the topic of this study, it has been useful in highlighting risk factors for dabigatran ineffectiveness in clinical practice, including those that might be modifiable. Given the strong correlation between dabigatran plasma levels and anticoagulant effect, therapeutic drug monitoring could provide valuable information for dose selection in patients on potentially interacting medicines, elderly patients with apparently normal renal function to ensure they receive an adequate dose, and where there are concerns about adherence. "^^xsd:string)

