ObjectPropertyAssertion(mp:references X2016_m_dabigatran_3rd_2016:RE-NOVATETrial X2016_m_dabigatran_3rd_2016:Ref.8)
DataPropertyAssertion(OpenPVSignal:has_content X2016_m_dabigatran_3rd_2016:RE-NOVATETrial "In the RE-MODEL trial (knee replacement), dabigatran treatment was for 6-10 days, while in the RE-NOVATE trial (hip replacement) it was for 28-35 days; respectively, 2,076 and 3,494 patients were treated. The rate of symptomatic pulmonary embolism during treatment was low, both with the 220 mg daily dose (0.0% for knee replacements, 0.4% for hip), and the 150 mg daily dose (0.1% for knee replacement and 0.1% for hip). The rate of symptomatic deep vein thrombosis was 0.1% for knee replacement and 0.5% for hip surgery within the 220 mg group; whereas recorded rates were 0.4% and 0.8% within the 150 mg daily dose group respectively. Similarly, the rate of symptomatic VTE during the three-month RE-NOVATE II study period was low (0.3%) and comparable with that reported in RE-NOVATE.7-9"^^xsd:string)

# Individual: X2016_m_dabigatran_3rd_2016:RE-NOVATE_trial_2 (RE-NOVATE trial 2)

AnnotationAssertion(rdfs:label X2016_m_dabigatran_3rd_2016:RE-NOVATE_trial_2 "RE-NOVATE trial 2"^^xsd:string)
ClassAssertion(OpenPVSignal:Clinical_trial_information X2016_m_dabigatran_3rd_2016:RE-NOVATE_trial_2)
ObjectPropertyAssertion(OpenPVSignal:is_supported_by_statistical_entity X2016_m_dabigatran_3rd_2016:RE-NOVATE_trial_2 X2016_m_dabigatran_3rd_2016:rateOfSymptomaticVTE)
ObjectPropertyAssertion(OpenPVSignal:refers_to_drug X2016_m_dabigatran_3rd_2016:RE-NOVATE_trial_2 X2016_m_dabigatran_3rd_2016:dabigatran)
ObjectPropertyAssertion(mp:references X2016_m_dabigatran_3rd_2016:RE-NOVATE_trial_2 X2016_m_dabigatran_3rd_2016:Ref.9)
DataPropertyAssertion(OpenPVSignal:has_content X2016_m_dabigatran_3rd_2016:RE-NOVATE_trial_2 "In the RE-MODEL trial (knee replacement), dabigatran treatment was for 6-10 days, while in the RE-NOVATE trial (hip replacement) it was for 28-35 days; respectively, 2,076 and 3,494 patients were treated. The rate of symptomatic pulmonary embolism during treatment was low, both with the 220 mg daily dose (0.0% for knee replacements, 0.4% for hip), and the 150 mg daily dose (0.1% for knee replacement and 0.1% for hip). The rate of symptomatic deep vein thrombosis was 0.1% for knee replacement and 0.5% for hip surgery within the 220 mg group; whereas recorded rates were 0.4% and 0.8% within the 150 mg daily dose group respectively. Similarly, the rate of symptomatic VTE during the three-month RE-NOVATE II study period was low (0.3%) and comparable with that reported in RE-NOVATE.7-9"^^xsd:string)

