# Individual: X2016_m_dabigatran_3rd_2016:ReportByShahAboutLackOfAdherence (Report by Shah about lack of adherence)

AnnotationAssertion(rdfs:label X2016_m_dabigatran_3rd_2016:ReportByShahAboutLackOfAdherence "Report by Shah about lack of adherence"^^xsd:string)
ClassAssertion(obo:OAE_0001197 X2016_m_dabigatran_3rd_2016:ReportByShahAboutLackOfAdherence)
ObjectPropertyAssertion(OpenPVSignal:refers_to_adverse_effect X2016_m_dabigatran_3rd_2016:ReportByShahAboutLackOfAdherence X2016_m_dabigatran_3rd_2016:atrial_thrombosis)
ObjectPropertyAssertion(OpenPVSignal:refers_to_drug X2016_m_dabigatran_3rd_2016:ReportByShahAboutLackOfAdherence X2016_m_dabigatran_3rd_2016:dabigatran)
ObjectPropertyAssertion(mp:references X2016_m_dabigatran_3rd_2016:ReportByShahAboutLackOfAdherence X2016_m_dabigatran_3rd_2016:Ref.13)
DataPropertyAssertion(OpenPVSignal:has_content X2016_m_dabigatran_3rd_2016:ReportByShahAboutLackOfAdherence "Shah et al. described left atrial thrombus formation with consequent cerebrovascular accident in a 60-year-old man on dabigatran therapy. This patient had a past medical history of hypertension, coronary artery disease, chronic atrial fibrillation, and stroke. They speculated that lack of patient adherence may have decreased the bioavailability and effectiveness of dabigatran.13  "^^xsd:string)

# Individual: X2016_m_dabigatran_3rd_2016:ReportBySharma (Report by Sharma )

AnnotationAssertion(rdfs:label X2016_m_dabigatran_3rd_2016:ReportBySharma "Report by Sharma "^^xsd:string)
ClassAssertion(obo:OAE_0001197 X2016_m_dabigatran_3rd_2016:ReportBySharma)
ObjectPropertyAssertion(OpenPVSignal:refers_to_adverse_effect X2016_m_dabigatran_3rd_2016:ReportBySharma X2016_m_dabigatran_3rd_2016:atrial_thrombosis)
ObjectPropertyAssertion(OpenPVSignal:refers_to_drug X2016_m_dabigatran_3rd_2016:ReportBySharma X2016_m_dabigatran_3rd_2016:dabigatran)
ObjectPropertyAssertion(mp:references X2016_m_dabigatran_3rd_2016:ReportBySharma X2016_m_dabigatran_3rd_2016:Ref.14)
DataPropertyAssertion(OpenPVSignal:has_content X2016_m_dabigatran_3rd_2016:ReportBySharma "Sharma et al. described two cases of dabigatran failure leading to left atrial thrombosis. One patient suffered a stroke due to cardiac embolism ten weeks after dabigatran therapy was started. This patient had a history of congestive heart failure. The other patient had a concomitant active lung cancer. They speculated that the “downstream” single-point blockade of the coagulation cascade (at the level of thrombin) may incite a compensatory increase in the “upstream” coagulation factor levels. At the same time they suggested that the absence of routine monitoring could prevent diagnosis of subtherapeutic drug levels. "^^xsd:string)

