# Individual: X2016_m_dabigatran_3rd_2016:possible_mechanism_for_thrombosis_during_dabigatran_therapy (possible mechanism for thrombosis during dabigatran therapy)

AnnotationAssertion(rdfs:label X2016_m_dabigatran_3rd_2016:possible_mechanism_for_thrombosis_during_dabigatran_therapy "possible mechanism for thrombosis during dabigatran therapy"^^xsd:string)
ClassAssertion(OpenPVSignal:Adverse_Effect_Mechanism X2016_m_dabigatran_3rd_2016:possible_mechanism_for_thrombosis_during_dabigatran_therapy)
ObjectPropertyAssertion(mp:references X2016_m_dabigatran_3rd_2016:possible_mechanism_for_thrombosis_during_dabigatran_therapy X2016_m_dabigatran_3rd_2016:Ref.25)
DataPropertyAssertion(OpenPVSignal:has_content X2016_m_dabigatran_3rd_2016:possible_mechanism_for_thrombosis_during_dabigatran_therapy "There is one published case series of thrombosis developing within one month of dabigatran withdrawal. The possibility of rebound, and therefore the question of how to stop dabigatran safely, was raised.25 Dabigatran has a much shorter half-life than warfarin and it is possible therefore that thrombosis might be more likely to develop when doses are missed or when therapy is discontinued."^^xsd:string)

# Individual: X2016_m_dabigatran_3rd_2016:predispositionForTheDevelopmentOfPulmonaryEmbolismForDabigatranPatients (predisposition for the development of pulmonary embolism for dabigatran patients)

AnnotationAssertion(rdfs:label X2016_m_dabigatran_3rd_2016:predispositionForTheDevelopmentOfPulmonaryEmbolismForDabigatranPatients "predisposition for the development of pulmonary embolism for dabigatran patients"^^xsd:string)
ClassAssertion(obo:OAE_0001182 X2016_m_dabigatran_3rd_2016:predispositionForTheDevelopmentOfPulmonaryEmbolismForDabigatranPatients)
ObjectPropertyAssertion(mp:references X2016_m_dabigatran_3rd_2016:predispositionForTheDevelopmentOfPulmonaryEmbolismForDabigatranPatients X2016_m_dabigatran_3rd_2016:Ref.21)
ObjectPropertyAssertion(mp:references X2016_m_dabigatran_3rd_2016:predispositionForTheDevelopmentOfPulmonaryEmbolismForDabigatranPatients X2016_m_dabigatran_3rd_2016:Ref.22)
ObjectPropertyAssertion(mp:references X2016_m_dabigatran_3rd_2016:predispositionForTheDevelopmentOfPulmonaryEmbolismForDabigatranPatients X2016_m_dabigatran_3rd_2016:Ref.23)
ObjectPropertyAssertion(mp:references X2016_m_dabigatran_3rd_2016:predispositionForTheDevelopmentOfPulmonaryEmbolismForDabigatranPatients X2016_m_dabigatran_3rd_2016:Ref.24)
DataPropertyAssertion(OpenPVSignal:has_content X2016_m_dabigatran_3rd_2016:predispositionForTheDevelopmentOfPulmonaryEmbolismForDabigatranPatients "It is therefore possible that patients who develop pulmonary embolism while taking dabigatran for stroke prevention represent a group of predisposed individuals in whom co-morbid hypercoagulable states overcome the effect of dabigatran. It is also known that AF is associated with a hypercoagulable state.21-23 Noel et al. described a higher incidence of deep vein thrombosis and pulmonary embolism in stroke patients with NVAF.21 However, atrial fibrillation is not listed as a cause of venous thromboembolism in standard texts unless there has been immobility due to stroke.2 4"^^xsd:string)

