DataPropertyAssertion(OpenPVSignal:has_content X2016_m_febuxostat_and_allegric_vasculitis_3rd_20:Mechanism_fo_febuxostat "Febuxostat is a 2-arylthiazole derivative that achieves its therapeutic effect of decreasing serum uric acid by selectively inhibiting xanthine oxidase (XO). Uric acid is the end product of purine metabolism in humans and is generated in the cascade of hypoxanthine being converted to xanthine and xanthine converted to uric acid. Both steps in the above transformations are catalyzed by XO . 
Febuxostat is a 2-arylthiazole derivative that achieves its therapeutic effect of decreasing serum uric acid by selectively inhibiting xanthine oxidase (XO). Uric acid is the end product of purine metabolism in humans and is generated in the cascade of hypoxanthine being converted to xanthine and xanthine converted to uric acid. Both steps in the above transformations are catalyzed by XO ."^^xsd:string)

