ObjectPropertyAssertion(OpenPVSignal:refers_to_drug X2016_m_febuxostat_and_allegric_vasculitis_3rd_20:literature_case X2016_m_febuxostat_and_allegric_vasculitis_3rd_20:febuxostat)
ObjectPropertyAssertion(mp:references X2016_m_febuxostat_and_allegric_vasculitis_3rd_20:literature_case X2016_m_febuxostat_and_allegric_vasculitis_3rd_20:Ref.5)
DataPropertyAssertion(OpenPVSignal:has_content X2016_m_febuxostat_and_allegric_vasculitis_3rd_20:literature_case "In the literature, there is a report on the use of febuxostat in allopurinol-intolerant patients. Although the drug was well tolerated in 12 of 13 patients, one patient previously hospitalized with documented exfoliative erythroderma during allopurinol treatment, developed biopsy-confirmed cutaneous leukocytoclastic vasculitis, likely but not definitively febuxostat-related. In the opinion of the authors, this occurrence early in treatment mandates caution, careful dose escalation, and close monitoring when febuxostat urate-lowering therapy is considered.5"^^xsd:string)

