ObjectPropertyAssertion(OpenPVSignal:refers_to_adverse_effect X2016_m_thiamazole_and_rhabdomyolysis_4rth_2016:Known_AE_for_thiamazole X2016_m_thiamazole_and_rhabdomyolysis_4rth_2016:skinReactions)
ObjectPropertyAssertion(OpenPVSignal:refers_to_adverse_effect X2016_m_thiamazole_and_rhabdomyolysis_4rth_2016:Known_AE_for_thiamazole X2016_m_thiamazole_and_rhabdomyolysis_4rth_2016:thrombocytopenia)
ObjectPropertyAssertion(OpenPVSignal:refers_to_drug X2016_m_thiamazole_and_rhabdomyolysis_4rth_2016:Known_AE_for_thiamazole X2016_m_thiamazole_and_rhabdomyolysis_4rth_2016:thiamazole)
DataPropertyAssertion(OpenPVSignal:has_content X2016_m_thiamazole_and_rhabdomyolysis_4rth_2016:Known_AE_for_thiamazole "Minor adverse reactions include gastrointestinal disorders, skin reactions and a variety of other reactions including myalgia. Serious adverse reactions include inhibition of myelopoieses (agranulocytosis, granulocytopenia, thrombocytopenia and aplastic anaemia), drug fever, a lupus-like syndrome, insulin autoimmune syndrome, hepatitis, periarteritis, and hypoprothrombinaemia"^^xsd:string)

# Individual: X2016_m_thiamazole_and_rhabdomyolysis_4rth_2016:Literature_and_Labelling (Literature and Labelling)

AnnotationAssertion(rdfs:label X2016_m_thiamazole_and_rhabdomyolysis_4rth_2016:Literature_and_Labelling "Literature and Labelling"^^xsd:string)
ClassAssertion(OpenPVSignal:Literature_information X2016_m_thiamazole_and_rhabdomyolysis_4rth_2016:Literature_and_Labelling)
ObjectPropertyAssertion(mp:references X2016_m_thiamazole_and_rhabdomyolysis_4rth_2016:Literature_and_Labelling X2016_m_thiamazole_and_rhabdomyolysis_4rth_2016:Ref.3)
ObjectPropertyAssertion(mp:references X2016_m_thiamazole_and_rhabdomyolysis_4rth_2016:Literature_and_Labelling X2016_m_thiamazole_and_rhabdomyolysis_4rth_2016:Ref.4)
ObjectPropertyAssertion(mp:references X2016_m_thiamazole_and_rhabdomyolysis_4rth_2016:Literature_and_Labelling X2016_m_thiamazole_and_rhabdomyolysis_4rth_2016:Ref.5)
DataPropertyAssertion(OpenPVSignal:has_content X2016_m_thiamazole_and_rhabdomyolysis_4rth_2016:Literature_and_Labelling "The product literature does not refer to rhabdomyolysis although it does mention myalgia as a possible adverse reaction. In the literature, there is one report describing rhabdomyolysis in association with thiamazole, interpreted as Case 18 in Table 1.3 This was reported as the first reported case of such an association. There is a literature report of another antithyroid drug, carbimazole (which is converted to thiamazole in the body) as a possible cause of rhabdomyolysis, in which Seow et al reported three patients who developed rhabdomyolyis during treatment with carbimazole.4 In the product literature for carbimazole, it is noted that isolated cases of myopathy have been reported.5"^^xsd:string)

