# Individual: X2016_m_thiamazole_and_rhabdomyolysis_4rth_2016:PossibleMechanismOfRhabdomyolysisDuringco-administrationOfThiamazoleAndRosuvastatin (Possible mechanism  of rhabdomyolysis during co-administration of thiamazole and rosuvastatin)

AnnotationAssertion(rdfs:label X2016_m_thiamazole_and_rhabdomyolysis_4rth_2016:PossibleMechanismOfRhabdomyolysisDuringco-administrationOfThiamazoleAndRosuvastatin "Possible mechanism  of rhabdomyolysis during co-administration of thiamazole and rosuvastatin"^^xsd:string)
ClassAssertion(OpenPVSignal:Adverse_Effect_Mechanism X2016_m_thiamazole_and_rhabdomyolysis_4rth_2016:PossibleMechanismOfRhabdomyolysisDuringco-administrationOfThiamazoleAndRosuvastatin)
ObjectPropertyAssertion(OpenPVSignal:refers_to_adverse_effect X2016_m_thiamazole_and_rhabdomyolysis_4rth_2016:PossibleMechanismOfRhabdomyolysisDuringco-administrationOfThiamazoleAndRosuvastatin X2016_m_thiamazole_and_rhabdomyolysis_4rth_2016:rhabdomyolysis)
ObjectPropertyAssertion(mp:references X2016_m_thiamazole_and_rhabdomyolysis_4rth_2016:PossibleMechanismOfRhabdomyolysisDuringco-administrationOfThiamazoleAndRosuvastatin X2016_m_thiamazole_and_rhabdomyolysis_4rth_2016:Ref.7)
ObjectPropertyAssertion(mp:references X2016_m_thiamazole_and_rhabdomyolysis_4rth_2016:PossibleMechanismOfRhabdomyolysisDuringco-administrationOfThiamazoleAndRosuvastatin X2016_m_thiamazole_and_rhabdomyolysis_4rth_2016:Ref.8)
DataPropertyAssertion(OpenPVSignal:has_content X2016_m_thiamazole_and_rhabdomyolysis_4rth_2016:PossibleMechanismOfRhabdomyolysisDuringco-administrationOfThiamazoleAndRosuvastatin "Thiamazole has been demonstrated to be an inhibitor of cytochrome P450 (CYP) 3A4 and a published case report demonstrated an interaction between thiamazole and erythromycin, well known to be metabolised by CYP 3A4.7,8 Inhibition of this enzyme can result in an accumulation of erythromycin and the occurrence of toxic effects . It is possible in Case 20 that thiamazole may have inhibited the metabolism of simvastatin and resulted in an accumulation of the drug which may have made the patient more susceptible to rhabdomyolysis."^^xsd:string)

