# Individual: X2016_m_thiamazole_and_rhabdomyolysis_4rth_2016:case15Information (case 15 information)

AnnotationAssertion(rdfs:label X2016_m_thiamazole_and_rhabdomyolysis_4rth_2016:case15Information "case 15 information"^^xsd:string)
ClassAssertion(OpenPVSignal:Case_Report_Information X2016_m_thiamazole_and_rhabdomyolysis_4rth_2016:case15Information)
DataPropertyAssertion(OpenPVSignal:has_content X2016_m_thiamazole_and_rhabdomyolysis_4rth_2016:case15Information "In Case 15, an unknown drug was co-suspected. However, although the nature of this drug is unknown, it was continued while thiamazole was withdrawn and the patient recovered so thiamazole appears a more likely cause. "^^xsd:string)

# Individual: X2016_m_thiamazole_and_rhabdomyolysis_4rth_2016:case17Information (case 17 information)

AnnotationAssertion(rdfs:label X2016_m_thiamazole_and_rhabdomyolysis_4rth_2016:case17Information "case 17 information"^^xsd:string)
ClassAssertion(OpenPVSignal:Case_Report_Information X2016_m_thiamazole_and_rhabdomyolysis_4rth_2016:case17Information)
DataPropertyAssertion(OpenPVSignal:has_content X2016_m_thiamazole_and_rhabdomyolysis_4rth_2016:case17Information "In Case 17, ketotifen was also suspected and although there are no dates available on which to ascertain the likelihood of causality, there is no reference to any muscle effects in the product information for ketotifen, and there is no reason to suspect it as a more likely cause"^^xsd:string)

# Individual: X2016_m_thiamazole_and_rhabdomyolysis_4rth_2016:case20Information (case 20 information)

AnnotationAssertion(rdfs:label X2016_m_thiamazole_and_rhabdomyolysis_4rth_2016:case20Information "case 20 information"^^xsd:string)
ClassAssertion(OpenPVSignal:Case_Report_Information X2016_m_thiamazole_and_rhabdomyolysis_4rth_2016:case20Information)
DataPropertyAssertion(OpenPVSignal:has_content X2016_m_thiamazole_and_rhabdomyolysis_4rth_2016:case20Information "It is possible in Case 20 that thiamazole may have inhibited the metabolism of simvastatin and resulted in an accumulation of the drug which may have made the patient more susceptible to rhabdomyolysis "^^xsd:string)

# Individual: X2016_m_thiamazole_and_rhabdomyolysis_4rth_2016:case3Information (case 3 information)

AnnotationAssertion(rdfs:label X2016_m_thiamazole_and_rhabdomyolysis_4rth_2016:case3Information "case 3 information"^^xsd:string)
ClassAssertion(OpenPVSignal:Case_Report_Information X2016_m_thiamazole_and_rhabdomyolysis_4rth_2016:case3Information)
DataPropertyAssertion(OpenPVSignal:has_content X2016_m_thiamazole_and_rhabdomyolysis_4rth_2016:case3Information "In Case 3/4, propylthiouracil was also suspected and although there are no dates available on which to ascertain the likelihood of causality, myopathy is listed as an adverse reaction in the product information for propylthiouracil and it may be a more likely cause "^^xsd:string)

# Individual: X2016_m_thiamazole_and_rhabdomyolysis_4rth_2016:case4Information (case 4 information)

AnnotationAssertion(rdfs:label X2016_m_thiamazole_and_rhabdomyolysis_4rth_2016:case4Information "case 4 information"^^xsd:string)
ClassAssertion(OpenPVSignal:Case_Report_Information X2016_m_thiamazole_and_rhabdomyolysis_4rth_2016:case4Information)
DataPropertyAssertion(OpenPVSignal:has_content X2016_m_thiamazole_and_rhabdomyolysis_4rth_2016:case4Information "In Case 3/4, propylthiouracil was also suspected and although there are no dates available on which to ascertain the likelihood of causality, myopathy is listed as an adverse reaction in the product information for propylthiouracil and it may be a more likely cause "^^xsd:string)

# Individual: X2016_m_thiamazole_and_rhabdomyolysis_4rth_2016:case7Information (case 7 information)

AnnotationAssertion(rdfs:label X2016_m_thiamazole_and_rhabdomyolysis_4rth_2016:case7Information "case 7 information"^^xsd:string)
ClassAssertion(OpenPVSignal:Case_Report_Information X2016_m_thiamazole_and_rhabdomyolysis_4rth_2016:case7Information)
DataPropertyAssertion(OpenPVSignal:has_content X2016_m_thiamazole_and_rhabdomyolysis_4rth_2016:case7Information "In Case 7, rosuvastatin is a co-suspected drug. Statins are a well-known cause of rhabdomyolysis and could be a more likely cause. Onset occurred nine days after initiation of rosuvastatin and recovery occurred after rosuvastatin withdrawal. This seems more indicative of causality than the use of thiamazole for which the reaction occurred six months after use - however, recovery also occurred after dose reduction of thiamazole. As discussed below, there is a possibility of an interaction between methimazole and rosuvastatin but rosuvastatin is less likely to be involved in CYP interactions than simvastatin.6"^^xsd:string)

