# Individual: X2016_m_dimenhydrinate_and_erythema_multifore_5th:AtypicalTypeToOnsetForSJS (Atypical type to onset for SJS)

AnnotationAssertion(rdfs:label X2016_m_dimenhydrinate_and_erythema_multifore_5th:AtypicalTypeToOnsetForSJS "Atypical type to onset for SJS"^^xsd:string)
ClassAssertion(obo:OAE_0001182 X2016_m_dimenhydrinate_and_erythema_multifore_5th:AtypicalTypeToOnsetForSJS)
DataPropertyAssertion(OpenPVSignal:has_content X2016_m_dimenhydrinate_and_erythema_multifore_5th:AtypicalTypeToOnsetForSJS "On the other hand, although SJS occurrence after short latency has been registered,14 the time to onset in this case series seems atypical when compared to the average 2-3 weeks. "^^xsd:string)

# Individual: X2016_m_dimenhydrinate_and_erythema_multifore_5th:Conclusions_content (Conclusions content)

AnnotationAssertion(rdfs:label X2016_m_dimenhydrinate_and_erythema_multifore_5th:Conclusions_content "Conclusions content"^^xsd:string)
ClassAssertion(OpenPVSignal:Conclusion X2016_m_dimenhydrinate_and_erythema_multifore_5th:Conclusions_content)
DataPropertyAssertion(OpenPVSignal:has_content X2016_m_dimenhydrinate_and_erythema_multifore_5th:Conclusions_content "The majority of the assessed cases from Asian countries appear to be supportive of severe skin reactions after use of dimenhydrinate. This is supported by a reasonable time to onset, known genetic predisposition to SJS/ TEN of Thais, Han Chinese and Malays, and structural similarity between dimenhydrinate xanthine moiety and pamabrom, associated with EM in a case report. Furthermore, these cases were less confounded by concomitant medications and underlying conditions compared to cases from other countries. Because the predisposition is known for drugs other than dimenhydrinate, there could be a regional sensitivity to skin-related conditions that inflates the number of reports following the administration of a drug. Despite limitations, and as an adjunct to the guidance from the Thai FDA, it is advisable to inform health-care professionals in other countries as well of this suspected safety issue. Over-the-counter availability of dimenhydrinate can constitute a challenge in avoiding undesirable effects, as interaction between physicians or pharmacists and patients is reduced in favour of access to treatment, underlining the role of pharmacovigilance centres in communicating the responsible use of medicines and the availability of other antihistamines."^^xsd:string)

# Individual: X2016_m_dimenhydrinate_and_erythema_multifore_5th:DataAgainstCausalityForSJS (Data against causality for SJS)

AnnotationAssertion(rdfs:label X2016_m_dimenhydrinate_and_erythema_multifore_5th:DataAgainstCausalityForSJS "Data against causality for SJS"^^xsd:string)
ClassAssertion(obo:OAE_0001182 X2016_m_dimenhydrinate_and_erythema_multifore_5th:DataAgainstCausalityForSJS)
DataPropertyAssertion(OpenPVSignal:has_content X2016_m_dimenhydrinate_and_erythema_multifore_5th:DataAgainstCausalityForSJS "Although the two drugs were taken during the same time interval, reporter suspicion indicates that a role of dimenhydrinate cannot be completely excluded. In one instance, only paracetamol was considered a suspected drug and along with carbamazepine it would appear to be a more likely explanation for SJS.  "^^xsd:string)

