# Individual: X2016_m_dimenhydrinate_and_erythema_multifore_5th:posible_mechansim (possible mechanism)

AnnotationAssertion(rdfs:label X2016_m_dimenhydrinate_and_erythema_multifore_5th:posible_mechansim "possible mechanism"^^xsd:string)
ClassAssertion(OpenPVSignal:Adverse_Effect_Mechanism X2016_m_dimenhydrinate_and_erythema_multifore_5th:posible_mechansim)
ObjectPropertyAssertion(OpenPVSignal:refers_to_adverse_effect X2016_m_dimenhydrinate_and_erythema_multifore_5th:posible_mechansim X2016_m_dimenhydrinate_and_erythema_multifore_5th:SJS)
ObjectPropertyAssertion(OpenPVSignal:refers_to_adverse_effect X2016_m_dimenhydrinate_and_erythema_multifore_5th:posible_mechansim X2016_m_dimenhydrinate_and_erythema_multifore_5th:erythemaMultiforme)
ObjectPropertyAssertion(mp:references X2016_m_dimenhydrinate_and_erythema_multifore_5th:posible_mechansim X2016_m_dimenhydrinate_and_erythema_multifore_5th:Ref.13)
ObjectPropertyAssertion(mp:references X2016_m_dimenhydrinate_and_erythema_multifore_5th:posible_mechansim X2016_m_dimenhydrinate_and_erythema_multifore_5th:Ref.17)
ObjectPropertyAssertion(mp:references X2016_m_dimenhydrinate_and_erythema_multifore_5th:posible_mechansim X2016_m_dimenhydrinate_and_erythema_multifore_5th:Ref.18)
DataPropertyAssertion(OpenPVSignal:has_content X2016_m_dimenhydrinate_and_erythema_multifore_5th:posible_mechansim "Tan and Sklar13 suggested the 8- bromotheophylline moiety to have been responsible for erythema multiforme, and similarly it could be postulated that the 8- chlorotheophylline component in dimenhydrinate might have played a role in the development of either SJS or EM. In fact, both molecules are identical in their xanthine group and differ only in the halogen in position 8 (bromine or chlorine). Although there is no evidence that correlates xanthines with SJS or EM, there are two case reports of theophylline, another xanthine, and severe erythema multiforme and SJS.17,18"^^xsd:string)

# Individual: X2016_m_dimenhydrinate_and_erythema_multifore_5th:possibleReportingBias (possible reporting bias)

AnnotationAssertion(rdfs:label X2016_m_dimenhydrinate_and_erythema_multifore_5th:possibleReportingBias "possible reporting bias"^^xsd:string)
ClassAssertion(obo:OAE_0001182 X2016_m_dimenhydrinate_and_erythema_multifore_5th:possibleReportingBias)
DataPropertyAssertion(OpenPVSignal:has_content X2016_m_dimenhydrinate_and_erythema_multifore_5th:possibleReportingBias "As the predisposition to SJS/EM in some Asian populations is well-described, physicians could be more prone to diagnosing SJS/EM, or more inclined to report it. Thailand is, in VigiBase®, the main contributor to Continental Asia reports when it comes to these skin conditions (48% of Continental Asia reports) and Continental Asia adds 30% of the total reports with the MedDRA PT Stevens Johnson Syndrome alone, which may point to a reporting bias."^^xsd:string)

