# Individual: X2016_m_dimenhydrinate_and_erythema_multifore_5th:two_cases_from_literature (two cases from literature)

AnnotationAssertion(rdfs:label X2016_m_dimenhydrinate_and_erythema_multifore_5th:two_cases_from_literature "two cases from literature"^^xsd:string)
ClassAssertion(obo:OAE_0001197 X2016_m_dimenhydrinate_and_erythema_multifore_5th:two_cases_from_literature)
ObjectPropertyAssertion(OpenPVSignal:refers_to_adverse_effect X2016_m_dimenhydrinate_and_erythema_multifore_5th:two_cases_from_literature X2016_m_dimenhydrinate_and_erythema_multifore_5th:SJS)
ObjectPropertyAssertion(OpenPVSignal:refers_to_adverse_effect X2016_m_dimenhydrinate_and_erythema_multifore_5th:two_cases_from_literature X2016_m_dimenhydrinate_and_erythema_multifore_5th:erythemaMultiforme)
ObjectPropertyAssertion(OpenPVSignal:refers_to_drug X2016_m_dimenhydrinate_and_erythema_multifore_5th:two_cases_from_literature X2016_m_dimenhydrinate_and_erythema_multifore_5th:dimenhydrinate)
ObjectPropertyAssertion(mp:references X2016_m_dimenhydrinate_and_erythema_multifore_5th:two_cases_from_literature X2016_m_dimenhydrinate_and_erythema_multifore_5th:Ref.12)
ObjectPropertyAssertion(mp:references X2016_m_dimenhydrinate_and_erythema_multifore_5th:two_cases_from_literature X2016_m_dimenhydrinate_and_erythema_multifore_5th:Ref.13)
DataPropertyAssertion(OpenPVSignal:has_content X2016_m_dimenhydrinate_and_erythema_multifore_5th:two_cases_from_literature "A review of the literature highlighted two case reports of interest. The first one involves a young Iranian man, aged 17, who repeatedly complained of symptoms of SJS after administration of dimenhydrinate for motion sickness. The boy took the drug at least three times, in two instances the symptoms were mild, self-limiting and not systemic. However, in the third and last instance there appeared genital and mouth ulcers along with systemic reactions (itching, redness). The diagnosis of SJS was confirmed by biopsy and after a recommendation to avoid dimenhydrinate and a one-year follow-up there was no re-occurrence of the reaction.12 The second case concerns a 22-year-old female from China. The woman suffered from periorbital oedema and generalized rash after dimenhydrinate administration, worsening to erythema multiforme after treatment with chlorphenamine and hydroxyzine. On two occasions, she had taken paracetamol and pamabrom (8- bromotheophylline) and suffered from similar episodes. Allergic tests for paracetamol yielded negative results. The authors concluded that the theophylline moiety (pamabrom and 8- chlorotheophylline) may have triggered the reaction, because the patient had taken diphenhydramine and paracetamol separately on other occasions without any consequences.13"^^xsd:string)

