# Individual: X2016_m_denosumab_vasculitis_6th:ConclusionContent (Conclusion content)

AnnotationAssertion(rdfs:label X2016_m_denosumab_vasculitis_6th:ConclusionContent "Conclusion content"^^xsd:string)
ClassAssertion(OpenPVSignal:Conclusion X2016_m_denosumab_vasculitis_6th:ConclusionContent)
DataPropertyAssertion(OpenPVSignal:has_content X2016_m_denosumab_vasculitis_6th:ConclusionContent "In summary, there are 30 reports associating vasculitis with the use of denosumab. Denosumab was the only drug suspected in 29 of the 30 reports. Time to onset is consistent with a drug induced effect. Dechallenge is not particularly supportive of a drug association but for a drug such as denosumab which is administered every six months, the concept of drug withdrawal is not meaningful. Although the patients in this case series had considerable morbidity, there is little in the reports to indicate any other possible cause for vasculitis. It is possible that denosumab may cause vasculitis using a similar mechanism to that of TNF-α inhibitors. "^^xsd:string)

# Individual: X2016_m_denosumab_vasculitis_6th:DenosumabAndMusculoskeletalPain (Denosumab and musculoskeletal pain)

