# Individual: X2016_m_denosumab_vasculitis_6th:TimeToOnsetOfVasculitis (Time to onset of vasculitis)

AnnotationAssertion(rdfs:label X2016_m_denosumab_vasculitis_6th:TimeToOnsetOfVasculitis "Time to onset of vasculitis"^^xsd:string)
ClassAssertion(obo:OAE_0001197 X2016_m_denosumab_vasculitis_6th:TimeToOnsetOfVasculitis)
ObjectPropertyAssertion(mp:references X2016_m_denosumab_vasculitis_6th:TimeToOnsetOfVasculitis X2016_m_denosumab_vasculitis_6th:Ref.8)
DataPropertyAssertion(OpenPVSignal:has_content X2016_m_denosumab_vasculitis_6th:TimeToOnsetOfVasculitis "Time to onset was reported in only 10 of the reports and ranged from three days to nine months after the drug was administered with a median of about two months. This would appear consistent with a drug induced effect since drug induced vasculitis is an immune mediated reaction which would be expected to take weeks or months to develop. Indeed, one report in the literature has noted that vasculitis in association with antithyroid drugs had a time to onset with a range of 1 to 372 months  (median: 42 months). "^^xsd:string)

