ObjectPropertyAssertion(OpenPVSignal:refers_to_drug X2016_m_denosumab_vasculitis_6th:Uncommon_ADR_of_denosumab X2016_m_denosumab_vasculitis_6th:denosumab)
ObjectPropertyAssertion(mp:references X2016_m_denosumab_vasculitis_6th:Uncommon_ADR_of_denosumab X2016_m_denosumab_vasculitis_6th:Ref.1)
DataPropertyAssertion(OpenPVSignal:has_content X2016_m_denosumab_vasculitis_6th:Uncommon_ADR_of_denosumab "Uncommon cases of cellulitis; rare cases of hypocalcaemia, hypersensitivity, 
osteonecrosis of the jaw and atypical femoral fractures have been observed in patients taking denosumab.1"^^xsd:string)

# Individual: X2016_m_denosumab_vasculitis_6th:VasculitisManifestationInTheBody (Vasculitis manifestation in the body)

AnnotationAssertion(rdfs:label X2016_m_denosumab_vasculitis_6th:VasculitisManifestationInTheBody "Vasculitis manifestation in the body"^^xsd:string)
ClassAssertion(OpenPVSignal:Free_text_reporting_element X2016_m_denosumab_vasculitis_6th:VasculitisManifestationInTheBody)
ObjectPropertyAssertion(OpenPVSignal:refers_to_adverse_effect X2016_m_denosumab_vasculitis_6th:VasculitisManifestationInTheBody X2016_m_denosumab_vasculitis_6th:vasculitis)
ObjectPropertyAssertion(mp:references X2016_m_denosumab_vasculitis_6th:VasculitisManifestationInTheBody X2016_m_denosumab_vasculitis_6th:Ref.5)
DataPropertyAssertion(OpenPVSignal:has_content X2016_m_denosumab_vasculitis_6th:VasculitisManifestationInTheBody "Vasculitis and its consequences may be the primary or sole manifestation of a disease or alternatively, it may be a secondary component of another primary disease. Vasculitis may be confined to a single organ, such as the skin, or it may simultaneously involve several organ systems"^^xsd:string)

# Individual: X2016_m_denosumab_vasculitis_6th:VasculitisMechanism (Vasculitis pathophysiology)

AnnotationAssertion(rdfs:label X2016_m_denosumab_vasculitis_6th:VasculitisMechanism "Vasculitis pathophysiology"^^xsd:string)
ClassAssertion(OpenPVSignal:Free_text_reporting_element X2016_m_denosumab_vasculitis_6th:VasculitisMechanism)
ObjectPropertyAssertion(OpenPVSignal:refers_to_adverse_effect X2016_m_denosumab_vasculitis_6th:VasculitisMechanism X2016_m_denosumab_vasculitis_6th:vasculitis)
ObjectPropertyAssertion(mp:references X2016_m_denosumab_vasculitis_6th:VasculitisMechanism X2016_m_denosumab_vasculitis_6th:Ref.2)
DataPropertyAssertion(OpenPVSignal:has_content X2016_m_denosumab_vasculitis_6th:VasculitisMechanism "Vasculitis comprises a heterogeneous group of inflammatory vascular lesions that can involve any kind of blood vessel, irrespective of its lumen or location. Vasculitis gives rise to such conditions as ischaemia or thrombosis, which may cause serious organ damage and be life-threatening. Vasculitis is a necrotizing inflammatory lesion of blood vessels, leading to their occlusion or disruption, with clinical sequelae. The clinicopathological diagnosis of vasculitis is supported by the demonstration of elevated levels of acute-phase reactants (demonstrated by, for example, erythrocyte sedimentation rate, differential blood count showing thrombocytosis and leukocytosis, and C-reactiveprotein), high levels of rheumatoid factors and cryoglobulins, hypocomplementaemia, antinuclear antibodies (ANA), and anti-neutrophil cytoplasmic antibodies (ANCA) especially those ANCAs directed against proteinase 3 or myeloperoxidase.2"^^xsd:string)

# Individual: X2016_m_denosumab_vasculitis_6th:Vasculitis_and_TNFa_inhibitors (Mechanism of vasculitis and TNFa inhibitors)

AnnotationAssertion(rdfs:label X2016_m_denosumab_vasculitis_6th:Vasculitis_and_TNFa_inhibitors "Mechanism of vasculitis and TNFa inhibitors"^^xsd:string)
ClassAssertion(obo:OAE_0001197 X2016_m_denosumab_vasculitis_6th:Vasculitis_and_TNFa_inhibitors)
ClassAssertion(OpenPVSignal:Adverse_Effect_Mechanism X2016_m_denosumab_vasculitis_6th:Vasculitis_and_TNFa_inhibitors)
ObjectPropertyAssertion(OpenPVSignal:refers_to_adverse_effect X2016_m_denosumab_vasculitis_6th:Vasculitis_and_TNFa_inhibitors X2016_m_denosumab_vasculitis_6th:vasculitis)
ObjectPropertyAssertion(mp:references X2016_m_denosumab_vasculitis_6th:Vasculitis_and_TNFa_inhibitors X2016_m_denosumab_vasculitis_6th:Ref.10)
ObjectPropertyAssertion(mp:references X2016_m_denosumab_vasculitis_6th:Vasculitis_and_TNFa_inhibitors X2016_m_denosumab_vasculitis_6th:Ref.11)
ObjectPropertyAssertion(mp:references X2016_m_denosumab_vasculitis_6th:Vasculitis_and_TNFa_inhibitors X2016_m_denosumab_vasculitis_6th:Ref.12)
DataPropertyAssertion(OpenPVSignal:has_content X2016_m_denosumab_vasculitis_6th:Vasculitis_and_TNFa_inhibitors "There have been reports of vasculitis in association with tumour necrosis factor (TNF)-α inhibitors.10,11 In one of these reports, the authors suggested a relationship between the introduction of therapy with TNF-α inhibitors and anti-drug antibody production. The resulting immune complexes and recruitment of inflammatory mediators may lead to cutaneous vasculitis.10 In another report, the authors documented 233 cases of autoimmune disease associated with TNF-α inhibitors including 113 cases of vasculitis.11 Since RANKL is a member of the TNF superfamily, it is possible that denosumab may cause vasculitis through a similar mechanism.12"^^xsd:string)

