# Individual: X2016_m_etanecert_6th:Data_against_the_signal_causality_relationship (Data against the signal causality relationship)

AnnotationAssertion(rdfs:label X2016_m_etanecert_6th:Data_against_the_signal_causality_relationship "Data against the signal causality relationship"^^xsd:string)
ClassAssertion(obo:OAE_0001182 X2016_m_etanecert_6th:Data_against_the_signal_causality_relationship)
DataPropertyAssertion(OpenPVSignal:has_content X2016_m_etanecert_6th:Data_against_the_signal_causality_relationship "On the other hand, for the cases where either a wrong injection technique or local infection were reported, the likely explanation is that poor technique could have led first to infection and then to ulceration. As these patients are all adults, they are likely to self-inject the drug; more efforts should be put into providing patients with training."^^xsd:string)
DataPropertyAssertion(OpenPVSignal:has_content X2016_m_etanecert_6th:Data_against_the_signal_causality_relationship "Two cases are unlikely to be related to etanercept, as in one the reaction occurred at a shingle vaccine injection site, and in the other the reaction occurred before the therapy was started. "^^xsd:string)

# Individual: X2016_m_etanecert_6th:Discussion_and_Conclusion (Discussion and Conclusion)

AnnotationAssertion(rdfs:label X2016_m_etanecert_6th:Discussion_and_Conclusion "Discussion and Conclusion"^^xsd:string)
ClassAssertion(OpenPVSignal:Conclusion X2016_m_etanecert_6th:Discussion_and_Conclusion)
ClassAssertion(OpenPVSignal:Discussion X2016_m_etanecert_6th:Discussion_and_Conclusion)
ObjectPropertyAssertion(mp:references X2016_m_etanecert_6th:Discussion_and_Conclusion X2016_m_etanecert_6th:Ref.1)
ObjectPropertyAssertion(mp:references X2016_m_etanecert_6th:Discussion_and_Conclusion X2016_m_etanecert_6th:Ref.2)
ObjectPropertyAssertion(mp:references X2016_m_etanecert_6th:Discussion_and_Conclusion X2016_m_etanecert_6th:Ref.4)
ObjectPropertyAssertion(mp:references X2016_m_etanecert_6th:Discussion_and_Conclusion X2016_m_etanecert_6th:Ref.5)
DataPropertyAssertion(OpenPVSignal:has_content X2016_m_etanecert_6th:Discussion_and_Conclusion "In the light of the ability of this medication to cause vasculitis1 , together with the predisposition of the underlying disease4 , detailed information provided by the original reports for this combination are consistent with manifestations of cutaneous vasculitis.5 These findings would therefore strengthen the hypothesis that etanercept induced injection site reactions are immune-mediated.2 On the other hand, for the cases where either a wrong injection technique or local infection were reported, the likely explanation is that poor technique could have led first to infection and then to ulceration. As these patients are all adults, they are likely to self-inject the drug; more efforts should be put into providing patients with training."^^xsd:string)

