# Individual: X2017_m_Lamivudine_2017_1st:SmidonReference (Smidon reference)

AnnotationAssertion(rdfs:label X2017_m_Lamivudine_2017_1st:SmidonReference "Smidon reference"^^xsd:string)
ClassAssertion(obo:OAE_0001197 X2017_m_Lamivudine_2017_1st:SmidonReference)
ObjectPropertyAssertion(OpenPVSignal:refers_to_adverse_effect X2017_m_Lamivudine_2017_1st:SmidonReference X2017_m_Lamivudine_2017_1st:hearingLoss)
ObjectPropertyAssertion(OpenPVSignal:refers_to_class X2017_m_Lamivudine_2017_1st:SmidonReference X2017_m_Lamivudine_2017_1st:HAART)
ObjectPropertyAssertion(OpenPVSignal:refers_to_class X2017_m_Lamivudine_2017_1st:SmidonReference <http://purl.org/OpenPVSignal/Signals/2017_1_lamivudine_hearingDecreased.owl#Nucleoside/Nucleotide_Reverse_Transcriptase_Inhibitors_(NRTI_or_NtRTI)>)
ObjectPropertyAssertion(OpenPVSignal:refers_to_drug X2017_m_Lamivudine_2017_1st:SmidonReference X2017_m_Lamivudine_2017_1st:zidovudine)
ObjectPropertyAssertion(mp:references X2017_m_Lamivudine_2017_1st:SmidonReference X2017_m_Lamivudine_2017_1st:Ref.12)
DataPropertyAssertion(OpenPVSignal:has_content X2017_m_Lamivudine_2017_1st:SmidonReference "In 2001, Smidon et al. reported three cases of possible ototoxicity from NRTIs.12 In one of the cases the audiology record of a patient on zidovudine monotherapy (pre-HAART era) revealed a decline in hearing over a nine-year period from near upper limits of normal to severe bilateral deafness. There were no associated opportunistic infections though he had suffered from noise exposure a decade earlier"^^xsd:string)
DataPropertyAssertion(OpenPVSignal:has_content X2017_m_Lamivudine_2017_1st:SmidonReference "Smidon et al. was early to highlight this possibility in three case reports following ARTs. He noted confounding factors in the interpretation of the findings notably prior hearing loss from other causes including infections, history of noise exposure and older patients (≥35years)."^^xsd:string)

