# Individual: X2017_m_levothyroxin_2nd:informationForReport1 (information for report 1)

AnnotationAssertion(rdfs:label X2017_m_levothyroxin_2nd:informationForReport1 "information for report 1"^^xsd:string)
ClassAssertion(OpenPVSignal:Case_Report_Information X2017_m_levothyroxin_2nd:informationForReport1)
DataPropertyAssertion(OpenPVSignal:has_content X2017_m_levothyroxin_2nd:informationForReport1 "A woman of 48 years had been on stable  levothyroxine treatment for hypothyroidism for six years when she began to suffer from confusion,  impairment of memory and impairment of  concentration, along with restlessness, paranoia  and panic reactions. By her own account, she  stopped levothyroxine, upon which the symptoms  resolved. When she restarted treatment, the  symptoms returned "^^xsd:string)

# Individual: X2017_m_levothyroxin_2nd:informationForReport2 (information for report 2)

AnnotationAssertion(rdfs:label X2017_m_levothyroxin_2nd:informationForReport2 "information for report 2"^^xsd:string)
ClassAssertion(OpenPVSignal:Case_Report_Information X2017_m_levothyroxin_2nd:informationForReport2)
DataPropertyAssertion(OpenPVSignal:has_content X2017_m_levothyroxin_2nd:informationForReport2 "A woman of 50 years initiated levothyroxine  treatment for latent hypothyroidism. Within hours,  she suffered panic attacks, tremor, and unrest. She  was more than once admitted to hospital, and she  mentioned that her social life was almost  impossible. The dose was subsequently reduced,  and finally the therapy was discontinued leading to  regression of the symptoms. At a later stage the  medication was restarted with recurrence of the  adverse effects within a week after start of  treatment. She was then switched to drops and  recovered completely . "^^xsd:string)

# Individual: X2017_m_levothyroxin_2nd:informationForReport3 (information for report 3)

AnnotationAssertion(rdfs:label X2017_m_levothyroxin_2nd:informationForReport3 "information for report 3"^^xsd:string)
ClassAssertion(OpenPVSignal:Case_Report_Information X2017_m_levothyroxin_2nd:informationForReport3)
DataPropertyAssertion(OpenPVSignal:has_content X2017_m_levothyroxin_2nd:informationForReport3 "A woman of 28 years initiated levothyroxine  treatment and suffered gradual symptoms of  anxiety and panic attacks, to the point where  she described neglecting her job, and  eventually going on 50% sick leave. She also  lost weight from a BMI of 25 to 19. After more  than a year she herself associated the panic  attacks and anxiety with her levothyroxine  treatment and lowered the dose, after which all  reactions abated and had not since returned"^^xsd:string)

# Individual: X2017_m_levothyroxin_2nd:informationForReport4 (information for report 4)

AnnotationAssertion(rdfs:label X2017_m_levothyroxin_2nd:informationForReport4 "information for report 4"^^xsd:string)
ClassAssertion(OpenPVSignal:Case_Report_Information X2017_m_levothyroxin_2nd:informationForReport4)
DataPropertyAssertion(OpenPVSignal:has_content X2017_m_levothyroxin_2nd:informationForReport4 "A woman of 51 years suffered severe anxiety  and panic attacks, along with muscle pain,  cramps, and extreme tiredness, while on  levothyroxine. She suspected that her dose  was possibly too high, but the doctor had said  that her levels were normal. The symptoms  forced her to work part-time, reduce her  leisure activities, and seek help for depression. "^^xsd:string)

# Individual: X2017_m_levothyroxin_2nd:informationForReport5 (information for report 5)

AnnotationAssertion(rdfs:label X2017_m_levothyroxin_2nd:informationForReport5 "information for report 5"^^xsd:string)
ClassAssertion(OpenPVSignal:Case_Report_Information X2017_m_levothyroxin_2nd:informationForReport5)
DataPropertyAssertion(OpenPVSignal:has_content X2017_m_levothyroxin_2nd:informationForReport5 "A woman of unknown age had been on  levothyroxine treatment for two years and  suffered trembling inside, paraesthesia and  panic reactions. She suspected that the  symptoms might be caused by levothyroxine,  and consulted several physicians on the  matter, but felt that they did not pay attention  to the symptoms. Against their  recommendation, she temporarily stopped her  levothyroxine treatment on several occasions,  but always resumed therapy. The outcome of  these dechallenge and rechallenge  interventions was not reported"^^xsd:string)

