# Individual: X2017_m_sglt2_inhibitors_3rd:case_1_info (case 1 info)

AnnotationAssertion(rdfs:label X2017_m_sglt2_inhibitors_3rd:case_1_info "case 1 info"^^xsd:string)
ClassAssertion(OpenPVSignal:Case_Report_Information X2017_m_sglt2_inhibitors_3rd:case_1_info)
DataPropertyAssertion(OpenPVSignal:has_content X2017_m_sglt2_inhibitors_3rd:case_1_info "A 71 year old female with a history of type 2 diabetes and hypertension was initiated on empagliflozin. The patient was treated for cystitis approximately one month after starting therapy. Also, the patient experienced non-serious events of thrush, burning in the urogenital area, redness in the urogenital area, blistering in the urogenital area and hypoglycaemia. In the course of five days the itching increased up to intolerability. Therapy for the event of cystitis was antibiotics and antifungal cream; therapy of the symptoms in the urogenital area included unspecified ointments without success and a mild-cortisone containing ointment which helped slightly. Empagliflozin was discontinued."^^xsd:string)

# Individual: X2017_m_sglt2_inhibitors_3rd:case_2_info (case 2 info)

AnnotationAssertion(rdfs:label X2017_m_sglt2_inhibitors_3rd:case_2_info "case 2 info"^^xsd:string)
ClassAssertion(OpenPVSignal:Case_Report_Information X2017_m_sglt2_inhibitors_3rd:case_2_info)
DataPropertyAssertion(OpenPVSignal:has_content X2017_m_sglt2_inhibitors_3rd:case_2_info "A 60 year old female experienced severe itching, soreness, and reddening of the genital area and an inability to sit while on therapy with dapagliflozin. The patient was diagnosed with candidal mycosis and treated with antifungal cream. The cream did not bring improvement and the patient discontinued dapagliflozin “on her own” in response to the events."^^xsd:string)

