# Individual: X2017_m_pregabalin_3rd:TiagabineStudy (Tiagabine study)

AnnotationAssertion(rdfs:label X2017_m_pregabalin_3rd:TiagabineStudy "Tiagabine study"^^xsd:string)
ClassAssertion(obo:OAE_0001197 X2017_m_pregabalin_3rd:TiagabineStudy)
ObjectPropertyAssertion(OpenPVSignal:refers_to_adverse_effect X2017_m_pregabalin_3rd:TiagabineStudy X2017_m_pregabalin_3rd:defectiveColourVision)
ObjectPropertyAssertion(OpenPVSignal:refers_to_drug X2017_m_pregabalin_3rd:TiagabineStudy X2017_m_pregabalin_3rd:tiagabine)
ObjectPropertyAssertion(mp:references X2017_m_pregabalin_3rd:TiagabineStudy X2017_m_pregabalin_3rd:Ref.11)
DataPropertyAssertion(OpenPVSignal:has_content X2017_m_pregabalin_3rd:TiagabineStudy "In another study, the effects of the GABA-ergic antiepileptic drug (AED), tiagabine, on colour vision and contrast sensitivity was investigated. Twenty newly-diagnosed patients with partial epilepsy (aged 19-72 years), receiving tiagabine as their initial monotherapy for 5-41 months were examined. Three patients were excluded from the colour vision evaluation for congenital red-green colour vision defects. Seven out of 17 patients (41%) had acquired colour vision deficit. This study suggests that AED therapy with tiagabine, as with other established and newer AEDs may interfere with colour perception "^^xsd:string)

