DataPropertyAssertion(OpenPVSignal:has_content X2017_m_ruxolitinib_4th:Litrerature_and_Labelling "Neuropathy is not described in current ruxolitinib drug labels1,4 and no literature reports on peripheral neuropathy have been found for ruxolitinib."^^xsd:string)

# Individual: X2017_m_ruxolitinib_4th:Mechanism_of_ruxolitinib (Mechanism of ruxolitinib)

AnnotationAssertion(rdfs:label X2017_m_ruxolitinib_4th:Mechanism_of_ruxolitinib "Mechanism of ruxolitinib"^^xsd:string)
ClassAssertion(OpenPVSignal:Mechanism X2017_m_ruxolitinib_4th:Mechanism_of_ruxolitinib)
ObjectPropertyAssertion(mp:references X2017_m_ruxolitinib_4th:Mechanism_of_ruxolitinib X2017_m_ruxolitinib_4th:Ref.1)
ObjectPropertyAssertion(mp:references X2017_m_ruxolitinib_4th:Mechanism_of_ruxolitinib X2017_m_ruxolitinib_4th:Ref.2)
ObjectPropertyAssertion(mp:references X2017_m_ruxolitinib_4th:Mechanism_of_ruxolitinib X2017_m_ruxolitinib_4th:Ref.3)
DataPropertyAssertion(OpenPVSignal:has_content X2017_m_ruxolitinib_4th:Mechanism_of_ruxolitinib "Ruxolitinib (INCB018424) is a selective inhibitor of the Janus Associated Kinases (JAKs) 1 and 2. These mediate the signalling of a number of cytokines and growth factors that are important for haematopoiesis and immune function1 Ruxolitinib has significant clinical benefits in patients with myelofibrosis by reducing spleen size, ameliorating debilitating myelofibrosis-related symptoms, and improving overall survival.2 Ruxolitinib has also been demonstrated to be superior to standard therapy in controlling the hematocrit, reducing the spleen volume, and improving symptoms associated with polycythemia vera.3"^^xsd:string)

