AnnotationAssertion(OpenPVSignal:has_MedDRA_prefered_term X2017_m_amitriptyline_5th:dryEyes "Dry eye"^^xsd:string)
AnnotationAssertion(rdfs:label X2017_m_amitriptyline_5th:dryEyes "dry eyes"^^xsd:string)
ClassAssertion(OpenPVSignal:Adverse_Effect X2017_m_amitriptyline_5th:dryEyes)

# Individual: X2017_m_amitriptyline_5th:introduction (introduction)

AnnotationAssertion(rdfs:label X2017_m_amitriptyline_5th:introduction "introduction"^^xsd:string)
ClassAssertion(OpenPVSignal:Introduction X2017_m_amitriptyline_5th:introduction)
DataPropertyAssertion(OpenPVSignal:has_content X2017_m_amitriptyline_5th:introduction "Amitriptyline belongs to the class of tricyclic antidepressants and is used for the treatment of depression, anxiety and chronic pain. It has anticholinergic effects, inhibiting the neurotransmitter acetylcholine present in the central and peripheral nervous systems. This inhibition has effects on several autonomous functions such as decreased saliva production, decreased mucus production in the nose and throat, decreased sweating, increased body temperature, dilation of the pupils and reduced bowel movements. As well as these effects, there is also the reduced production of tears, causing the eyes to feel dry.1"^^xsd:string)

