# Individual: X2017_m_natalizumab_6th:Proposed_mechanism_behind_natalizumab_and_CNSL (Proposed mechanism behind natalizumab and CNSL)

AnnotationAssertion(rdfs:label X2017_m_natalizumab_6th:Proposed_mechanism_behind_natalizumab_and_CNSL "Proposed mechanism behind natalizumab and CNSL"^^xsd:string)
ClassAssertion(OpenPVSignal:Adverse_Effect_Mechanism X2017_m_natalizumab_6th:Proposed_mechanism_behind_natalizumab_and_CNSL)
ObjectPropertyAssertion(OpenPVSignal:refers_to_unconfirmed_adverse_effect X2017_m_natalizumab_6th:Proposed_mechanism_behind_natalizumab_and_CNSL <http://purl.org/OpenPVSignal/Signals/2017_6_natalizumab_centralNervousSystemLymphoma.owl#centralNervousSystemLymphoma(cnsl)>)
DataPropertyAssertion(OpenPVSignal:has_content X2017_m_natalizumab_6th:Proposed_mechanism_behind_natalizumab_and_CNSL "This could be supported by the mechanism through which natalizumab exerts therapeutic action, which might also make it a promoter of malignant cell growth by reducing CNS immunosurveillance.  Within the case series, the original extract of case 10 reports a rapid growth of a previously identified lesion after two infusions of natalizumab, compatible with the history of the case presented by Phan Ba et al."^^xsd:string)

