# Individual: X2018_m_ciprofloxacin_1st_2018:AKI_pathophysiology (AKI pathophysiology)

AnnotationAssertion(rdfs:label X2018_m_ciprofloxacin_1st_2018:AKI_pathophysiology "AKI pathophysiology"^^xsd:string)
ClassAssertion(OpenPVSignal:Free_text_reporting_element X2018_m_ciprofloxacin_1st_2018:AKI_pathophysiology)
ObjectPropertyAssertion(OpenPVSignal:refers_to_adverse_effect X2018_m_ciprofloxacin_1st_2018:AKI_pathophysiology X2018_m_ciprofloxacin_1st_2018:acuteKidneyInjury)
DataPropertyAssertion(OpenPVSignal:has_content X2018_m_ciprofloxacin_1st_2018:AKI_pathophysiology "A range of pre-renal, renal and post-renal clinical conditions can lead to AKI. Drugs can be involved at any of these levels and so may cause conditions leading to pre-renal injury by volume depletion e.g. through haemorrhage or dehydration, or through a direct effect on glomerular arteriolar pressures. Drug-induced direct renal toxicity e.g. due to interstitial nephritis or acute tubular necrosis is well-recognised. Promotion of renal stone formation can lead to post-renal obstruction and AKI."^^xsd:string)

