AnnotationAssertion(rdfs:label X2018_m_ciprofloxacin_1st_2018:Mechanism_of_Enalapril "Mechanism of Enalapril"^^xsd:string)
ClassAssertion(OpenPVSignal:Mechanism X2018_m_ciprofloxacin_1st_2018:Mechanism_of_Enalapril)
ObjectPropertyAssertion(OpenPVSignal:is_part_of X2018_m_ciprofloxacin_1st_2018:Mechanism_of_Enalapril X2018_m_ciprofloxacin_1st_2018:introduction)
DataPropertyAssertion(OpenPVSignal:has_content X2018_m_ciprofloxacin_1st_2018:Mechanism_of_Enalapril "Enalapril is an angiotensin converting enzyme (ACE) inhibitor used to reduce blood pressure and treat cardiac failure. ACE inhibitors decrease the production of angiotensin II, a substance which causes post-glomerular arteriolar constriction thus maintaining glomerular capillary filtration."^^xsd:string)

# Individual: X2018_m_ciprofloxacin_1st_2018:Mechanism_of_renal_toxicity (Mechanism of enalapril and renal toxicity)

AnnotationAssertion(rdfs:label X2018_m_ciprofloxacin_1st_2018:Mechanism_of_renal_toxicity "Mechanism of enalapril and renal toxicity"^^xsd:string)
ClassAssertion(OpenPVSignal:Adverse_Effect_Mechanism X2018_m_ciprofloxacin_1st_2018:Mechanism_of_renal_toxicity)
ObjectPropertyAssertion(OpenPVSignal:refers_to_adverse_effect X2018_m_ciprofloxacin_1st_2018:Mechanism_of_renal_toxicity X2018_m_ciprofloxacin_1st_2018:renal_failure)
ObjectPropertyAssertion(mp:references X2018_m_ciprofloxacin_1st_2018:Mechanism_of_renal_toxicity X2018_m_ciprofloxacin_1st_2018:Ref.4)
DataPropertyAssertion(OpenPVSignal:has_content X2018_m_ciprofloxacin_1st_2018:Mechanism_of_renal_toxicity "ACE inhibitors decrease the production of angiotensin II, a substance which causes post-glomerular arteriolar constriction thus maintaining glomerular capillary filtration. Usually pre-glomerular arteriolar pressures are high enough for adequate filtration in the presence of ACE inhibition but drugs and clinical conditions that affect renal blood flow and pre-glomerular arteriolar pressures may trigger renal failure in patients taking ACE inhibitors These include concomitant use of loop, thiazide or potassium-sparing diuretics, and prostaglandin inhibitors (NSAIDs), renal artery stenosis, renal transplant, old age, ischaemic heart disease and congestive heart failure, sodium restriction, sodium depletion, volume depletion, hypotension and gastrointestinal fluid loss.4"^^xsd:string)

