# Individual: X2018_m_ciprofloxacin_1st_2018:lomaestro_review (lomaestro review)

AnnotationAssertion(rdfs:label X2018_m_ciprofloxacin_1st_2018:lomaestro_review "lomaestro review"^^xsd:string)
ClassAssertion(obo:OAE_0001197 X2018_m_ciprofloxacin_1st_2018:lomaestro_review)
ObjectPropertyAssertion(OpenPVSignal:refers_to_adverse_effect X2018_m_ciprofloxacin_1st_2018:lomaestro_review X2018_m_ciprofloxacin_1st_2018:nephrotoxicity)
ObjectPropertyAssertion(OpenPVSignal:refers_to_class X2018_m_ciprofloxacin_1st_2018:lomaestro_review X2018_m_ciprofloxacin_1st_2018:fluroquinolones)
ObjectPropertyAssertion(mp:references X2018_m_ciprofloxacin_1st_2018:lomaestro_review X2018_m_ciprofloxacin_1st_2018:Ref.2)
DataPropertyAssertion(OpenPVSignal:has_content X2018_m_ciprofloxacin_1st_2018:lomaestro_review "Lomaestro2 conducted a literature review to ascertain the incidence and characteristics of fluoroquinolone-related nephrotoxicity. Publications were mostly case reports and the incidence was difficult to estimate. Nearly all of the 44 reports of acute renal failure identified involved patients aged over 50 years. The most frequently reported pathology was acute interstitial nephritis. A high proportion of patients were taking other nephrotoxic medicines, particularly chemotherapeutic and immunosuppressive agents. One patient was taking an ACE inhibitor."^^xsd:string)

