# Individual: X2018_ivermectin_1st:Ivermectin_mechanism (Ivermectin mechanism)

AnnotationAssertion(rdfs:label X2018_ivermectin_1st:Ivermectin_mechanism "Ivermectin mechanism"^^xsd:string)
ClassAssertion(OpenPVSignal:Mechanism X2018_ivermectin_1st:Ivermectin_mechanism)
ObjectPropertyAssertion(mp:references X2018_ivermectin_1st:Ivermectin_mechanism X2018_ivermectin_1st:Ref.3)
DataPropertyAssertion(OpenPVSignal:has_content X2018_ivermectin_1st:Ivermectin_mechanism "Ivermectin acts by binding to glutamate-gated chloride ion channels which occur in invertebrate nerve and muscle cells; an increase in the permeability of the cell membrane results in paralysis and death of the parasite. It can also bind to mammalian GABA receptors and GABA-gated ion channels; however, neurotoxicity is prevented by the action of the P-glycoprotein drug pump (mdr-1) which limits penetration of the blood- brain barrier within the allowable dosage ranges for humans"^^xsd:string)

