# Individual: X2018_m_Quetiapine_2nd:CaseReportInfo1 (Case report info 1)

AnnotationAssertion(rdfs:label X2018_m_Quetiapine_2nd:CaseReportInfo1 "Case report info 1"^^xsd:string)
ClassAssertion(OpenPVSignal:Case_Report_Information X2018_m_Quetiapine_2nd:CaseReportInfo1)
DataPropertyAssertion(OpenPVSignal:has_content X2018_m_Quetiapine_2nd:CaseReportInfo1 "In  case 1, the reporter concluded that the patient  was predisposed to valproic acid  hepatotoxicity on the basis of repeated  positive rechallenges, and that quetiapine was  responsible for the CPK increase. After  withdrawal of valproate, the patient recovered  from hepatic complications, after quetiapine  dechallenge his CPK went back to normal."^^xsd:string)
DataPropertyAssertion(OpenPVSignal:has_content X2018_m_Quetiapine_2nd:CaseReportInfo1 "Literature reference: Erdogan et al. VA levels: 50 mg/l, thyroid function normal.
AST, ALT, LDH elevation linked to VA, while CPK and CPK-MB increase to Q.
History of hepatic enzyme increases while on VA and CPK increase on Q. VA
withdrawn first, with lowering of hepatic enzymes. Followed by increase in CPK
after Q dose was raised to 400 mg/day. Q then discontinued and CPK values back to normal."^^xsd:string)

# Individual: X2018_m_Quetiapine_2nd:CaseReportInfo10 (Case report info 10)

AnnotationAssertion(rdfs:label X2018_m_Quetiapine_2nd:CaseReportInfo10 "Case report info 10"^^xsd:string)
ClassAssertion(OpenPVSignal:Case_Report_Information X2018_m_Quetiapine_2nd:CaseReportInfo10)
DataPropertyAssertion(OpenPVSignal:has_content X2018_m_Quetiapine_2nd:CaseReportInfo10 "Cases which did  not co-report any of the above discussed  conditions are 9 and 10, both describing a  decrease in consciousness. Both could be  quetiapine dose-related: the first reports a prescribed overdose, and the second an unintentional four-fold overdose due to lack of patient adherence."^^xsd:string)
DataPropertyAssertion(OpenPVSignal:has_content X2018_m_Quetiapine_2nd:CaseReportInfo10 "Hospitalized due to fever and suspected
pneumonia, treated with levofloxacin.
Antipsychotic regimen had not been taken by
patient and was started during hospital stay."^^xsd:string)

# Individual: X2018_m_Quetiapine_2nd:CaseReportInfo11 (Case report info 11)

AnnotationAssertion(rdfs:label X2018_m_Quetiapine_2nd:CaseReportInfo11 "Case report info 11"^^xsd:string)
ClassAssertion(OpenPVSignal:Case_Report_Information X2018_m_Quetiapine_2nd:CaseReportInfo11)
DataPropertyAssertion(OpenPVSignal:has_content X2018_m_Quetiapine_2nd:CaseReportInfo11 "In another patient (case 11), depressed consciousness co-occurred with gait disturbances and around the same time of a quetiapine dose increase. The reported off-label indication was depression, and the incremental dosing occurred according to the label. "^^xsd:string)
DataPropertyAssertion(OpenPVSignal:has_content X2018_m_Quetiapine_2nd:CaseReportInfo11 "The overdose was not intentional but reported
by the patient as she considered her physician
to be overdosing her."^^xsd:string)

# Individual: X2018_m_Quetiapine_2nd:CaseReportInfo12 (Case report info 12)

AnnotationAssertion(rdfs:label X2018_m_Quetiapine_2nd:CaseReportInfo12 "Case report info 12"^^xsd:string)
ClassAssertion(OpenPVSignal:Case_Report_Information X2018_m_Quetiapine_2nd:CaseReportInfo12)
DataPropertyAssertion(OpenPVSignal:has_content X2018_m_Quetiapine_2nd:CaseReportInfo12 "Case 12 reports pseudoparkinsonism induced by increased plasma levels of quetiapine."^^xsd:string)
DataPropertyAssertion(OpenPVSignal:has_content X2018_m_Quetiapine_2nd:CaseReportInfo12 "Literature reference: De Dios et al. Cortical-subcortical atrophy. VA: 78 mg/l after
events."^^xsd:string)

# Individual: X2018_m_Quetiapine_2nd:CaseReportInfo13 (Case report info 13)

AnnotationAssertion(rdfs:label X2018_m_Quetiapine_2nd:CaseReportInfo13 "Case report info 13"^^xsd:string)
ClassAssertion(OpenPVSignal:Case_Report_Information X2018_m_Quetiapine_2nd:CaseReportInfo13)
DataPropertyAssertion(OpenPVSignal:has_content X2018_m_Quetiapine_2nd:CaseReportInfo13 "History: benign prostatic hyperplasia, lacunar
infarction, nervous system disorder NOS,
cerebral degeneration, emergency care,
hospitalization, chronic kidney disease.
Q was added on VA and lithium.
VA dose brought up from 900 mg per day to
1600 mg per day on the day Q was started.
Q: 283 mcg/l (reference:
70-170 mcg/l); VA within therapeutic levels;
aripiprazole below therapeutic levels."^^xsd:string)
DataPropertyAssertion(OpenPVSignal:has_content X2018_m_Quetiapine_2nd:CaseReportInfo13 "Similarly, case 13 lists parkinsonism and depressed consciousness, attributed to a pharmacokinetic interaction leading to increased quetiapine plasma levels and a recovery after dose reduction."^^xsd:string)

# Individual: X2018_m_Quetiapine_2nd:CaseReportInfo17 (Case report info 17)

AnnotationAssertion(rdfs:label X2018_m_Quetiapine_2nd:CaseReportInfo17 "Case report info 17"^^xsd:string)
ClassAssertion(OpenPVSignal:Case_Report_Information X2018_m_Quetiapine_2nd:CaseReportInfo17)
ObjectPropertyAssertion(mp:references X2018_m_Quetiapine_2nd:CaseReportInfo17 X2018_m_Quetiapine_2nd:Ref.17)
DataPropertyAssertion(OpenPVSignal:has_content X2018_m_Quetiapine_2nd:CaseReportInfo17 "Alternatively, valproic acid  encephalopathy can also reasonably explain  decreased consciousness and coma. Valproic  acid metabolites can inhibit the urea cycle and  cause hyperammonemia, as in case 17. 17"^^xsd:string)
DataPropertyAssertion(OpenPVSignal:has_content X2018_m_Quetiapine_2nd:CaseReportInfo17 "Literature reference: Erling et al.
Hyperammonemic coma due to VA. VA:
756 mcmol/l (no reference provided but
above therapeutic)."^^xsd:string)

# Individual: X2018_m_Quetiapine_2nd:CaseReportInfo18 (Case report info 18)

AnnotationAssertion(rdfs:label X2018_m_Quetiapine_2nd:CaseReportInfo18 "Case report info 18"^^xsd:string)
ClassAssertion(OpenPVSignal:Case_Report_Information X2018_m_Quetiapine_2nd:CaseReportInfo18)
DataPropertyAssertion(OpenPVSignal:has_content X2018_m_Quetiapine_2nd:CaseReportInfo18 "Literature reference: Wu et al.
Coma/depressed consciousness due to
hyperglycaemia (high- sugar dieting habits).
Patient without history of diabetes."^^xsd:string)
DataPropertyAssertion(OpenPVSignal:has_content X2018_m_Quetiapine_2nd:CaseReportInfo18 "Wu  et al. (case 18) suggest that the patient’s  hyperglycaemic coma was promoted by high  dose quetiapine and possibly complicated by  valproic acid co-administration, but worsened  by high sugar consumption."^^xsd:string)

# Individual: X2018_m_Quetiapine_2nd:CaseReportInfo19 (Case report info 19)

AnnotationAssertion(rdfs:label X2018_m_Quetiapine_2nd:CaseReportInfo19 "Case report info 19"^^xsd:string)
ClassAssertion(OpenPVSignal:Case_Report_Information X2018_m_Quetiapine_2nd:CaseReportInfo19)
DataPropertyAssertion(OpenPVSignal:has_content X2018_m_Quetiapine_2nd:CaseReportInfo19 "VA introduced after 11 days of Q use. Q can
increase plasma concentration of lithium."^^xsd:string)

# Individual: X2018_m_Quetiapine_2nd:CaseReportInfo2 (Case report info 2)

AnnotationAssertion(rdfs:label X2018_m_Quetiapine_2nd:CaseReportInfo2 "Case report info 2"^^xsd:string)
ClassAssertion(OpenPVSignal:Case_Report_Information X2018_m_Quetiapine_2nd:CaseReportInfo2)
DataPropertyAssertion(OpenPVSignal:has_content X2018_m_Quetiapine_2nd:CaseReportInfo2 "Literature reference: Reiche et al.
Suspected interaction between VA and
pipamperone as well as between VA and
Q. Q levels below therapeutic: 25 ng/ml
(reference 70-170 ng/ml), VA levels within
therapeutic range: 46 mcg/ml (reference 30-
100 mcg/ml)."^^xsd:string)
DataPropertyAssertion(OpenPVSignal:has_content X2018_m_Quetiapine_2nd:CaseReportInfo2 "Reiche et al. (case 2) suggest a blood CPK  increase caused by valproic acid resulting from  prolonged clearance due to interaction with  concomitant pipamperone. They do not,  however, exclude the possibility of a  pharmacodynamic interaction between valproic  acid and quetiapine, adding that quetiapine  was below therapeutic levels at admission to  hospital."^^xsd:string)

# Individual: X2018_m_Quetiapine_2nd:CaseReportInfo20 (Case report info 20)

AnnotationAssertion(rdfs:label X2018_m_Quetiapine_2nd:CaseReportInfo20 "Case report info 20"^^xsd:string)
ClassAssertion(OpenPVSignal:Case_Report_Information X2018_m_Quetiapine_2nd:CaseReportInfo20)
DataPropertyAssertion(OpenPVSignal:has_content X2018_m_Quetiapine_2nd:CaseReportInfo20 "Possible error in reporting VA dose (mg instead
of grams)."^^xsd:string)

# Individual: X2018_m_Quetiapine_2nd:CaseReportInfo4 (Case report info 4)

AnnotationAssertion(rdfs:label X2018_m_Quetiapine_2nd:CaseReportInfo4 "Case report info 4"^^xsd:string)
ClassAssertion(OpenPVSignal:Case_Report_Information X2018_m_Quetiapine_2nd:CaseReportInfo4)
DataPropertyAssertion(OpenPVSignal:has_content X2018_m_Quetiapine_2nd:CaseReportInfo4 "In case 4, a quetiapine valproate pharmacokinetic interaction  was suspected to have induced rhabdomyolysis as  part of an abortive NMS form. The patient’s  symptoms began with neck stiffness, which  resembles a cervical dystonia literature case,  suspected to have been a pharmacokinetic  interaction between quetiapine and valproic  acid. 23 "^^xsd:string)
DataPropertyAssertion(OpenPVSignal:has_content X2018_m_Quetiapine_2nd:CaseReportInfo4 "Literature reference: Jahn et al.
Suspect of abortive neuroleptic malignant
syndrome with fever (37.9 C), tremor in
extremities. VA 82.4 mg/l."^^xsd:string)

# Individual: X2018_m_Quetiapine_2nd:CaseReportInfo5 (Case report info 5)

