DataPropertyAssertion(OpenPVSignal:has_content X2018_m_Quetiapine_2nd:CaseReportInfo8 "Acute cholecystitis. Developed reactions after
surgery, lithium- induced diabetes insipidus
pre-existing, hypernatraemia due to
decreased consciousness and subsequent
reduced liquids intake. Recent increase of Q."^^xsd:string)
DataPropertyAssertion(OpenPVSignal:has_content X2018_m_Quetiapine_2nd:CaseReportInfo8 "In case 8, extrapyramidal symptoms and depressed level of consciousness are co-reported after quetiapine dose increase"^^xsd:string)

# Individual: X2018_m_Quetiapine_2nd:CaseReportInfo9 (Case report info 9)

AnnotationAssertion(rdfs:label X2018_m_Quetiapine_2nd:CaseReportInfo9 "Case report info 9"^^xsd:string)
ClassAssertion(OpenPVSignal:Case_Report_Information X2018_m_Quetiapine_2nd:CaseReportInfo9)
DataPropertyAssertion(OpenPVSignal:has_content X2018_m_Quetiapine_2nd:CaseReportInfo9 "Cases which did  not co-report any of the above discussed  conditions are 9 and 10, both describing a  decrease in consciousness. Both could be  quetiapine dose-related: the first reports a prescribed overdose, and the second an unintentional four-fold overdose due to lack of patient adherence."^^xsd:string)
DataPropertyAssertion(OpenPVSignal:has_content X2018_m_Quetiapine_2nd:CaseReportInfo9 "Q above studied doses. Q at 191 ng/ml
(reference 70-170 ng/ ml). VA at 11.2
mcg/ml (reference 50-100 mcg/ml).
Reactions occurred at the day of peak Q
concentration. VA was introduced the same
day. Perazine cannot be excluded, but was
introduced five days before valproate"^^xsd:string)

