# Individual: X2018_m_Agomelatine_4rth_2018:introduction (introduction)

AnnotationAssertion(rdfs:label X2018_m_Agomelatine_4rth_2018:introduction "introduction"^^xsd:string)
ClassAssertion(OpenPVSignal:Introduction X2018_m_Agomelatine_4rth_2018:introduction)
ObjectPropertyAssertion(mp:references X2018_m_Agomelatine_4rth_2018:introduction X2018_m_Agomelatine_4rth_2018:Ref.1)
ObjectPropertyAssertion(mp:references X2018_m_Agomelatine_4rth_2018:introduction X2018_m_Agomelatine_4rth_2018:Ref.2)
DataPropertyAssertion(OpenPVSignal:has_content X2018_m_Agomelatine_4rth_2018:introduction "Agomelatine is a MT1 and MT2 melatonin receptor agonist, and a serotonin (5-HT2c) antagonist. It is approved in Europe, Australia and Latin America for the treatment of major depression in adults. The efficacy and safety of agomelatine have been established in elderly depressed patients over 75 years of age, but clinical data showed no effect. Therefore, agomelatine should not be used by patients older than 75 years. The recommended dose is 25 mg once daily taken orally at bedtime. If there is no improvement of symptoms after a couple of weeks, the dose may be increased to 50 mg once daily, i.e. two 25 mg tablets taken at the same time at bedtime.1,2"^^xsd:string)

