DataPropertyAssertion(OpenPVSignal:has_content X2018_m_desogestrel_2018_5th:Panic_attack_pathophysiology "According to the Diagnostic and Statistical Manual of Mental Disorders, Fifth Edition (DSM-5), a panic attack is defined as a discrete period of intense fear or discomfort, often accompanied by physical symptoms such as palpitations and trembling. Experiencing repeated, consistent panic attacks that get in the way of everyday functioning is considered a defining symptom of panic disorder.2"^^xsd:string)

