# Individual: X2018_m_desogestrel_2018_5th:Suicidal_ideation_pathophysiology (Suicidal ideation pathophysiology)

AnnotationAssertion(rdfs:label X2018_m_desogestrel_2018_5th:Suicidal_ideation_pathophysiology "Suicidal ideation pathophysiology"^^xsd:string)
ClassAssertion(OpenPVSignal:Free_text_reporting_element X2018_m_desogestrel_2018_5th:Suicidal_ideation_pathophysiology)
ObjectPropertyAssertion(OpenPVSignal:refers_to_adverse_effect X2018_m_desogestrel_2018_5th:Suicidal_ideation_pathophysiology X2018_m_desogestrel_2018_5th:SuicidalIdeation)
ObjectPropertyAssertion(mp:references X2018_m_desogestrel_2018_5th:Suicidal_ideation_pathophysiology X2018_m_desogestrel_2018_5th:Ref.3)
DataPropertyAssertion(OpenPVSignal:has_content X2018_m_desogestrel_2018_5th:Suicidal_ideation_pathophysiology "Suicidal ideation could be translated to thoughts of harming oneself or bringing about one’s own death and is most closely associated with major depression or chronic dysphoria. The prevalence is highest among adolescents and the elderly. Among adolescents it is approximately 12%. Symptoms and signs include depression, poor sleep, anxiety, decreased appetite and mood changes. Among adolescents who experience thoughts of suicide, girls and young women suffer about twice as often as boys. About one in three persons who have suicidal ideations actually tries to commit suicide.3"^^xsd:string)

