# Individual: X2018_m_edoxaban_5th_2018:introduction (introduction)

AnnotationAssertion(rdfs:label X2018_m_edoxaban_5th_2018:introduction "introduction"^^xsd:string)
ClassAssertion(OpenPVSignal:Introduction X2018_m_edoxaban_5th_2018:introduction)
ObjectPropertyAssertion(mp:references X2018_m_edoxaban_5th_2018:introduction X2018_m_edoxaban_5th_2018:Ref.1)
DataPropertyAssertion(OpenPVSignal:has_content X2018_m_edoxaban_5th_2018:introduction "Edoxaban is an anti-coagulant drug indicated to prevent thromboembolic disease in patients diagnosed with atrial fibrillation, including one or more risk factors such as history of stroke or transient ischaemic attack, age 75 years or older, diabetes mellitus or hypertension. The drug is also approved for treatment of deep vein thrombosis and pulmonary embolism.1  The recommended dose differs according to the indication but ranges between 30 mg and 60 mg once a day. In patients with body weight lower than 60 kg, or taking P-glycoprotein inhibiting drugs , such as ciclosporin, dronedarone, erythromycin, ketoconazole, or suffering from moderate or severe renal impairment, the dose should be reduced to 30 mg daily"^^xsd:string)

