# Individual: X2018_m_Aflibercept_6th_2018:Pharmacokinetics_of_aflibercept_intravitrial_administration (Pharmacokinetics of aflibercept intravitrial administration)

AnnotationAssertion(rdfs:label X2018_m_Aflibercept_6th_2018:Pharmacokinetics_of_aflibercept_intravitrial_administration "Pharmacokinetics of aflibercept intravitrial administration"^^xsd:string)
ClassAssertion(OpenPVSignal:Mechanism X2018_m_Aflibercept_6th_2018:Pharmacokinetics_of_aflibercept_intravitrial_administration)
ObjectPropertyAssertion(mp:references X2018_m_Aflibercept_6th_2018:Pharmacokinetics_of_aflibercept_intravitrial_administration X2018_m_Aflibercept_6th_2018:Ref.1)
DataPropertyAssertion(OpenPVSignal:has_content X2018_m_Aflibercept_6th_2018:Pharmacokinetics_of_aflibercept_intravitrial_administration "In the ocular indications, aflibercept is administered intravitreally as a 2 mg dose, to be repeated every month for three consecutive months, followed by 
every other month.
The product labelling of aflibercept presents data on the pharmacokinetics of intravitreal administration. With a dose of 2 mg per eye, the mean plasma Cmax was 0.02 mcg/mL which was reached within 1 to 3 days, while the aflibercept:VEGF complex concentrations reach a Cmax of 0.186 mcg/mL within 14 to 28 days of a 2 mg dose. Aflibercept did not accumulate in the plasma with repeated intravitreal dosing every 4 weeks"^^xsd:string)

