# Individual: X2018_m_ceftriaxone_2018_6th:Mechanism_of_ceftriaxone (Mechanism of ceftriaxone)

AnnotationAssertion(rdfs:label X2018_m_ceftriaxone_2018_6th:Mechanism_of_ceftriaxone "Mechanism of ceftriaxone"^^xsd:string)
ClassAssertion(OpenPVSignal:Mechanism X2018_m_ceftriaxone_2018_6th:Mechanism_of_ceftriaxone)
DataPropertyAssertion(OpenPVSignal:has_content X2018_m_ceftriaxone_2018_6th:Mechanism_of_ceftriaxone "Ceftriaxone is a cephalosporin antibiotic which inhibits bacterial cell wall synthesis following attachment to PBPs. This results in the interruption of cell wall (peptidoglycan) biosynthesis, which leads to bacterial cell lysis and death. It is used in the treatment of a large variety of infections ."^^xsd:string)

