# Individual: X2019_m_levofloxacin_1st:Impaired_renal_function_and_levofloxacin (Impaired renal function and levofloxacin)

AnnotationAssertion(rdfs:label X2019_m_levofloxacin_1st:Impaired_renal_function_and_levofloxacin "Impaired renal function and levofloxacin"^^xsd:string)
ClassAssertion(OpenPVSignal:Adverse_Effect_Mechanism X2019_m_levofloxacin_1st:Impaired_renal_function_and_levofloxacin)
DataPropertyAssertion(OpenPVSignal:has_content X2019_m_levofloxacin_1st:Impaired_renal_function_and_levofloxacin "Although the product labels indicate that increasing age alone does not increase the risk of levofloxacin-related CNS adverse effects these are more likely to occur in the elderly as renal function diminishes with age, accelerated by some age-related clinical conditions. This decline may not always be detected if serum creatinine is low due to decreased muscle mass. Thus, accurate measurement of renal function and dose adjustment to avoid accumulation of levofloxacin is essential."^^xsd:string)

