# Individual: X2019_m_Methotrexate_Incorrect_drug_administration_rate2019_1st:introduction (introduction)

AnnotationAssertion(rdfs:label X2019_m_Methotrexate_Incorrect_drug_administration_rate2019_1st:introduction "introduction"^^xsd:string)
ClassAssertion(OpenPVSignal:Introduction X2019_m_Methotrexate_Incorrect_drug_administration_rate2019_1st:introduction)
DataPropertyAssertion(OpenPVSignal:has_content X2019_m_Methotrexate_Incorrect_drug_administration_rate2019_1st:introduction "Methotrexate is a folic acid antagonist used in the treatment of rheumatoid arthritis and severe psoriasis when the patient has been unresponsive to other, conventional therapies.1,2 It is also used to induce regression in neoplastic conditions such as acute leukaemia, non-Hodgkin's lymphoma, soft-tissue and osteogenic sarcomas, and solid tumours such as breast, lung, head and neck, bladder, cervix, ovaries, and testicles carcinoma . In the treatment of rheumatoid arthritis and psoriasis, methotrexate is given as a weekly dose . This dose can be divided into three doses to be taken within 24 hours, at 12-hour intervals (applicable for the tablet formulation). In cancer treatment, single doses of methotrexate are given on not more than five consecutive days, followed by a rest period of at least two weeks between treatments"^^xsd:string)

