# Individual: X2019_m_Esomeprazole_and_gynaecomastia_in_obese_adults_2nd_2019:esomeprazoleTriggeringGynaecomastia (esomeprazole triggering gynaecomastia)

AnnotationAssertion(rdfs:label X2019_m_Esomeprazole_and_gynaecomastia_in_obese_adults_2nd_2019:esomeprazoleTriggeringGynaecomastia "esomeprazole triggering gynaecomastia"^^xsd:string)
ClassAssertion(OpenPVSignal:Adverse_Effect_Mechanism X2019_m_Esomeprazole_and_gynaecomastia_in_obese_adults_2nd_2019:esomeprazoleTriggeringGynaecomastia)
ObjectPropertyAssertion(OpenPVSignal:refers_to_adverse_effect X2019_m_Esomeprazole_and_gynaecomastia_in_obese_adults_2nd_2019:esomeprazoleTriggeringGynaecomastia X2019_m_Esomeprazole_and_gynaecomastia_in_obese_adults_2nd_2019:Gynecomastia)
ObjectPropertyAssertion(mp:references X2019_m_Esomeprazole_and_gynaecomastia_in_obese_adults_2nd_2019:esomeprazoleTriggeringGynaecomastia X2019_m_Esomeprazole_and_gynaecomastia_in_obese_adults_2nd_2019:Ref.7)
ObjectPropertyAssertion(mp:references X2019_m_Esomeprazole_and_gynaecomastia_in_obese_adults_2nd_2019:esomeprazoleTriggeringGynaecomastia X2019_m_Esomeprazole_and_gynaecomastia_in_obese_adults_2nd_2019:Ref.8)
ObjectPropertyAssertion(mp:references X2019_m_Esomeprazole_and_gynaecomastia_in_obese_adults_2nd_2019:esomeprazoleTriggeringGynaecomastia X2019_m_Esomeprazole_and_gynaecomastia_in_obese_adults_2nd_2019:Ref.9)
DataPropertyAssertion(OpenPVSignal:has_content X2019_m_Esomeprazole_and_gynaecomastia_in_obese_adults_2nd_2019:esomeprazoleTriggeringGynaecomastia "Omeprazole and its S-enantiomer esomeprazole at high concentrations appear to inhibit cytochrome P450 (CYP) 3A4 – which strongly catalyses the oxidation of estradiol, its major catabolic pathway – giving rise to an increase in estradiol levels.7 Omeprazole is extensively metabolised by CYP2C19, for which >15 variant alleles associated with a decreased metabolism have been identified (the frequency of poor metabolisers among Europeans ranges from 1% to 6% 8,9) and it is possible that such patients, when treated for long periods with higher doses of omeprazole, would be at particular risk for the development of gynaecomastia.
Esomeprazole is known to cause gynaecomastia, as stated in the label. Their metabolic pathway appears to catalyse oxidation of estradiol, thereby increasing estradiol levels, and is strongly dose dependent. In this particular series, all six patients with gynaecomastia were obese, whereas the breast enlargement regressed upon removal of esomeprazole in the two mildly obese patients, but not in the remaining four very obese patients."^^xsd:string)

