# Individual: X2019_m_Esomeprazole_and_gynaecomastia_in_obese_adults_2nd_2019:infoForPatient3 (info for patient 3)

AnnotationAssertion(rdfs:label X2019_m_Esomeprazole_and_gynaecomastia_in_obese_adults_2nd_2019:infoForPatient3 "info for patient 3"^^xsd:string)
ClassAssertion(OpenPVSignal:Case_Report_Information X2019_m_Esomeprazole_and_gynaecomastia_in_obese_adults_2nd_2019:infoForPatient3)
DataPropertyAssertion(OpenPVSignal:has_content X2019_m_Esomeprazole_and_gynaecomastia_in_obese_adults_2nd_2019:infoForPatient3 "A 51-year old male, very obese (BMI=41.3), received esomeprazole for two years and lercanidipine for five years, as well as hydrochlorothiazide and tramadol for unspecified periods. He developed left breast enlargement after taking the drugs for several years. A mammogram showed an apparently normal well-developed breast, without adenopathy. The enlargement persisted despite dechallenge and rechallenge of esomeprazole and lercanidipine."^^xsd:string)

# Individual: X2019_m_Esomeprazole_and_gynaecomastia_in_obese_adults_2nd_2019:infoForPatient4 (info for patient 4)

AnnotationAssertion(rdfs:label X2019_m_Esomeprazole_and_gynaecomastia_in_obese_adults_2nd_2019:infoForPatient4 "info for patient 4"^^xsd:string)
ClassAssertion(OpenPVSignal:Case_Report_Information X2019_m_Esomeprazole_and_gynaecomastia_in_obese_adults_2nd_2019:infoForPatient4)
DataPropertyAssertion(OpenPVSignal:has_content X2019_m_Esomeprazole_and_gynaecomastia_in_obese_adults_2nd_2019:infoForPatient4 "A 61-year old slightly obese male patient (BMI=31.8), with non-Hodgkin B type lymphoma (stage 4) with multiple adenopathies and obstructive renal insufficiency (urethral infiltration), who had been a heavy smoker, was prescribed esomeprazole, amlodipine and diclofenac. He received esomeprazole 20 mg due to gastric pain and gastroesophageal reflux, and had the dose doubled to 40 mg after three days. Two days later, he developed pain and enlargement of both breasts. The gynaecomastia regressed within four weeks.
Hormone levels were not checked."^^xsd:string)

# Individual: X2019_m_Esomeprazole_and_gynaecomastia_in_obese_adults_2nd_2019:infoForPatient5 (info for patient 5)

AnnotationAssertion(rdfs:label X2019_m_Esomeprazole_and_gynaecomastia_in_obese_adults_2nd_2019:infoForPatient5 "info for patient 5"^^xsd:string)
ClassAssertion(OpenPVSignal:Case_Report_Information X2019_m_Esomeprazole_and_gynaecomastia_in_obese_adults_2nd_2019:infoForPatient5)
DataPropertyAssertion(OpenPVSignal:has_content X2019_m_Esomeprazole_and_gynaecomastia_in_obese_adults_2nd_2019:infoForPatient5 "A 60-year old male (BMI=30.4), with sarcoidosis and pyrosis, who had been taking ranitidine for over 7 1/2 years, switched to omeprazole (20 mg twice a day) for seven months and then esomeprazole (20 mg twice a day). He developed breast enlargement when on ranitidine, so one month later he began taking omeprazole and later switched to esomeprazole. Gynaecomastia persisted even after the switches."^^xsd:string)

# Individual: X2019_m_Esomeprazole_and_gynaecomastia_in_obese_adults_2nd_2019:infoForPatient6 (info for patient 6)

AnnotationAssertion(rdfs:label X2019_m_Esomeprazole_and_gynaecomastia_in_obese_adults_2nd_2019:infoForPatient6 "info for patient 6"^^xsd:string)
ClassAssertion(OpenPVSignal:Case_Report_Information X2019_m_Esomeprazole_and_gynaecomastia_in_obese_adults_2nd_2019:infoForPatient6)
DataPropertyAssertion(OpenPVSignal:has_content X2019_m_Esomeprazole_and_gynaecomastia_in_obese_adults_2nd_2019:infoForPatient6 "A 43-year old very obese male (BMI=39.0) received esomeprazole for five months for gastroesophageal reflux. Soon after, he reported decreased libido, partial erectile difficulty and breast enlargement. After discontinuation of the drug, he recovered erection and libido, but gynaecomastia persisted."^^xsd:string)

