DataPropertyAssertion(OpenPVSignal:has_content X2019_m_Esomeprazole_and_gynaecomastia_in_obese_adults_2nd_2019:ranitidineTriggeringGynaecomastia "Patient 5, with the lowest BMI (30.4), who had persistent enlarged breasts, had been taking
ranitidine for over 7 1/2 years. Ranitidine, like cimetidine, is a H2 histamine receptor blocker and one of the drug classes that has been implicated with gynaecomastia, with relative risk >7 for treated patients, and strongly dose-dependent.5"^^xsd:string)

