# Individual: X2019_m_Phenprocoumon_Accidental_overdose_1st_2019:Mechanism_of_phenprocoumon (Mechanism of phenprocomoun)

AnnotationAssertion(rdfs:label X2019_m_Phenprocoumon_Accidental_overdose_1st_2019:Mechanism_of_phenprocoumon "Mechanism of phenprocomoun"^^xsd:string)
ClassAssertion(OpenPVSignal:Mechanism X2019_m_Phenprocoumon_Accidental_overdose_1st_2019:Mechanism_of_phenprocoumon)
ObjectPropertyAssertion(mp:references X2019_m_Phenprocoumon_Accidental_overdose_1st_2019:Mechanism_of_phenprocoumon X2019_m_Phenprocoumon_Accidental_overdose_1st_2019:Ref.1)
DataPropertyAssertion(OpenPVSignal:has_content X2019_m_Phenprocoumon_Accidental_overdose_1st_2019:Mechanism_of_phenprocoumon "Phenprocoumon is a long-acting vitamin K antagonist approved to treat and prevent thromboembolic disease. The oral anticoagulant is also indicated in patients diagnosed with atrial fibrillation for the prevention of ischemic stroke. Phenprocoumon and any other drugs in the anti coagulant family act by preventing further extension of a formed clot thus preventing secondary thromboembolic consequences which may lead to serious, sometimes fatal outcomes.1"^^xsd:string)

