AnnotationAssertion(rdfs:label X2019_m_Phenprocoumon_Accidental_overdose_1st_2019:conclusion "conclusion"^^xsd:string)
ClassAssertion(OpenPVSignal:Conclusion X2019_m_Phenprocoumon_Accidental_overdose_1st_2019:conclusion)
DataPropertyAssertion(OpenPVSignal:has_content X2019_m_Phenprocoumon_Accidental_overdose_1st_2019:conclusion "Anticoagulated patients are a vulnerable group requiring coagulation monitoring by health-care professionals to achieve the optimal pharmacological effect without causing bleeding. The population treated is generally elderly and takes these drugs in combination with other medication, thus increasing the risk of confusion and medication error. Switching products at the pharmacy level requires adequate information and reassurance that the patient has fully understood the dosing and monitoring instructions essential to prevent harm, including life-threatening events"^^xsd:string)

# Individual: X2019_m_Phenprocoumon_Accidental_overdose_1st_2019:introduction (introduction)

AnnotationAssertion(rdfs:label X2019_m_Phenprocoumon_Accidental_overdose_1st_2019:introduction "introduction"^^xsd:string)
ClassAssertion(OpenPVSignal:Introduction X2019_m_Phenprocoumon_Accidental_overdose_1st_2019:introduction)
ObjectPropertyAssertion(mp:references X2019_m_Phenprocoumon_Accidental_overdose_1st_2019:introduction X2019_m_Phenprocoumon_Accidental_overdose_1st_2019:Ref.1)
DataPropertyAssertion(OpenPVSignal:has_content X2019_m_Phenprocoumon_Accidental_overdose_1st_2019:introduction "Phenprocoumon is a long-acting vitamin K antagonist approved to treat and prevent thromboembolic disease. The oral anticoagulant is also indicated in patients diagnosed with atrial fibrillation for the prevention of ischemic stroke. Phenprocoumon and any other drugs in the anti- coagulant family act by preventing further extension of a formed clot thus preventing secondary thromboembolic consequences which may lead to serious, sometimes fatal outcomes.1"^^xsd:string)

