# Individual: X2019_m_Gi_pain_2019_4rth:Clinical_bioavailability_study (Clinical bioavailability study)

AnnotationAssertion(rdfs:label X2019_m_Gi_pain_2019_4rth:Clinical_bioavailability_study "Clinical bioavailability study"^^xsd:string)
ClassAssertion(obo:OAE_0001197 X2019_m_Gi_pain_2019_4rth:Clinical_bioavailability_study)
ClassAssertion(OpenPVSignal:Clinical_trial_information X2019_m_Gi_pain_2019_4rth:Clinical_bioavailability_study)
ObjectPropertyAssertion(OpenPVSignal:refers_to_adverse_effect X2019_m_Gi_pain_2019_4rth:Clinical_bioavailability_study X2019_m_Gi_pain_2019_4rth:gastrointestinal_adverse_event)
ObjectPropertyAssertion(OpenPVSignal:refers_to_drug X2019_m_Gi_pain_2019_4rth:Clinical_bioavailability_study X2019_m_Gi_pain_2019_4rth:guaifenesin)
ObjectPropertyAssertion(OpenPVSignal:refers_to_drug X2019_m_Gi_pain_2019_4rth:Clinical_bioavailability_study X2019_m_Gi_pain_2019_4rth:paracetamol)
ObjectPropertyAssertion(OpenPVSignal:refers_to_drug X2019_m_Gi_pain_2019_4rth:Clinical_bioavailability_study X2019_m_Gi_pain_2019_4rth:phenylephrine)
DataPropertyAssertion(OpenPVSignal:has_content X2019_m_Gi_pain_2019_4rth:Clinical_bioavailability_study "In a study investigating the bioavailability of a new oral syrup product containing guaifenesin, paracetamol, and phenylephrine, 45 patients were enrolled. Two patients reported GI adverse events (nothing more was specified) following the use of the test product consisting of the new oral syrup, and four patients reported GI adverse events following the use of the reference product consisting of an established oral liquid containing the same combination of substances. The authors considered the reported GI adverse events in this study as related to the liquid formulation, without any further discussion.10 In the VigiBase case series, the drug formulations used by the patients were liquid, tablet, capsule, and powder for oral solution, but patients in this case series still experienced sudden, severe abdominal pain in temporal association with these products."^^xsd:string)

# Individual: X2019_m_Gi_pain_2019_4rth:Conclusion_content (Conclusion content)

AnnotationAssertion(rdfs:label X2019_m_Gi_pain_2019_4rth:Conclusion_content "Conclusion content"^^xsd:string)
ClassAssertion(OpenPVSignal:Conclusion X2019_m_Gi_pain_2019_4rth:Conclusion_content)
DataPropertyAssertion(OpenPVSignal:has_content X2019_m_Gi_pain_2019_4rth:Conclusion_content "The VigiBase reports revealed a pattern where patients described severe upper abdominal pain following the intake of combination products containing guaifenesin, paracetamol, and phenylephrine, many times with a sudden onset and recovery after stopping the drug. The PILs for these products describe abdominal/stomach discomfort or stomach aches/upsets, however in some PILs, the only GI-related adverse reactions listed are nausea and vomiting. Patients might not recognise the descriptions in the PILs as a reflection of their severe experiences of abdominal pain, so consideration should be made to better describe abdominal pains in the information to patients."^^xsd:string)

# Individual: X2019_m_Gi_pain_2019_4rth:Connection_of_guaifenesin_with_GI_adverse_effects (Connection of guaifenesin with GI adverse effects)

AnnotationAssertion(rdfs:label X2019_m_Gi_pain_2019_4rth:Connection_of_guaifenesin_with_GI_adverse_effects "Connection of guaifenesin with GI adverse effects"^^xsd:string)
