ObjectPropertyAssertion(mp:references X2019_m_Methylphenidate_2019_4rth:Dyskinesia_pathology X2019_m_Methylphenidate_2019_4rth:Ref.5)
ObjectPropertyAssertion(mp:references X2019_m_Methylphenidate_2019_4rth:Dyskinesia_pathology X2019_m_Methylphenidate_2019_4rth:Ref.6)
DataPropertyAssertion(OpenPVSignal:has_content X2019_m_Methylphenidate_2019_4rth:Dyskinesia_pathology "Dyskinesia, on the other hand is characterized by abnormal, involuntary, repetitive and persistent movements affecting the mouth and face, extremities and the trunk.6 Tardive dyskinesia can develop after treatment with dopamine receptor-blocking agents, usually one month after starting treatment.5 Symptoms are not painful but can still be debilitating."^^xsd:string)

