# Individual: X2019_m_Methylphenidate_2019_4rth:Proposed_mechanism_of_dystonic_reaction (Proposed mechanism of dystonic reaction)

AnnotationAssertion(rdfs:label X2019_m_Methylphenidate_2019_4rth:Proposed_mechanism_of_dystonic_reaction "Proposed mechanism of dystonic reaction"^^xsd:string)
ClassAssertion(OpenPVSignal:Adverse_Effect_Mechanism X2019_m_Methylphenidate_2019_4rth:Proposed_mechanism_of_dystonic_reaction)
ObjectPropertyAssertion(OpenPVSignal:refers_to_adverse_effect X2019_m_Methylphenidate_2019_4rth:Proposed_mechanism_of_dystonic_reaction X2019_m_Methylphenidate_2019_4rth:dystonia)
ObjectPropertyAssertion(mp:references X2019_m_Methylphenidate_2019_4rth:Proposed_mechanism_of_dystonic_reaction X2019_m_Methylphenidate_2019_4rth:Ref.12)
ObjectPropertyAssertion(mp:references X2019_m_Methylphenidate_2019_4rth:Proposed_mechanism_of_dystonic_reaction X2019_m_Methylphenidate_2019_4rth:Ref.13)
ObjectPropertyAssertion(mp:references X2019_m_Methylphenidate_2019_4rth:Proposed_mechanism_of_dystonic_reaction X2019_m_Methylphenidate_2019_4rth:Ref.14)
ObjectPropertyAssertion(mp:references X2019_m_Methylphenidate_2019_4rth:Proposed_mechanism_of_dystonic_reaction X2019_m_Methylphenidate_2019_4rth:Ref.15)
DataPropertyAssertion(OpenPVSignal:has_content X2019_m_Methylphenidate_2019_4rth:Proposed_mechanism_of_dystonic_reaction "However, the literature reports of dystonia associated with methylphenidate withdrawal12-15 suggest that methylphenidate could cause dystonic reactions by disrupting the dopamine balance. In these cases, the patients were treated with both methylphenidate which stimulates dopamine action, and with antipsychotics which block dopamine action and seemed to have reached a balance in dopamine levels. They only experienced dystonic reactions when methylphenidate was withdrawn, that is when the dopamine balance was disrupted."^^xsd:string)

