TTO reported in 22 cases. TTO was within one day in ten of these cases. 
In four cases trismus occurred after abrupt withdrawal (3) or dose reduction (1) of methylphenidate"^^xsd:string)

# Individual: X2019_m_Methylphenidate_2019_4rth:UK_PIL (UK PIL)

AnnotationAssertion(rdfs:label X2019_m_Methylphenidate_2019_4rth:UK_PIL "UK PIL"^^xsd:string)
ClassAssertion(OpenPVSignal:Structured_Product_Labels_information X2019_m_Methylphenidate_2019_4rth:UK_PIL)
ObjectPropertyAssertion(OpenPVSignal:refers_to_adverse_effect X2019_m_Methylphenidate_2019_4rth:UK_PIL X2019_m_Methylphenidate_2019_4rth:muscleSpasms)
ObjectPropertyAssertion(OpenPVSignal:refers_to_adverse_effect X2019_m_Methylphenidate_2019_4rth:UK_PIL X2019_m_Methylphenidate_2019_4rth:muscleTwitching)
ObjectPropertyAssertion(OpenPVSignal:refers_to_adverse_effect X2019_m_Methylphenidate_2019_4rth:UK_PIL X2019_m_Methylphenidate_2019_4rth:muscle_cramps)
ObjectPropertyAssertion(OpenPVSignal:refers_to_adverse_effect X2019_m_Methylphenidate_2019_4rth:UK_PIL X2019_m_Methylphenidate_2019_4rth:muscle_pain)
ObjectPropertyAssertion(OpenPVSignal:refers_to_adverse_effect X2019_m_Methylphenidate_2019_4rth:UK_PIL X2019_m_Methylphenidate_2019_4rth:muscle_tightness)
ObjectPropertyAssertion(OpenPVSignal:refers_to_adverse_effect X2019_m_Methylphenidate_2019_4rth:UK_PIL X2019_m_Methylphenidate_2019_4rth:teeth_clenching)
ObjectPropertyAssertion(OpenPVSignal:refers_to_adverse_effect X2019_m_Methylphenidate_2019_4rth:UK_PIL X2019_m_Methylphenidate_2019_4rth:teeth_grinding)
ObjectPropertyAssertion(OpenPVSignal:refers_to_drug X2019_m_Methylphenidate_2019_4rth:UK_PIL X2019_m_Methylphenidate_2019_4rth:methylphenidate)
ObjectPropertyAssertion(mp:references X2019_m_Methylphenidate_2019_4rth:UK_PIL X2019_m_Methylphenidate_2019_4rth:Ref.10)
DataPropertyAssertion(OpenPVSignal:has_content X2019_m_Methylphenidate_2019_4rth:UK_PIL "In the UK Patient Information Leaflet (PIL), the following adverse reactions are described: “muscle spasms which you cannot control affecting your eyes, head, neck, body and nervous system”, “muscle tightness, muscle cramps”, “muscle pain, muscle twitching”.10 Jaw-specific reactions are not covered in the leaflet, although “uncontrolled speech and body movements” and “clenching or grinding your teeth” are."^^xsd:string)

