# Individual: X2019_m_Methylphenidate_2019_4rth:case_15_info (case 15 info)

AnnotationAssertion(rdfs:label X2019_m_Methylphenidate_2019_4rth:case_15_info "case 15 info"^^xsd:string)
ClassAssertion(OpenPVSignal:Case_Report_Information X2019_m_Methylphenidate_2019_4rth:case_15_info)
DataPropertyAssertion(OpenPVSignal:has_content X2019_m_Methylphenidate_2019_4rth:case_15_info "Dose not changed/Reaction abated Comment: the report narrative states that the methylphenidate dose was reduced from 108 to 90 mg after one year of treatment and withdrawn completely after four years. reports. However, it is unclear whether the patient recovered from jaw cramps before or after the dose reduction/withdrawal."^^xsd:string)

# Individual: X2019_m_Methylphenidate_2019_4rth:case_1_info (case 1 info)

AnnotationAssertion(rdfs:label X2019_m_Methylphenidate_2019_4rth:case_1_info "case 1 info"^^xsd:string)
ClassAssertion(OpenPVSignal:Case_Report_Information X2019_m_Methylphenidate_2019_4rth:case_1_info)
DataPropertyAssertion(OpenPVSignal:has_content X2019_m_Methylphenidate_2019_4rth:case_1_info "Dose increased/No effect observed It is unclear if the dose increase refers to the increase from 18 to 27 mg which occurred before reaction onset."^^xsd:string)

# Individual: X2019_m_Methylphenidate_2019_4rth:case_20_info (case 20 info)

AnnotationAssertion(rdfs:label X2019_m_Methylphenidate_2019_4rth:case_20_info "case 20 info"^^xsd:string)
ClassAssertion(OpenPVSignal:Case_Report_Information X2019_m_Methylphenidate_2019_4rth:case_20_info)
ObjectPropertyAssertion(mp:references X2019_m_Methylphenidate_2019_4rth:case_20_info X2019_m_Methylphenidate_2019_4rth:Ref.8)
DataPropertyAssertion(OpenPVSignal:has_content X2019_m_Methylphenidate_2019_4rth:case_20_info "In one case (20), a positive rechallenge was reported. The case describes a 40-year-old female who experienced extrapyramidal symptoms consisting of involuntary movement of the tongue and trismus 30 minutes after methylphenidate administration. The drug was withdrawn, and the patient recovered. The patient was then treated with methylphenidate slow-release and the symptoms were reported to be less severe. The case was first described in a signal published by the Netherlands Pharmacovigilance Centre Lareb.8"^^xsd:string)

# Individual: X2019_m_Methylphenidate_2019_4rth:case_22_info (case 22 info)

AnnotationAssertion(rdfs:label X2019_m_Methylphenidate_2019_4rth:case_22_info "case 22 info"^^xsd:string)
ClassAssertion(OpenPVSignal:Case_Report_Information X2019_m_Methylphenidate_2019_4rth:case_22_info)
DataPropertyAssertion(OpenPVSignal:has_content X2019_m_Methylphenidate_2019_4rth:case_22_info "In another case (22), a 21-year-old female experienced trismus two days after administration of methylphenidate. The patient was reported to be recovering without changing the drug treatment. She also used oestrogen with levonorgestrel (treatment with propranolol was also reported which started after trismus occurred)."^^xsd:string)

# Individual: X2019_m_Methylphenidate_2019_4rth:case_23_info (case 23 info)

AnnotationAssertion(rdfs:label X2019_m_Methylphenidate_2019_4rth:case_23_info "case 23 info"^^xsd:string)
ClassAssertion(OpenPVSignal:Case_Report_Information X2019_m_Methylphenidate_2019_4rth:case_23_info)
DataPropertyAssertion(OpenPVSignal:has_content X2019_m_Methylphenidate_2019_4rth:case_23_info "Comment: reaction occurred upon abrupt withdrawal of methylphenidate while still on concomitant treatment with antipsychotics. Patient had used the drug for four years but the reaction occurred 33 hours after the last dose."^^xsd:string)

# Individual: X2019_m_Methylphenidate_2019_4rth:case_24_info (case 24 info)

AnnotationAssertion(rdfs:label X2019_m_Methylphenidate_2019_4rth:case_24_info "case 24 info"^^xsd:string)
ClassAssertion(OpenPVSignal:Case_Report_Information X2019_m_Methylphenidate_2019_4rth:case_24_info)
DataPropertyAssertion(OpenPVSignal:has_content X2019_m_Methylphenidate_2019_4rth:case_24_info "Comment: reaction occurred upon abrupt reduction of methylphenidate dose (from 80-120 mg to 20 mg). Patient had used the drug for one year and the reaction occurred on the same day as dose was reduced."^^xsd:string)
DataPropertyAssertion(OpenPVSignal:has_content X2019_m_Methylphenidate_2019_4rth:case_24_info "In another case (24) the patient was not treated with antipsychotics but still experienced trismus after a rapid decrease in the methylphenidate dose. The patient had used methylphenidate for one year and was normally treated with 80-120 mg/day. On the same day as she took only 20 mg, she developed trismus and jaw pain. The patient was also taking metoprolol and sumatriptan for migraine, both reported as suspected."^^xsd:string)

# Individual: X2019_m_Methylphenidate_2019_4rth:case_2_info (case 2 info)

AnnotationAssertion(rdfs:label X2019_m_Methylphenidate_2019_4rth:case_2_info "case 2 info"^^xsd:string)
ClassAssertion(OpenPVSignal:Case_Report_Information X2019_m_Methylphenidate_2019_4rth:case_2_info)
DataPropertyAssertion(OpenPVSignal:has_content X2019_m_Methylphenidate_2019_4rth:case_2_info "Comment: reaction occurred upon abrupt withdrawal of methylphenidate while still on concomitant treatment with antipsychotics The authors of this literature report suspect chronic aripiprazole and methylphenidate usage combined with propofol administration in he short-term absence of methylphenidate made this patient susceptible to dystonic reactions."^^xsd:string)

# Individual: X2019_m_Methylphenidate_2019_4rth:case_38_info (case 38 info)

AnnotationAssertion(rdfs:label X2019_m_Methylphenidate_2019_4rth:case_38_info "case 38 info"^^xsd:string)
ClassAssertion(OpenPVSignal:Case_Report_Information X2019_m_Methylphenidate_2019_4rth:case_38_info)
DataPropertyAssertion(OpenPVSignal:has_content X2019_m_Methylphenidate_2019_4rth:case_38_info "The third case (38) describes a 35-year-old female experiencing tightness of jaw muscles within a month after starting methylphenidate treatment which she recovered from without changing the administration of methylphenidate."^^xsd:string)

# Individual: X2019_m_Methylphenidate_2019_4rth:case_3_info (case 3 info)

AnnotationAssertion(rdfs:label X2019_m_Methylphenidate_2019_4rth:case_3_info "case 3 info"^^xsd:string)
ClassAssertion(OpenPVSignal:Case_Report_Information X2019_m_Methylphenidate_2019_4rth:case_3_info)
DataPropertyAssertion(OpenPVSignal:has_content X2019_m_Methylphenidate_2019_4rth:case_3_info "Dose not changed/Reaction abated Comment: trismus occurred after methylphenidate dose was increased from 30 to 40 mg. The event then resolved spontaneously without changing the dose."^^xsd:string)
DataPropertyAssertion(OpenPVSignal:has_content X2019_m_Methylphenidate_2019_4rth:case_3_info "One case (3) concerned a 29-year-old female who experienced one episode of trismus after increasing the methylphenidate dose from 30 to 40 mg. The adverse event resolved spontaneously, and the patient did not experience similar events later. No other concomitant drugs were reported."^^xsd:string)

# Individual: X2019_m_Methylphenidate_2019_4rth:case_info_12 (case 12 info)

AnnotationAssertion(rdfs:label X2019_m_Methylphenidate_2019_4rth:case_info_12 "case 12 info"^^xsd:string)
ClassAssertion(OpenPVSignal:Case_Report_Information X2019_m_Methylphenidate_2019_4rth:case_info_12)
DataPropertyAssertion(OpenPVSignal:has_content X2019_m_Methylphenidate_2019_4rth:case_info_12 "Comment: patient experienced the adverse reactions after withdrawal of both methylphenidate and diphenhydramine. Patient was treated with methylphenidate for 1.5 years before the withdrawal."^^xsd:string)

