AnnotationAssertion(rdfs:label X2019_m_IUS_and_supressed_lactation_2019_5th:Alima_Tapsoba "Alima Tapsoba"^^xsd:string)
ClassAssertion(OpenPVSignal:Author X2019_m_IUS_and_supressed_lactation_2019_5th:Alima_Tapsoba)
DataPropertyAssertion(OpenPVSignal:has_affiliation X2019_m_IUS_and_supressed_lactation_2019_5th:Alima_Tapsoba "Health Canada"^^xsd:string)
DataPropertyAssertion(OpenPVSignal:has_first_name X2019_m_IUS_and_supressed_lactation_2019_5th:Alima_Tapsoba "Alima"^^xsd:string)
DataPropertyAssertion(OpenPVSignal:has_last_name X2019_m_IUS_and_supressed_lactation_2019_5th:Alima_Tapsoba "Tapsoba"^^xsd:string)

# Individual: X2019_m_IUS_and_supressed_lactation_2019_5th:Case_1 (Case 1)

AnnotationAssertion(rdfs:label X2019_m_IUS_and_supressed_lactation_2019_5th:Case_1 "Case 1"^^xsd:string)
ClassAssertion(OpenPVSignal:Case_Report_Information X2019_m_IUS_and_supressed_lactation_2019_5th:Case_1)
DataPropertyAssertion(OpenPVSignal:has_content X2019_m_IUS_and_supressed_lactation_2019_5th:Case_1 "A physician described the patient experience with LNG-releasing intrauterine device (IUD) as “Mother has Mirena IUD inserted. Baby did not gain weight. The change from a baby who was previously gaining weight very well was chronologically related to the IUD. Removal of IUD”"^^xsd:string)

# Individual: X2019_m_IUS_and_supressed_lactation_2019_5th:Case_2 (Case 2)

AnnotationAssertion(rdfs:label X2019_m_IUS_and_supressed_lactation_2019_5th:Case_2 "Case 2"^^xsd:string)
ClassAssertion(OpenPVSignal:Case_Report_Information X2019_m_IUS_and_supressed_lactation_2019_5th:Case_2)
DataPropertyAssertion(OpenPVSignal:has_content X2019_m_IUS_and_supressed_lactation_2019_5th:Case_2 "Case 2: Similarly, another Lactation doctor reported the following regarding the patient “Patient had Mirena inserted about 6 months postpartum and was pumping her breast. At the time of insertion she was pumping 4-5xday and
 getting 60-80 ml per breast. Her supply gradually decreased to 20-30 per breast and the letdown would take 8-10 minutes. IUD removed and supply was back within 1 week, Also the letdown now very fast”."^^xsd:string)

# Individual: X2019_m_IUS_and_supressed_lactation_2019_5th:Case_3 (Case 3)

AnnotationAssertion(rdfs:label X2019_m_IUS_and_supressed_lactation_2019_5th:Case_3 "Case 3"^^xsd:string)
ClassAssertion(OpenPVSignal:Case_Report_Information X2019_m_IUS_and_supressed_lactation_2019_5th:Case_3)
DataPropertyAssertion(OpenPVSignal:has_content X2019_m_IUS_and_supressed_lactation_2019_5th:Case_3 "Case 3: A family physician detailed patient experiences while on LNG as follows “Patient had Mirena IUD for contraception at the time of breast feeding. Milk supply dropped within 7-10 days.
IUD was removed and ten days after removed, her milk supply returned back to normal.”"^^xsd:string)

# Individual: X2019_m_IUS_and_supressed_lactation_2019_5th:Conclusion_content (Conclusion content)

AnnotationAssertion(rdfs:label X2019_m_IUS_and_supressed_lactation_2019_5th:Conclusion_content "Conclusion content"^^xsd:string)
ClassAssertion(OpenPVSignal:Conclusion X2019_m_IUS_and_supressed_lactation_2019_5th:Conclusion_content)
DataPropertyAssertion(OpenPVSignal:has_content X2019_m_IUS_and_supressed_lactation_2019_5th:Conclusion_content "There are currently no literature references suggesting that LNG-IUS products decrease breast milk production in breastfeeding mothers and the biological plausibility of suppressed lactation remains unclear. However, there are post-market reports of suppressed lactation in breastfeeding women using LNG-IUS with a probable/ possible causality. Isolated cases of suppressed lactation with the use of LNG-IUS is labelled in the USA and Canada based on post-marketing experience. This risk should be labelled consistently for all LNG-IUS products worldwide so that health care professionals and patients may benefit from increased awareness of the occurrence of isolated post-marketing reports of decreased milk production among women using LNG-IUS products."^^xsd:string)

# Individual: X2019_m_IUS_and_supressed_lactation_2019_5th:Dosage_of_LNG-IUS (Dosage of LNG-IUS)

AnnotationAssertion(rdfs:label X2019_m_IUS_and_supressed_lactation_2019_5th:Dosage_of_LNG-IUS "Dosage of LNG-IUS"^^xsd:string)
ClassAssertion(OpenPVSignal:Dosage X2019_m_IUS_and_supressed_lactation_2019_5th:Dosage_of_LNG-IUS)
DataPropertyAssertion(OpenPVSignal:has_content X2019_m_IUS_and_supressed_lactation_2019_5th:Dosage_of_LNG-IUS "52 mg, 19.5 mg and 13.5 mg LNG"^^xsd:string)

