# Individual: X2019_m_IUS_and_supressed_lactation_2019_5th:Limitations_of_current_analysis (Limitations of current analysis)

AnnotationAssertion(rdfs:label X2019_m_IUS_and_supressed_lactation_2019_5th:Limitations_of_current_analysis "Limitations of current analysis"^^xsd:string)
ClassAssertion(obo:OAE_0001182 X2019_m_IUS_and_supressed_lactation_2019_5th:Limitations_of_current_analysis)
DataPropertyAssertion(OpenPVSignal:has_content X2019_m_IUS_and_supressed_lactation_2019_5th:Limitations_of_current_analysis "Several physiological factors can cause decreased/suppressed lactation (stress, infrequent breastfeeding, introduction of formula, etc.).
Information regarding possible maternal or neonatal factors is not available in the reports. Information on objective evidence suggesting decreased lactation (such as infant weight, stool/urine outputs, amount of breast milk expressed before and after insertion of the IUS etc.) is missing in most of these reports."^^xsd:string)

