# Individual: X2019_m_levonergestrel_6th_2019:case (Case 2 Information)

AnnotationAssertion(rdfs:label X2019_m_levonergestrel_6th_2019:case "Case 2 Information"^^xsd:string)
ClassAssertion(OpenPVSignal:Case_Report_Information X2019_m_levonergestrel_6th_2019:case)
DataPropertyAssertion(OpenPVSignal:has_content X2019_m_levonergestrel_6th_2019:case "In one case the reporter herself describes that she experienced a panic attack seven years prior when using an oral contraceptive, Cerazette (desogestrel). Twelve days after the insertion of the LNG-IUD she experienced severe panic attacks, along with difficulty breathing. The symptoms ended after discontinuation of the treatment. She had told her gynaecologist about the side effects. He was surprised and said that the patient was the first in 20 years to have these side effects. The device was removed at the patient’s request and she has been feeling better since."^^xsd:string)

