# Individual: X2019_m_Nintedanib_and_ischaemic_colitis_6th_2019:Case_Info_6 (Case Info 6)

AnnotationAssertion(rdfs:label X2019_m_Nintedanib_and_ischaemic_colitis_6th_2019:Case_Info_6 "Case Info 6"^^xsd:string)
ClassAssertion(OpenPVSignal:Case_Report_Information X2019_m_Nintedanib_and_ischaemic_colitis_6th_2019:Case_Info_6)
ObjectPropertyAssertion(OpenPVSignal:refers_to_patient X2019_m_Nintedanib_and_ischaemic_colitis_6th_2019:Case_Info_6 X2019_m_Nintedanib_and_ischaemic_colitis_6th_2019:Patient6)
DataPropertyAssertion(OpenPVSignal:has_content X2019_m_Nintedanib_and_ischaemic_colitis_6th_2019:Case_Info_6 "185 cm"^^xsd:string)
DataPropertyAssertion(OpenPVSignal:has_content X2019_m_Nintedanib_and_ischaemic_colitis_6th_2019:Case_Info_6 "Patient presented with abdominal pain 27 days after initiation on nintedanib. Admitted to hospital, diagnosed with ischaemic colitis (grade 2), and treated with mesalazin. Five days later, the patient experienced obstipation. Ten days later, the patient had stomach pain (grade 3), acute mesenteric ischemia (grade 4), 
thromboembolic event (grade 4), and peripheral ischemia (grade 3). Had thromobectomy of arteria mesenterica superior, explorative laparotomy and small intestinal segment resection. Hospitalisation complicated by wound healing disorder which led to cardiovascular failure, sepsis and death."^^xsd:string)

# Individual: X2019_m_Nintedanib_and_ischaemic_colitis_6th_2019:Case_Info_8 (Case Info 8)

AnnotationAssertion(rdfs:label X2019_m_Nintedanib_and_ischaemic_colitis_6th_2019:Case_Info_8 "Case Info 8"^^xsd:string)
ClassAssertion(OpenPVSignal:Case_Report_Information X2019_m_Nintedanib_and_ischaemic_colitis_6th_2019:Case_Info_8)
ObjectPropertyAssertion(OpenPVSignal:refers_to_patient X2019_m_Nintedanib_and_ischaemic_colitis_6th_2019:Case_Info_8 X2019_m_Nintedanib_and_ischaemic_colitis_6th_2019:Patient8)
DataPropertyAssertion(OpenPVSignal:has_content X2019_m_Nintedanib_and_ischaemic_colitis_6th_2019:Case_Info_8 "Surgery preparation of colon descendens, sigmoideum and upper rectum with intense and distinct ischemic necrosis of gut wall, inclusion of max. 2.3 cm polyp, without evidence of vital mucosa. Beside a 0.9 cm in sano resected tubular adenoma with slight intraepithelial neoplasia (low-grade adenoma following WHO-classification). Transmural hemorraghic necrosis (reaching out up to the resection area) of gut wall without inflammation, as appropriate for ischemia."^^xsd:string)

