# Individual: X2019_m_Nintedanib_and_ischaemic_colitis_6th_2019:Labelling_and_literature (Labelling and literature)

AnnotationAssertion(rdfs:label X2019_m_Nintedanib_and_ischaemic_colitis_6th_2019:Labelling_and_literature "Labelling and literature"^^xsd:string)
ClassAssertion(OpenPVSignal:Literature_information X2019_m_Nintedanib_and_ischaemic_colitis_6th_2019:Labelling_and_literature)
ObjectPropertyAssertion(mp:references X2019_m_Nintedanib_and_ischaemic_colitis_6th_2019:Labelling_and_literature X2019_m_Nintedanib_and_ischaemic_colitis_6th_2019:Ref.3)
ObjectPropertyAssertion(mp:references X2019_m_Nintedanib_and_ischaemic_colitis_6th_2019:Labelling_and_literature X2019_m_Nintedanib_and_ischaemic_colitis_6th_2019:Ref.4)
DataPropertyAssertion(OpenPVSignal:has_content X2019_m_Nintedanib_and_ischaemic_colitis_6th_2019:Labelling_and_literature "Product labelling for nintedanib includes warnings for diarrhoea and gastrointestinal perforation in section 4.4 of the Summary of Product Characteristics. There is also information regarding management options for serious cases of diarrhoea including hydration, anti-diarrhoeal products, and dose reduction and information regarding potential risk factors for gastrointestinal perforation, such as previous abdominal surgery or peptic ulceration, and diverticular disease and concomitant use of corticosteroids or NSAIDs. Included in the list of ADRs in section 4.8 are nausea, vomiting, diarrhoea, abdominal pain and pancreatitis.3
Within the risk management plan were the identified risks of diarrhoea and liver function abnormalities as important identified risks and “perforation” as an important potential risk; there were no planned post-authorisation safety studies to further characterise any risks for the gastrointestinal system.4"^^xsd:string)

